g a repair, delta for the compounding growth of the", "tokens": [50640, 350, 25637, 497, 337, 264, 5588, 19922, 295, 6265, 990, 257, 10535, 11, 8289, 337, 264, 14154, 278, 4599, 295, 264, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05602706133664309, "compression_ratio": 1.6302521008403361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169073458610628e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 58000, "start": 591.36, "end": 598.14, "text": " problem, and P for the exponential cost of the eventual fix. You got it. So how do these variables", "tokens": [50933, 1154, 11, 293, 430, 337, 264, 21510, 2063, 295, 264, 33160, 3191, 13, 509, 658, 309, 13, 407, 577, 360, 613, 9102, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05602706133664309, "compression_ratio": 1.6302521008403361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169073458610628e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 58000, "start": 598.14, "end": 604.62, "text": " actually interact? Because this leads us to the core of the essay, the central mathematical proof.", "tokens": [51272, 767, 4648, 30, 1436, 341, 6689, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 295, 264, 16238, 11, 264, 5777, 18894, 8177, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05602706133664309, "compression_ratio": 1.6302521008403361, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169073458610628e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 60462, "start": 604.62, "end": 609.54, "text": " And I have to admit, when I was reading this section, it just forced me to completely rethink", "tokens": [50365, 400, 286, 362, 281, 9796, 11, 562, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 3541, 11, 309, 445, 7579, 385, 281, 2584, 34595, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 60462, "start": 609.54, "end": 612.92, "text": " how decisions are made. It's the central breakthrough of the paper, without a doubt.", "tokens": [50611, 577, 5327, 366, 1027, 13, 467, 311, 264, 5777, 22397, 295, 264, 3035, 11, 1553, 257, 6385, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 60462, "start": 613.24, "end": 616.96, "text": " The author proves that when you sit there and ask, when should I defer fixing this,", "tokens": [50796, 440, 3793, 25019, 300, 562, 291, 1394, 456, 293, 1029, 11, 562, 820, 286, 25704, 19442, 341, 11, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 60462, "start": 617.28, "end": 620.4, "text": " you are not actually asking one complicated question. Wait, really?", "tokens": [50998, 291, 366, 406, 767, 3365, 472, 6179, 1168, 13, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 60462, "start": 620.62, "end": 625.7, "text": " No, you're asking two entirely separate mathematical questions that are governed by completely disjoint", "tokens": [51165, 883, 11, 291, 434, 3365, 732, 7696, 4994, 18894, 1651, 300, 366, 35529, 538, 2584, 717, 48613, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 60462, "start": 625.7, "end": 630.1800000000001, "text": " mechanisms. And that is the part that is so counterintuitive to me. Yeah.", "tokens": [51419, 15902, 13, 400, 300, 307, 264, 644, 300, 307, 370, 5682, 686, 48314, 281, 385, 13, 865, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06652708376868297, "compression_ratio": 1.6765676567656767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743026035419436e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 63018, "start": 630.18, "end": 635.38, "text": " Because I always thought of when to fix as a single sliding scale. Yeah. But the text says,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 286, 1009, 1194, 295, 562, 281, 3191, 382, 257, 2167, 21169, 4373, 13, 865, 13, 583, 264, 