": 659.5, "end": 664.82, "text": " It proves that this immediate threshold is governed entirely by the ratio of the fixed", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 300, 341, 11629, 14678, 307, 35529, 7696, 538, 264, 8509, 295, 264, 6806, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 65950, "start": 664.82, "end": 670.48, "text": " overheads. It ignores the compounding delta and the convexity P completely. Yes. The actual", "tokens": [50631, 19922, 82, 13, 467, 5335, 2706, 264, 14154, 278, 8289, 293, 264, 42432, 507, 430, 2584, 13, 1079, 13, 440, 3539, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 65950, "start": 670.48, "end": 674.86, "text": " physical nature of the problem doesn't even enter the equation yet. And this is just a brilliant", "tokens": [50914, 4001, 3687, 295, 264, 1154, 1177, 380, 754, 3242, 264, 5367, 1939, 13, 400, 341, 307, 445, 257, 10248, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 65950, "start": 674.86, "end": 680.66, "text": " structural insight by Fliction. The math dictates that if the initiation cost of a repair kappa R is", "tokens": [51133, 15067, 11269, 538, 3235, 4105, 13, 440, 5221, 12569, 1024, 300, 498, 264, 43569, 2063, 295, 257, 10535, 350, 25637, 497, 307, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 65950, "start": 680.66, "end": 685.8, "text": " cheaper than the continuous standing cost of maintenance kappa M, then a rational deferral window opens", "tokens": [51423, 12284, 813, 264, 10957, 4877, 2063, 295, 11258, 350, 25637, 376, 11, 550, 257, 15090, 25704, 2155, 4910, 9870, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 65950, "start": 685.8, "end": 689.42, "text": " immediately. Okay, wait, let's go back to my gym and ER analysis. Oh yes, perfect. So if you're", "tokens": [51680, 4258, 13, 1033, 11, 1699, 11, 718, 311, 352, 646, 281, 452, 9222, 293, 14929, 5215, 13, 876, 2086, 11, 2176, 13, 407, 498, 291, 434, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0977710485458374, "compression_ratio": 1.659942363112392, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043165722828598e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 68942, "start": 689.42, "end": 693.8199999999999, "text": " premium gym membership and personal trainer fees, your kappa M costs you $10,000 a month.", "tokens": [50365, 12049, 9222, 16560, 293, 2973, 21110, 13370, 11, 428, 350, 25637, 376, 5497, 291, 1848, 3279, 11, 1360, 257, 1618, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09046738426964562, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.789735677368287e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 68942, "start": 694.4599999999999, "end": 699.04, "text": " But the flat administrative fee to walk into the ER, your kappa R is only $50.", "tokens": [50617, 583, 264, 4962, 17900, 12054, 281, 1792, 666, 264, 14929, 11, 428, 350, 25637, 497, 307, 787, 1848, 2803, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09046738426964562, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.789735677368287e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 68942, "start": 699.68, "end": 705.16, "text": " Then purely on day one, before we even look at your actual biological health or the compounding rate", "tokens": [50878, 1396, 17491, 322, 786, 472, 11, 949, 321, 754, 574, 412, 428, 3539, 13910, 1585, 420, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09046738426964562, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.789735677368287e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 68942, "start": 705.16, "end": 711.16, "text": " of arterial plaque, the pure math of the overhead says, cancel the gym membership and wait until you", "tokens": [51152, 295, 30455, 831, 36542, 11, 264, 6075, 5221, 295, 264, 19922, 1619, 11, 10373, 264, 9222, 16560, 293, 1699, 1826, 291, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09046738426964562, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.789735677368287e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 68942, "start": 711.16, "end": 716.54, "text": " are sick. Exactly. Because the overhead of maintaining the capacity to fix the problem continuously", "tokens": [51452, 366, 4998, 13, 7587, 13, 1436, 264, 19922, 295, 14916, 264, 6042, 281, 3191, 264, 1154, 15684, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09046738426964562, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.789735677368287e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 71654, "start": 716.54, "end": 721.5, "text": " is vastly disproportionate to the overhead of triggering a one-off fix. Wow.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 41426, 28734, 473, 281, 264, 19922, 295, 40406, 257, 472, 12, 4506, 3191, 13, 3153, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06206631092798142, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352514623490852e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 71654, "start": 721.5, "end": 727.0, "text": " If kappa R is strictly less than kappa M, you unconditionally get what the author calls a unique", "tokens": [50613, 759, 350, 25637, 497, 307, 20792, 1570, 813, 350, 25637, 376, 11, 291, 34959, 15899, 483, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 257, 3845, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06206631092798142, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352514623490852e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 71654, "start": 727.0, "end": 733.8199999999999, "text": " threshold, T star. A window opens where doing absolutely nothing is mathematically cheaper than", "tokens": [50888, 14678, 11, 314, 3543, 13, 316, 4910, 9870, 689, 884, 3122, 1825, 307, 44003, 12284, 813, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06206631092798142, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352514623490852e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 71654, "start": 733.8199999999999, "end": 738.98, "text": " continuous intervention. But of course, that's only question one. Because the real world rarely offers", "tokens": [51229, 10957, 13176, 13, 583, 295, 1164, 11, 300, 311, 787, 1168, 472, 13, 1436, 264, 957, 1002, 13752, 7736, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06206631092798142, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.3352514623490852e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 73898, "start": 738.98, "end": 744.8000000000001, "text": " us a $10,000 gym membership and a $50 ER visit. Unfortunately. What happens if the standing", "tokens": [50365, 505, 257, 1848, 3279, 11, 1360, 9222, 16560, 293, 257, 1848, 2803, 14929, 3441, 13, 8590, 13, 708, 2314, 498, 264, 4877, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10458384804103686, "compression_ratio": 1.663265306122449, "no_speech_prob": 1.6346203904338275e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 73898, "start": 744.8000000000001, "end": 749.76, "text": " maintenance is actually incredibly cheap and the shock cost of a repair initiation is astronomical?", "tokens": [50656, 11258, 307, 767, 6252, 7084, 293, 264, 5588, 2063, 295, 257, 10535, 43569, 307, 49035, 30, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10458384804103686, "compression_ratio": 1.663265306122449, "no_speech_prob": 1.6346203904338275e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 73898, "start": 750.14, "end": 755.46, "text": " What if kappa M is less than or equal to kappa R? That brings us to the far more complex scenario,", "tokens": [50923, 708, 498, 350, 25637, 376, 307, 1570, 813, 420, 2681, 281, 350, 25637, 497, 30, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 1400, 544, 3997, 9005, 11, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10458384804103686, "compression_ratio": 1.663265306122449, "no_speech_prob": 1.6346203904338275e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 73898, "start": 755.66, "end": 760.74, "text": " which is question two. The author calls this the late recovery regime. The late recovery regime.", "tokens": [51199, 597, 307, 1168, 732, 13, 440, 3793, 5498, 341, 264, 3469, 8597, 13120, 13, 440, 3469, 8597, 13120, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10458384804103686, "compression_ratio": 1.663265306122449, "no_speech_prob": 1.6346203904338275e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 73898, "start": 760.82, "end": 766.64, "text": " Okay. If maintenance is cheaper than initiating a repair, then deferral is initially a terrible idea.", "tokens": [51457, 1033, 13, 759, 11258, 307, 12284, 813, 6265, 990, 257, 10535, 11, 550, 25704, 2155, 307, 9105, 257, 6237, 1558, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10458384804103686, "compression_ratio": 1.663265306122449, "no_speech_prob": 1.6346203904338275e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 76664, "start": 766.64, "end": 772.14, "text": " You should definitely pay for the cheap maintenance on day one. But the author asks this fascinating", "tokens": [50365, 509, 820, 2138, 1689, 337, 264, 7084, 11258, 322, 786, 472, 13, 583, 264, 3793, 8962, 341, 10343, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 76664, "start": 772.14, "end": 778.14, "text": " follow-up. Even if maintenance wins on day one, does a deferral window open later?", "tokens": [50640, 1524, 12, 1010, 13, 2754, 498, 11258, 10641, 322, 786, 472, 11, 775, 257, 25704, 2155, 4910, 1269, 1780, 30, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 76664, "start": 778.34, "end": 782.8, "text": " And this is where the math just gets incredibly wild. Let's try to visualize this for you,", "tokens": [50950, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 5221, 445, 2170, 6252, 4868, 13, 961, 311, 853, 281, 23273, 341, 337, 291, 11, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 76664, "start": 782.92, "end": 785.64, "text": " the listener, because we're talking about intersecting curves on a graph here.", "tokens": [51179, 264, 31569, 11, 570, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 27815, 278, 19490, 322, 257, 4295, 510, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 76664, "start": 785.68, "end": 787.52, "text": " Yeah. A mental image really helps here.", "tokens": [51317, 865, 13, 316, 4973, 3256, 534, 3665, 510, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 76664, "start": 787.64, "end": 793.12, "text": " Right. If I wait to fix something, common sense says the damage compounds. The fix gets exponentially", "tokens": [51415, 1779, 13, 759, 286, 1699, 281, 3191, 746, 11, 2689, 2020, 1619, 264, 4344, 21810, 13, 440, 3191, 2170, 37330, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06338780965560521, "compression_ratio": 1.5916398713826367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750278464608415e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 79312, "start": 793.12, "end": 799.2, "text": " harder. The cost goes up. But this theorem proves there are mathematical situations where waiting", "tokens": [50365, 6081, 13, 440, 2063, 1709, 493, 13, 583, 341, 20904, 25019, 456, 366, 18894, 6851, 689, 3806, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06086233287181669, "compression_ratio": 1.741444866920152, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881406874666213e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 79312, "start": 799.2, "end": 806.04, "text": " is a bad idea on day one becomes the smart economic move on day 10, but then becomes a terrible idea", "tokens": [50669, 307, 257, 1578, 1558, 322, 786, 472, 3643, 264, 4069, 4836, 1286, 322, 786, 1266, 11, 457, 550, 3643, 257, 6237, 1558, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06086233287181669, "compression_ratio": 1.741444866920152, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881406874666213e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 79312, "start": 806.04, "end": 809.32, "text": " again on day 20. The window opens and then the window closes.", "tokens": [51011, 797, 322, 786, 945, 13, 440, 4910, 9870, 293, 550, 264, 4910, 24157, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06086233287181669, "compression_ratio": 1.741444866920152, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881406874666213e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 79312, "start": 810.02, "end": 815.82, "text": " Right. But why? Why would the window close? Why does the math create a temporary sweet spot for", "tokens": [51210, 1779, 13, 583, 983, 30, 1545, 576, 264, 4910, 1998, 30, 1545, 775, 264, 5221, 1884, 257, 13413, 3844, 4008, 337, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06086233287181669, "compression_ratio": 1.741444866920152, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881406874666213e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 79312, "start": 815.82, "end": 821.24, "text": " procrastination? To understand the mechanism behind this, we have to visualize the mathematical curve", "tokens": [51500, 39306, 2486, 30, 1407, 1223, 264, 7513, 2261, 341, 11, 321, 362, 281, 23273, 264, 18894, 7605, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06086233287181669, "compression_ratio": 1.741444866920152, "no_speech_prob": 1.3881406874666213e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 82124, "start": 821.24, "end": 825.28, "text": " of the cost differential. The author calls this D of T. D of T.", "tokens": [50365, 295, 264, 2063, 15756, 13, 440, 3793, 5498, 341, 413, 295, 314, 13, 413, 295, 314, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 82124, "start": 825.54, "end": 831.08, "text": " This curve represents the cost of deferred repair minus the accumulated cost of continuous maintenance", "tokens": [50580, 639, 7605, 8855, 264, 2063, 295, 25704, 986, 10535, 3175, 264, 31346, 2063, 295, 10957, 11258, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 82124, "start": 831.08, "end": 834.92, "text": " over time. So we're comparing two completely different geometric shapes.", "tokens": [50857, 670, 565, 13, 407, 321, 434, 15763, 732, 2584, 819, 33246, 10854, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 82124, "start": 835.0, "end": 839.5, "text": " Okay. Let's build this graph. So on the x-axis, we have time passing. And on the y-axis,", "tokens": [51053, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 1322, 341, 4295, 13, 407, 322, 264, 2031, 12, 24633, 11, 321, 362, 565, 8437, 13, 400, 322, 264, 288, 12, 24633, 11, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 82124, "start": 839.7, "end": 841.04, "text": " we have the difference in cost.", "tokens": [51288, 321, 362, 264, 2649, 294, 2063, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 82124, "start": 841.12, "end": 846.32, "text": " Exactly. Now, the accumulated cost of continuous maintenance grows linearly. It's a steady,", "tokens": [51359, 7587, 13, 823, 11, 264, 31346, 2063, 295, 10957, 11258, 13156, 43586, 13, 467, 311, 257, 13211, 11, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945661681038993, "compression_ratio": 1.7936507936507937, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211886213161498e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 84632, "start": 846.32, "end": 850.9200000000001, "text": " predictable, upward slope. You pay your kappa M every single day.", "tokens": [50365, 27737, 11, 23452, 13525, 13, 509, 1689, 428, 350, 25637, 376, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 84632, "start": 850.9200000000001, "end": 852.0200000000001, "text": " Like clockwork.", "tokens": [50595, 1743, 7830, 1902, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 84632, "start": 852.36, "end": 858.3000000000001, "text": " Right. But the cost of deferred repair behaves differently. Because of the exponential convexity,", "tokens": [50667, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 2063, 295, 25704, 986, 10535, 36896, 7614, 13, 1436, 295, 264, 21510, 42432, 507, 11, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 84632, "start": 858.44, "end": 865.1, "text": " our P variable, and the compounding damage, delta, the repair cost doesn't start high. It starts low,", "tokens": [50971, 527, 430, 7006, 11, 293, 264, 14154, 278, 4344, 11, 8289, 11, 264, 10535, 2063, 1177, 380, 722, 1090, 13, 467, 3719, 2295, 11, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 84632, "start": 865.24, "end": 868.12, "text": " but eventually it curves violently upward to infinity.", "tokens": [51311, 457, 4728, 309, 19490, 46728, 23452, 281, 13202, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 84632, "start": 868.62, "end": 872.32, "text": " So because the continuous maintenance takes an immediate, heavy, linear toll,", "tokens": [51480, 407, 570, 264, 10957, 11258, 2516, 364, 11629, 11, 4676, 11, 8213, 16629, 11, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18213094846166747, "compression_ratio": 1.550561797752809, "no_speech_prob": 1.3509869221592363e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 87232, "start": 872.32, "end": 877.72, "text": " but the deferred repair cost starts slow before it explodes, the difference between them forms a", "tokens": [50365, 457, 264, 25704, 986, 10535, 2063, 3719, 2964, 949, 309, 42610, 11, 264, 2649, 1296, 552, 6422, 257, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697317538054093, "compression_ratio": 1.7098976109215016, "no_speech_prob": 2.201372330951079e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 87232, "start": 877.72, "end": 883.94, "text": " specific shape. It forms a single dip, a valley on the graph. A valley. Right. The curve of D of T", "tokens": [50635, 2685, 3909, 13, 467, 6422, 257, 2167, 10460, 11, 257, 17636, 322, 264, 4295, 13, 316, 17636, 13, 1779, 13, 440, 7605, 295, 413, 295, 314, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697317538054093, "compression_ratio": 1.7098976109215016, "no_speech_prob": 2.201372330951079e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 87232, "start": 883.94, "end": 889.6400000000001, "text": " starts above zero, meaning maintenance is currently the cheaper dominant strategy. But if the parameters", "tokens": [50946, 3719, 3673, 4018, 11, 3620, 11258, 307, 4362, 264, 12284, 15657, 5206, 13, 583, 498, 264, 9834, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697317538054093, "compression_ratio": 1.7098976109215016, "no_speech_prob": 2.201372330951079e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 87232, "start": 889.6400000000001, "end": 895.82, "text": " align, the unconstrained minimum of that curve, the very bottom of the valley, might actually dip below", "tokens": [51231, 7975, 11, 264, 35847, 19639, 2001, 7285, 295, 300, 7605, 11, 264, 588, 2767, 295, 264, 17636, 11, 1062, 767, 10460, 2507, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697317538054093, "compression_ratio": 1.7098976109215016, "no_speech_prob": 2.201372330951079e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 87232, "start": 895.82, "end": 901.6400000000001, "text": " the zero line as time passes. And the moment that curve crosses into the negative, it means that", "tokens": [51540, 264, 4018, 1622, 382, 565, 11335, 13, 400, 264, 1623, 300, 7605, 28467, 666, 264, 3671, 11, 309, 1355, 300, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697317538054093, "compression_ratio": 1.7098976109215016, "no_speech_prob": 2.201372330951079e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 90164, "start": 901.64, "end": 908.66, "text": " suddenly, shockingly, a massive delayed repair is now cheaper than the accumulated exhausting drain", "tokens": [50365, 5800, 11, 5588, 12163, 11, 257, 5994, 20268, 10535, 307, 586, 12284, 813, 264, 31346, 34076, 12339, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07120126158326537, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610317280287614e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 90164, "start": 908.66, "end": 912.52, "text": " of all that daily continuous maintenance. The deferral window has opened.", "tokens": [50716, 295, 439, 300, 5212, 10957, 11258, 13, 440, 25704, 2155, 4910, 575, 5625, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07120126158326537, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610317280287614e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 90164, "start": 912.92, "end": 919.1999999999999, "text": " Yes. But here is the critical part of the late recovery completion theorem. That curve cannot stay", "tokens": [50929, 1079, 13, 583, 510, 307, 264, 4924, 644, 295, 264, 3469, 8597, 19372, 20904, 13, 663, 7605, 2644, 1754, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07120126158326537, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610317280287614e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 90164, "start": 919.1999999999999, "end": 921.38, "text": " in the negative. Because of the exponential part.", "tokens": [51243, 294, 264, 3671, 13, 1436, 295, 264, 21510, 644, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07120126158326537, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610317280287614e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 90164, "start": 921.5, "end": 927.4399999999999, "text": " Exactly. Because the repair cost is driven by exponential convexity P, it will eventually outpace", "tokens": [51358, 7587, 13, 1436, 264, 10535, 2063, 307, 9555, 538, 21510, 42432, 507, 430, 11, 309, 486, 4728, 484, 17940, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07120126158326537, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610317280287614e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 92744, "start": 927.44, "end": 931.9200000000001, "text": " any linear accumulation. The curve hits the bottom of the valley and then rockets back up,", "tokens": [50365, 604, 8213, 35647, 13, 440, 7605, 8664, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 17636, 293, 550, 28361, 646, 493, 11, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 92744, "start": 932.08, "end": 934.46, "text": " crossing the zero line again. And the window slams shut.", "tokens": [50597, 14712, 264, 4018, 1622, 797, 13, 400, 264, 4910, 1061, 4070, 5309, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 92744, "start": 934.46, "end": 938.7600000000001, "text": " The theorem mathematically guarantees that if a deferral window opens later,", "tokens": [50716, 440, 20904, 44003, 32567, 300, 498, 257, 25704, 2155, 4910, 9870, 1780, 11, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 92744, "start": 939.1600000000001, "end": 943.9200000000001, "text": " it is a strictly finite interval. It's not a permanent cutover to a new strategy.", "tokens": [50951, 309, 307, 257, 20792, 19362, 15035, 13, 467, 311, 406, 257, 10996, 1723, 3570, 281, 257, 777, 5206, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 92744, "start": 944.4000000000001, "end": 951.0200000000001, "text": " There is a precise, mathematically optimal window to procrastinate, bracketed on both sides by points", "tokens": [51213, 821, 307, 257, 13600, 11, 44003, 16252, 4910, 281, 39306, 13923, 11, 12305, 10993, 322, 1293, 4881, 538, 2793, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 92744, "start": 951.0200000000001, "end": 957.1800000000001, "text": " of catastrophic ruin. That is just incredible. The idea that procrastination isn't a straight line", "tokens": [51544, 295, 34915, 15514, 13, 663, 307, 445, 4651, 13, 440, 1558, 300, 39306, 2486, 1943, 380, 257, 2997, 1622, 51852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10015364107878312, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 1.803786829103482e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 95718, "start": 957.18, "end": 960.1999999999999, "text": " toward failure, but a temporary valley of efficiency.", "tokens": [50365, 7361, 7763, 11, 457, 257, 13413, 17636, 295, 10493, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 95718, "start": 960.4799999999999, "end": 962.6999999999999, "text": " It really changes how you look at delays.", "tokens": [50530, 467, 534, 2962, 577, 291, 574, 412, 28610, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 95718, "start": 962.6999999999999, "end": 969.14, "text": " Totally. But the author also introduces a caveat here, right? A concept called the early recovery", "tokens": [50641, 22837, 13, 583, 264, 3793, 611, 31472, 257, 43012, 510, 11, 558, 30, 316, 3410, 1219, 264, 2440, 8597, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 95718, "start": 969.14, "end": 973.92, "text": " condition. Because this valley doesn't always dip below the zero line.", "tokens": [50963, 4188, 13, 1436, 341, 17636, 1177, 380, 1009, 10460, 2507, 264, 4018, 1622, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 95718, "start": 974.04, "end": 975.7199999999999, "text": " That's an essential clarification. Yeah.", "tokens": [51208, 663, 311, 364, 7115, 34449, 13, 865, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 95718, "start": 975.8599999999999, "end": 976.02, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51299, 865, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 95718, "start": 976.2399999999999, "end": 981.78, "text": " The early recovery condition dictates that if the mathematical curve reaches the bottom of its valley,", "tokens": [51318, 440, 2440, 8597, 4188, 12569, 1024, 300, 498, 264, 18894, 7605, 14235, 264, 2767, 295, 1080, 17636, 11, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 95718, "start": 981.9799999999999, "end": 987.06, "text": " the point of maximum advantage for deferred repair before the first unit of time has even passed,", "tokens": [51605, 264, 935, 295, 6674, 5002, 337, 25704, 986, 10535, 949, 264, 700, 4985, 295, 565, 575, 754, 4678, 11, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12136808757124276, "compression_ratio": 1.673202614379085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132659665281767e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 98718, "start": 987.18, "end": 992.62, "text": " then the window never opens. Wait, how can it reach the bottom of the valley before time even", "tokens": [50365, 550, 264, 4910, 1128, 9870, 13, 3802, 11, 577, 393, 309, 2524, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 17636, 949, 565, 754, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0744612364642388, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 98718, "start": 992.62, "end": 998.4, "text": " starts? I mean, in pure math, it means the geometry of the curves places the lowest point to the left of", "tokens": [50637, 3719, 30, 286, 914, 11, 294, 6075, 5221, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 19490, 3190, 264, 12437, 935, 281, 264, 1411, 295, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0744612364642388, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 98718, "start": 998.4, "end": 1003.76, "text": " the y-axis. Oh, I see. In physical terms, it means the system has already passed its theoretical point", "tokens": [50926, 264, 288, 12, 24633, 13, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 682, 4001, 2115, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 1185, 575, 1217, 4678, 1080, 20864, 935, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0744612364642388, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 98718, "start": 1003.76, "end": 1008.3, "text": " of maximum advantage before you are even capable of making your first intervention decision.", "tokens": [51194, 295, 6674, 5002, 949, 291, 366, 754, 8189, 295, 1455, 428, 700, 13176, 3537, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0744612364642388, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 98718, "start": 1008.78, "end": 1014.28, "text": " If that condition holds, continuous maintenance weakly dominates repair from the very first moment,", "tokens": [51445, 759, 300, 4188, 9190, 11, 10957, 11258, 5336, 356, 8859, 1024, 10535, 490, 264, 588, 700, 1623, 11, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0744612364642388, "compression_ratio": 1.703448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 101428, "start": 1014.28, "end": 1016.02, "text": " and it will dominate it forever.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 309, 486, 28246, 309, 5680, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 101428, "start": 1016.4399999999999, "end": 1022.5, "text": " So, to summarize this incredibly elegant core theorem, deciding when to defer is really a", "tokens": [50473, 407, 11, 281, 20858, 341, 6252, 21117, 4965, 20904, 11, 17990, 562, 281, 25704, 307, 534, 257, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 101428, "start": 1022.5, "end": 1023.72, "text": " two-part test. Yes.", "tokens": [50776, 732, 12, 6971, 1500, 13, 1079, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 101428, "start": 1023.88, "end": 1029.22, "text": " Question one just looks at the static overheads. Is the standing cost of readiness cheaper than the", "tokens": [50845, 14464, 472, 445, 1542, 412, 264, 13437, 19922, 82, 13, 1119, 264, 4877, 2063, 295, 34954, 12284, 813, 264, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 101428, "start": 1029.22, "end": 1032.86, "text": " shock cost of initiation? If no, you delay immediately.", "tokens": [51112, 5588, 2063, 295, 43569, 30, 759, 572, 11, 291, 8577, 4258, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 101428, "start": 1033.1, "end": 1033.3999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51306, 1779, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939270264063126, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214498056195016e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 103340, "start": 1033.4, "end": 1038.74, "text": " If, yes, we move to question two, which is purely geometric, we look at the shape of the compounding", "tokens": [50365, 759, 11, 2086, 11, 321, 1286, 281, 1168, 732, 11, 597, 307, 17491, 33246, 11, 321, 574, 412, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 14154, 278, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 103340, "start": 1038.74, "end": 1043.8200000000002, "text": " cost curve to see if the delayed exponential explosion temporarily dips below the immediate", "tokens": [50632, 2063, 7605, 281, 536, 498, 264, 20268, 21510, 15673, 23750, 47814, 2507, 264, 11629, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 103340, "start": 1043.8200000000002, "end": 1048.1200000000001, "text": " linear drain of maintenance. If it does, we get a finite window to delay.", "tokens": [50886, 8213, 12339, 295, 11258, 13, 759, 309, 775, 11, 321, 483, 257, 19362, 4910, 281, 8577, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 103340, "start": 1048.38, "end": 1053.22, "text": " And what Fliction has achieved here is an exhaustive classification. These two questions and their", "tokens": [51114, 400, 437, 3235, 4105, 575, 11042, 510, 307, 364, 14687, 488, 21538, 13, 1981, 732, 1651, 293, 641, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 103340, "start": 1053.22, "end": 1059.1200000000001, "text": " respective mechanisms yield a complete map of every possible deferral regime in any system.", "tokens": [51356, 23649, 15902, 11257, 257, 3566, 4471, 295, 633, 1944, 25704, 2155, 13120, 294, 604, 1185, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 103340, "start": 1059.5, "end": 1060.46, "text": " The math is absolute.", "tokens": [51670, 440, 5221, 307, 8236, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08021746741400824, "compression_ratio": 1.6348122866894197, "no_speech_prob": 1.52489457692917e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 106046, "start": 1060.46, "end": 1065.1200000000001, "text": " But there is a catch. The math is absolute. We are humans operating inside messy reality.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 456, 307, 257, 3745, 13, 440, 5221, 307, 8236, 13, 492, 366, 6255, 7447, 1854, 16191, 4103, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 106046, "start": 1065.96, "end": 1066.26, "text": " Very true.", "tokens": [50640, 4372, 2074, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 106046, "start": 1066.38, "end": 1070.22, "text": " We don't have perfect godlike knowledge of these variables. What happens when we miscalculate?", "tokens": [50661, 492, 500, 380, 362, 2176, 3044, 4092, 3601, 295, 613, 9102, 13, 708, 2314, 562, 321, 3346, 9895, 2444, 473, 30, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 106046, "start": 1070.9, "end": 1074.3400000000001, "text": " Specifically, what happens when we misjudge that silent killer we talked about,", "tokens": [50887, 26058, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 321, 3346, 9218, 432, 300, 12784, 13364, 321, 2825, 466, 11, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 106046, "start": 1074.76, "end": 1079.22, "text": " compounding deviation? Because this leads us into the third major section of the text,", "tokens": [51080, 14154, 278, 25163, 30, 1436, 341, 6689, 505, 666, 264, 2636, 2563, 3541, 295, 264, 2487, 11, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 106046, "start": 1079.7, "end": 1081.0, "text": " the danger of the static view.", "tokens": [51327, 264, 4330, 295, 264, 13437, 1910, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 106046, "start": 1081.26, "end": 1087.1000000000001, "text": " The altar pivots from theoretical classification to a really profound warning about human intuition here.", "tokens": [51405, 440, 31435, 280, 592, 1971, 490, 20864, 21538, 281, 257, 534, 14382, 9164, 466, 1952, 24002, 510, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13478769807734042, "compression_ratio": 1.6633333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.3164352380700137e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 108710, "start": 1087.1, "end": 1092.34, "text": " This section outlines exactly what happens when a system tries to estimate its threshold.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 3541, 40125, 2293, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 1185, 9898, 281, 12539, 1080, 14678, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 108710, "start": 1092.8999999999999, "end": 1098.4399999999998, "text": " You know, how long it can safely wait to fix a problem under the real-world condition of compounding delta", "tokens": [50655, 509, 458, 11, 577, 938, 309, 393, 11750, 1699, 281, 3191, 257, 1154, 833, 264, 957, 12, 13217, 4188, 295, 14154, 278, 8289, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 108710, "start": 1098.4399999999998, "end": 1101.52, "text": " versus a static baseline where delta equals zero.", "tokens": [50932, 5717, 257, 13437, 20518, 689, 8289, 6915, 4018, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 108710, "start": 1102.1, "end": 1106.6999999999998, "text": " Let's go back to our baseline of the paper backlog that doesn't breed.", "tokens": [51115, 961, 311, 352, 646, 281, 527, 20518, 295, 264, 3035, 47364, 300, 1177, 380, 18971, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 108710, "start": 1107.24, "end": 1108.3799999999999, "text": " The static environment.", "tokens": [51372, 440, 13437, 2823, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 108710, "start": 1109.08, "end": 1113.48, "text": " The altar gives a name to the threshold in that static baseline, which is T1.", "tokens": [51464, 440, 31435, 2709, 257, 1315, 281, 264, 14678, 294, 300, 13437, 20518, 11, 597, 307, 314, 16, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1553440960970792, "compression_ratio": 1.6303501945525292, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503476524768137e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 111348, "start": 1113.48, "end": 1119.54, "text": " Right. T1 represents how long you think you have if you assume the problem just accumulates linearly", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 314, 16, 8855, 577, 938, 291, 519, 291, 362, 498, 291, 6552, 264, 1154, 445, 12989, 26192, 43586, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 111348, "start": 1119.54, "end": 1125.54, "text": " without actively worsening itself. It relies purely on the curvature of cost, p, and the ratio of those", "tokens": [50668, 1553, 13022, 47567, 4559, 2564, 13, 467, 30910, 17491, 322, 264, 37638, 295, 2063, 11, 280, 11, 293, 264, 8509, 295, 729, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 111348, "start": 1125.54, "end": 1126.8, "text": " overheads we just discussed.", "tokens": [50968, 19922, 82, 321, 445, 7152, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 111348, "start": 1127.02, "end": 1127.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51042, 1779, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 111348, "start": 1127.28, "end": 1132.08, "text": " It's an incredibly common assumption in management and engineering. We look at a problem, we gauge its", "tokens": [51055, 467, 311, 364, 6252, 2689, 15302, 294, 4592, 293, 7043, 13, 492, 574, 412, 257, 1154, 11, 321, 17924, 1080, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 111348, "start": 1132.08, "end": 1136.38, "text": " current size, and we calculate a timeline based on a static snapshot of the decay.", "tokens": [51295, 2190, 2744, 11, 293, 321, 8873, 257, 12933, 2361, 322, 257, 13437, 30163, 295, 264, 21039, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 111348, "start": 1136.58, "end": 1142.64, "text": " We assume the windshield crack is just a static physical feature, not an active process of structural failure.", "tokens": [51520, 492, 6552, 264, 39996, 6226, 307, 445, 257, 13437, 4001, 4111, 11, 406, 364, 4967, 1399, 295, 15067, 7763, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09381074052516038, "compression_ratio": 1.6940063091482649, "no_speech_prob": 2.1931211187375954e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 114264, "start": 1142.64, "end": 1148.7, "text": " Exactly. But the author derives a perturbative estimate to show the exact mathematical penalty", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 583, 264, 3793, 1163, 1539, 257, 40468, 1166, 12539, 281, 855, 264, 1900, 18894, 16263, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07614535892132632, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747604822051065e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 114264, "start": 1148.7, "end": 1154.96, "text": " of that assumption. They show exactly how much time you lose when you introduce even a tiny fractional", "tokens": [50668, 295, 300, 15302, 13, 814, 855, 2293, 577, 709, 565, 291, 3624, 562, 291, 5366, 754, 257, 5870, 17948, 1966, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07614535892132632, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747604822051065e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 114264, "start": 1154.96, "end": 1157.94, "text": " bit of compounding delta into a system you thought was static.", "tokens": [50981, 857, 295, 14154, 278, 8289, 666, 257, 1185, 291, 1194, 390, 13437, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07614535892132632, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747604822051065e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 114264, "start": 1158.4, "end": 1164.5800000000002, "text": " And the math here reveals a mechanism that feels almost cruel, honestly. The text explicitly states", "tokens": [51153, 400, 264, 5221, 510, 20893, 257, 7513, 300, 3417, 1920, 16022, 11, 6095, 13, 440, 2487, 20803, 4368, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07614535892132632, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747604822051065e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 114264, "start": 1164.5800000000002, "end": 1168.76, "text": " that the delta correction, the amount of time subtracted from your safe window scales,", "tokens": [51462, 300, 264, 8289, 19984, 11, 264, 2372, 295, 565, 16390, 292, 490, 428, 3273, 4910, 17408, 11, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07614535892132632, "compression_ratio": 1.6555555555555554, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747604822051065e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 116876, "start": 1168.76, "end": 1172.56, "text": " with the value of T1 multiplied by T1 minus 1.", "tokens": [50365, 365, 264, 2158, 295, 314, 16, 17207, 538, 314, 16, 3175, 502, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 116876, "start": 1172.72, "end": 1175.76, "text": " Which is a devastating formula if you think about its implications.", "tokens": [50563, 3013, 307, 257, 21280, 8513, 498, 291, 519, 466, 1080, 16602, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 116876, "start": 1176.18, "end": 1178.7, "text": " Let's break down why that formula is so devastating.", "tokens": [50736, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 983, 300, 8513, 307, 370, 21280, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 116876, "start": 1179.58, "end": 1185.54, "text": " If the penalty scales with T1 times T1 minus 1, that means systems with a large static baseline", "tokens": [50906, 759, 264, 16263, 17408, 365, 314, 16, 1413, 314, 16, 3175, 502, 11, 300, 1355, 3652, 365, 257, 2416, 13437, 20518, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 116876, "start": 1185.54, "end": 1191.28, "text": " systems that look like they can tolerate a massive long deferral window are punished geometrically", "tokens": [51204, 3652, 300, 574, 411, 436, 393, 25773, 257, 5994, 938, 25704, 2155, 4910, 366, 22365, 12956, 81, 984, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 116876, "start": 1191.28, "end": 1192.68, "text": " harder than fragile systems.", "tokens": [51491, 6081, 813, 23847, 3652, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 116876, "start": 1192.82, "end": 1196.24, "text": " Let's run some hypothetical numbers to illustrate this, because the mechanism is key.", "tokens": [51568, 961, 311, 1190, 512, 33053, 3547, 281, 23221, 341, 11, 570, 264, 7513, 307, 2141, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10251652342932564, "compression_ratio": 1.6795774647887325, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104548893047023e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 119624, "start": 1196.24, "end": 1202.16, "text": " If a small, fragile system calculates its static threshold T1 as just two days, the penalty", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1359, 11, 23847, 1185, 4322, 1024, 1080, 13437, 14678, 314, 16, 382, 445, 732, 1708, 11, 264, 16263, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 119624, "start": 1202.16, "end": 1205.24, "text": " from compounding scales with 2 times 1, which is 2.", "tokens": [50661, 490, 14154, 278, 17408, 365, 568, 1413, 502, 11, 597, 307, 568, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 119624, "start": 1205.32, "end": 1206.68, "text": " Okay, so the penalty is small.", "tokens": [50819, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 16263, 307, 1359, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 119624, "start": 1206.96, "end": 1213.34, "text": " Right. But if a massive, resilient system calculates its T1 as 10 days, the penalty doesn't just", "tokens": [50901, 1779, 13, 583, 498, 257, 5994, 11, 23699, 1185, 4322, 1024, 1080, 314, 16, 382, 1266, 1708, 11, 264, 16263, 1177, 380, 445, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 119624, "start": 1213.34, "end": 1217.1200000000001, "text": " scale by 10. It scales by 10 times 9, which is 90.", "tokens": [51220, 4373, 538, 1266, 13, 467, 17408, 538, 1266, 1413, 1722, 11, 597, 307, 4289, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 119624, "start": 1217.32, "end": 1222.5, "text": " Wow. The larger your apparent buffer, the faster the compounding reality eats it alive.", "tokens": [51419, 3153, 13, 440, 4833, 428, 18335, 21762, 11, 264, 4663, 264, 14154, 278, 4103, 18109, 309, 5465, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07976690068975226, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579865073032776e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 122250, "start": 1222.5, "end": 1223.02, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 122250, "start": 1223.1, "end": 1227.74, "text": " I want to build out an analogy here to make sure this counterintuitive mechanism is crystal clear.", "tokens": [50395, 286, 528, 281, 1322, 484, 364, 21663, 510, 281, 652, 988, 341, 5682, 686, 48314, 7513, 307, 13662, 1850, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 122250, "start": 1227.86, "end": 1228.34, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [50633, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 122250, "start": 1228.58, "end": 1233.8, "text": " Imagine a massive, wealthy, incredibly well-resourced global corporation.", "tokens": [50669, 11739, 257, 5994, 11, 17707, 11, 6252, 731, 12, 495, 396, 1232, 4338, 22197, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 122250, "start": 1234.42, "end": 1238.72, "text": " They discover a deep toxic cultural issue in one of their core departments.", "tokens": [50961, 814, 4411, 257, 2452, 12786, 6988, 2734, 294, 472, 295, 641, 4965, 15326, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 122250, "start": 1239.24, "end": 1244.14, "text": " Because they have billions in the bank, standing HR infrastructure, and massive market share,", "tokens": [51202, 1436, 436, 362, 17375, 294, 264, 3765, 11, 4877, 19460, 6896, 11, 293, 5994, 2142, 2073, 11, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 122250, "start": 1244.58, "end": 1247.36, "text": " their nominal baseline, their T1, is huge.", "tokens": [51469, 641, 41641, 20518, 11, 641, 314, 16, 11, 307, 2603, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 122250, "start": 1247.48, "end": 1248.38, "text": " Yeah, they feel invincible.", "tokens": [51614, 865, 11, 436, 841, 48514, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218786720917603, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360735225240846e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 124838, "start": 1248.38, "end": 1252.8000000000002, "text": " They look at the static snapshot of the problem and think, we have a five-year runway to slowly", "tokens": [50365, 814, 574, 412, 264, 13437, 30163, 295, 264, 1154, 293, 519, 11, 321, 362, 257, 1732, 12, 5294, 26642, 281, 5692, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 124838, "start": 1252.8000000000002, "end": 1255.5200000000002, "text": " fix this culture before it actually impacts our bottom line.", "tokens": [50586, 3191, 341, 3713, 949, 309, 767, 11606, 527, 2767, 1622, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 124838, "start": 1255.64, "end": 1259.14, "text": " They're relying entirely on the strength of their standing overheads to protect them.", "tokens": [50728, 814, 434, 24140, 7696, 322, 264, 3800, 295, 641, 4877, 19922, 82, 281, 2371, 552, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 124838, "start": 1259.2800000000002, "end": 1259.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50910, 7587, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 124838, "start": 1259.94, "end": 1260.1200000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50943, 865, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 124838, "start": 1260.2800000000002, "end": 1263.4, "text": " But because they think they have so much time, they defer the intervention.", "tokens": [50960, 583, 570, 436, 519, 436, 362, 370, 709, 565, 11, 436, 25704, 264, 13176, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 124838, "start": 1263.5400000000002, "end": 1264.2, "text": " They leave it alone.", "tokens": [51123, 814, 1856, 309, 3312, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 124838, "start": 1264.8200000000002, "end": 1267.18, "text": " But toxic culture is not a static paper pile.", "tokens": [51187, 583, 12786, 3713, 307, 406, 257, 13437, 3035, 14375, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 124838, "start": 1267.5800000000002, "end": 1268.44, "text": " It has a high delta.", "tokens": [51325, 467, 575, 257, 1090, 8289, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 124838, "start": 1268.9, "end": 1269.5600000000002, "text": " It compounds.", "tokens": [51391, 467, 21810, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 124838, "start": 1269.72, "end": 1270.1200000000001, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51432, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 124838, "start": 1270.1200000000001, "end": 1270.98, "text": " Good people quit.", "tokens": [51452, 2205, 561, 10366, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 124838, "start": 1271.42, "end": 1273.5600000000002, "text": " Bad managers hire more bad managers.", "tokens": [51517, 11523, 14084, 11158, 544, 1578, 14084, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 124838, "start": 1274.0400000000002, "end": 1275.24, "text": " Resentment breeds apathy.", "tokens": [51648, 5015, 317, 518, 41609, 1882, 9527, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13572027299787615, "compression_ratio": 1.6319018404907975, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070373736389094e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 127524, "start": 1275.24, "end": 1278.04, "text": " The deviation amplifies endogenously.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 25163, 9731, 11221, 917, 8799, 5098, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 127524, "start": 1278.84, "end": 1284.28, "text": " And because their initial static baseline was so large, the math of T1 times T1 minus", "tokens": [50545, 400, 570, 641, 5883, 13437, 20518, 390, 370, 2416, 11, 264, 5221, 295, 314, 16, 1413, 314, 16, 3175, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 127524, "start": 1284.28, "end": 1289.52, "text": " one says their five-year runway actually evaporates exponentially faster than a tiny, fragile,", "tokens": [50817, 472, 1619, 641, 1732, 12, 5294, 26642, 767, 26315, 1024, 37330, 4663, 813, 257, 5870, 11, 23847, 11, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 127524, "start": 1289.8, "end": 1295.34, "text": " 10-person startup that discovered the exact same toxic culture but knew from day one it", "tokens": [51093, 1266, 12, 10813, 18578, 300, 6941, 264, 1900, 912, 12786, 3713, 457, 2586, 490, 786, 472, 309, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 127524, "start": 1295.34, "end": 1296.92, "text": " only had three months to survive.", "tokens": [51370, 787, 632, 1045, 2493, 281, 7867, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 127524, "start": 1297.18, "end": 1300.8, "text": " The mechanism in your analogy perfectly mirrors the mathematical proof.", "tokens": [51462, 440, 7513, 294, 428, 21663, 6239, 24238, 264, 18894, 8177, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0971280666107827, "compression_ratio": 1.537313432835821, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856353773394116e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 130080, "start": 1300.8, "end": 1305.78, "text": " The text explicitly demonstrates that deferral tolerance is not eroded uniformly across", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 20803, 31034, 300, 25704, 2155, 23368, 307, 406, 1189, 12340, 48806, 2108, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 130080, "start": 1305.78, "end": 1306.62, "text": " different systems.", "tokens": [50614, 819, 3652, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 130080, "start": 1306.8999999999999, "end": 1311.58, "text": " It's eroded fastest in the precise systems that most appear on a static reading to be", "tokens": [50670, 467, 311, 1189, 12340, 14573, 294, 264, 13600, 3652, 300, 881, 4204, 322, 257, 13437, 3760, 281, 312, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 130080, "start": 1311.58, "end": 1312.8, "text": " able to afford the delay.", "tokens": [50904, 1075, 281, 6157, 264, 8577, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 130080, "start": 1313.2, "end": 1316.2, "text": " Institutional strength literally creates a lethal illusion of time.", "tokens": [50985, 2730, 41859, 3800, 3736, 7829, 257, 34562, 18854, 295, 565, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 130080, "start": 1316.48, "end": 1318.8999999999999, "text": " The bigger you are, the more the static view lies to you.", "tokens": [51149, 440, 3801, 291, 366, 11, 264, 544, 264, 13437, 1910, 9134, 281, 291, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 130080, "start": 1319.04, "end": 1320.6599999999999, "text": " That is the core warning of the essay.", "tokens": [51277, 663, 307, 264, 4965, 9164, 295, 264, 16238, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 130080, "start": 1320.9199999999998, "end": 1325.76, "text": " If a system reasons about its deferral windows without actively, continuously recalculating the", "tokens": [51371, 759, 257, 1185, 4112, 466, 1080, 25704, 2155, 9309, 1553, 13022, 11, 15684, 850, 304, 2444, 990, 264, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 130080, "start": 1325.76, "end": 1329.46, "text": " delta parameter, if it just looks at the static size of the problem and the current cost of", "tokens": [51613, 8289, 13075, 11, 498, 309, 445, 1542, 412, 264, 13437, 2744, 295, 264, 1154, 293, 264, 2190, 2063, 295, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09054238146001642, "compression_ratio": 1.7303030303030302, "no_speech_prob": 1.5103112987677192e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 132946, "start": 1329.46, "end": 1333.66, "text": " the fix, it will systematically and aggressively overestimate how much time it has until", "tokens": [50365, 264, 3191, 11, 309, 486, 39531, 293, 32024, 670, 377, 2905, 577, 709, 565, 309, 575, 1826, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 132946, "start": 1333.66, "end": 1335.1200000000001, "text": " catastrophic failure.", "tokens": [50575, 34915, 7763, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 132946, "start": 1335.28, "end": 1335.9, "text": " That's terrifying.", "tokens": [50656, 663, 311, 18106, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 132946, "start": 1336.04, "end": 1336.48, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50694, 467, 307, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 132946, "start": 1336.78, "end": 1342.4, "text": " The exact same growth rate that seems negligible on day one will devour a generous threshold", "tokens": [50731, 440, 1900, 912, 4599, 3314, 300, 2544, 32570, 964, 322, 786, 472, 486, 1905, 396, 257, 14537, 14678, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 132946, "start": 1342.4, "end": 1344.22, "text": " disproportionately fast.", "tokens": [51012, 43397, 2370, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 132946, "start": 1344.66, "end": 1347.28, "text": " So we've spent a lot of time in the abstract math here.", "tokens": [51125, 407, 321, 600, 4418, 257, 688, 295, 565, 294, 264, 12649, 5221, 510, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 132946, "start": 1347.28, "end": 1351.96, "text": " We have our continuous linear drains, our delayed exponential explosions, or evaporating", "tokens": [51256, 492, 362, 527, 10957, 8213, 47694, 11, 527, 20268, 21510, 36872, 11, 420, 26315, 990, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 132946, "start": 1351.96, "end": 1352.5, "text": " runways.", "tokens": [51490, 1190, 942, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 132946, "start": 1352.74, "end": 1356.6000000000001, "text": " But the author doesn't just leave this as an abstract theory for mathematicians.", "tokens": [51529, 583, 264, 3793, 1177, 380, 445, 1856, 341, 382, 364, 12649, 5261, 337, 32811, 2567, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 132946, "start": 1356.7, "end": 1357.42, "text": " No, they don't.", "tokens": [51727, 883, 11, 436, 500, 380, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15290381416441903, "compression_ratio": 1.6031746031746033, "no_speech_prob": 2.092410012616286e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 135742, "start": 1357.42, "end": 1364.0800000000002, "text": " They stress test this framework against actual, messy, physical reality.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 4244, 1500, 341, 8388, 1970, 3539, 11, 16191, 11, 4001, 4103, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 135742, "start": 1364.68, "end": 1369.46, "text": " And that takes us into the most fascinating part of the essay, the four arenas of breakdown.", "tokens": [50728, 400, 300, 2516, 505, 666, 264, 881, 10343, 644, 295, 264, 16238, 11, 264, 1451, 3212, 296, 295, 18188, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 135742, "start": 1369.88, "end": 1374.48, "text": " This is where Fliction demonstrates the universal applicability of the crossover theorem.", "tokens": [50988, 639, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 31034, 264, 11455, 2580, 2310, 295, 264, 33837, 20904, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 135742, "start": 1375.0600000000002, "end": 1380.68, "text": " The author selects four distinct real-world arenas and uses each one to isolate and illustrate", "tokens": [51247, 440, 3793, 3048, 82, 1451, 10644, 957, 12, 13217, 3212, 296, 293, 4960, 1184, 472, 281, 25660, 293, 23221, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 135742, "start": 1380.68, "end": 1383.1000000000001, "text": " the dominance of a single mathematical parameter.", "tokens": [51528, 264, 34987, 295, 257, 2167, 18894, 13075, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 135742, "start": 1383.4, "end": 1384.38, "text": " Okay, let's go through them.", "tokens": [51664, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 352, 807, 552, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168708840596309, "compression_ratio": 1.6007462686567164, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039045632089e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 138438, "start": 1384.38, "end": 1389.1000000000001, "text": " The first arena is biological homeostasis, which serves to illustrate the sheer power", "tokens": [50365, 440, 700, 18451, 307, 13910, 1280, 555, 26632, 11, 597, 13451, 281, 23221, 264, 23061, 1347, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 138438, "start": 1389.1000000000001, "end": 1390.1200000000001, "text": " of the Delta regime.", "tokens": [50601, 295, 264, 18183, 13120, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 138438, "start": 1390.1200000000001, "end": 1393.3400000000001, "text": " The biological examples in the text are visceral, I have to say.", "tokens": [50652, 440, 13910, 5110, 294, 264, 2487, 366, 1452, 47879, 11, 286, 362, 281, 584, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 138438, "start": 1393.7600000000002, "end": 1398.1000000000001, "text": " The author talks about an untreated infection in the bloodstream, an unmanaged vascular condition,", "tokens": [50834, 440, 3793, 6686, 466, 364, 1701, 26559, 11764, 294, 264, 3390, 9291, 11, 364, 517, 1601, 2980, 371, 22084, 4188, 11, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 138438, "start": 1398.2800000000002, "end": 1400.18, "text": " or a severe metabolic imbalance.", "tokens": [51060, 420, 257, 8922, 36464, 43007, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 138438, "start": 1400.42, "end": 1405.1200000000001, "text": " In a biological system, you're dealing with an environment where deviation almost always", "tokens": [51167, 682, 257, 13910, 1185, 11, 291, 434, 6260, 365, 364, 2823, 689, 25163, 1920, 1009, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1306275388468867, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.507135562184292e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 140512, "start": 1405.12, "end": 1407.34, "text": " has active endogenous amplification.", "tokens": [50365, 575, 4967, 917, 45519, 9731, 3774, 13, 50476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 140512, "start": 1408.1799999999998, "end": 1412.06, "text": " An untreated bacterial infection doesn't just sit statically in the tissue.", "tokens": [50518, 1107, 1701, 26559, 35632, 11764, 1177, 380, 445, 1394, 2219, 984, 294, 264, 12404, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 140512, "start": 1412.06, "end": 1413.1999999999998, "text": " It's not a paper pile.", "tokens": [50712, 467, 311, 406, 257, 3035, 14375, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 140512, "start": 1413.3799999999999, "end": 1413.9799999999998, "text": " Far from it.", "tokens": [50778, 9067, 490, 309, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 140512, "start": 1414.3999999999999, "end": 1419.4799999999998, "text": " The pathological process physically alters the very conditions of the body, raising temperature,", "tokens": [50829, 440, 3100, 4383, 1399, 9762, 419, 1559, 264, 588, 4487, 295, 264, 1772, 11, 11225, 4292, 11, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 140512, "start": 1419.9199999999998, "end": 1424.78, "text": " destroying local immune cells, altering pH, which in turn allows the bacteria to multiply", "tokens": [51105, 19926, 2654, 11992, 5438, 11, 11337, 278, 21677, 11, 597, 294, 1261, 4045, 264, 11763, 281, 12972, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 140512, "start": 1424.78, "end": 1425.62, "text": " even faster.", "tokens": [51348, 754, 4663, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 140512, "start": 1426.02, "end": 1428.78, "text": " The damage creates the environment for faster damage.", "tokens": [51410, 440, 4344, 7829, 264, 2823, 337, 4663, 4344, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997421893876852, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006080989233178e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 142878, "start": 1428.78, "end": 1432.8799999999999, "text": " So biological homeostasis is fundamentally a high Delta environment.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 13910, 1280, 555, 26632, 307, 17879, 257, 1090, 18183, 2823, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 142878, "start": 1433.06, "end": 1433.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50579, 7587, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 142878, "start": 1433.82, "end": 1438.22, "text": " And the relevant theoretical point the author makes here is not just the basic fact that", "tokens": [50617, 400, 264, 7340, 20864, 935, 264, 3793, 1669, 510, 307, 406, 445, 264, 3875, 1186, 300, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 142878, "start": 1438.22, "end": 1443.7, "text": " infections are dangerous, but that biological systems perfectly illustrate the lethal danger", "tokens": [50837, 19478, 366, 5795, 11, 457, 300, 13910, 3652, 6239, 23221, 264, 34562, 4330, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 142878, "start": 1443.7, "end": 1445.5, "text": " of the static view we just discussed.", "tokens": [51111, 295, 264, 13437, 1910, 321, 445, 7152, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 142878, "start": 1445.68, "end": 1445.82, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51210, 1779, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450992128742275, "compression_ratio": 1.5353535353535352, "no_speech_prob": 1.85018168320783e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 144582, "start": 1445.82, "end": 1451.1, "text": " A slow-growing chronic condition might initially seem to give a patient a long time to seek", "tokens": [50365, 316, 2964, 12, 861, 9637, 14493, 4188, 1062, 9105, 1643, 281, 976, 257, 4537, 257, 938, 565, 281, 8075, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 144582, "start": 1451.1, "end": 1451.48, "text": " treatment.", "tokens": [50629, 5032, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 144582, "start": 1451.6399999999999, "end": 1457.24, "text": " It presents a very large nominal T1, but because it's a biological process with an active Delta,", "tokens": [50656, 467, 13533, 257, 588, 2416, 41641, 314, 16, 11, 457, 570, 309, 311, 257, 13910, 1399, 365, 364, 4967, 18183, 11, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 144582, "start": 1457.62, "end": 1462.78, "text": " it's exactly the class of conditions most vulnerable to sudden, seemingly inexplicable", "tokens": [50955, 309, 311, 2293, 264, 1508, 295, 4487, 881, 10955, 281, 3990, 11, 18709, 29961, 4770, 712, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 144582, "start": 1462.78, "end": 1463.32, "text": " collapse.", "tokens": [51213, 15584, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 144582, "start": 1463.3799999999999, "end": 1467.26, "text": " Because that generous threshold collapses rapidly under the compounding reality.", "tokens": [51243, 1436, 300, 14537, 14678, 48765, 12910, 833, 264, 14154, 278, 4103, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 144582, "start": 1467.6, "end": 1468.08, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51454, 7587, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 144582, "start": 1468.32, "end": 1472.3999999999999, "text": " Tricking the patient who thought they had plenty of time based on their static diagnosis.", "tokens": [51490, 1765, 10401, 264, 4537, 567, 1194, 436, 632, 7140, 295, 565, 2361, 322, 641, 13437, 15217, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 144582, "start": 1472.84, "end": 1474.5, "text": " The math comes for the human body.", "tokens": [51716, 440, 5221, 1487, 337, 264, 1952, 1772, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14792778912712545, "compression_ratio": 1.6222222222222222, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354565693185943e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 147450, "start": 1474.5, "end": 1477.36, "text": " Okay, moving to the second arena.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 2684, 281, 264, 1150, 18451, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 147450, "start": 1478.28, "end": 1479.06, "text": " Software maintenance.", "tokens": [50554, 27428, 11258, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 147450, "start": 1479.94, "end": 1484.34, "text": " The text states that software perfectly illustrates the existence condition from question one.", "tokens": [50637, 440, 2487, 4368, 300, 4722, 6239, 41718, 264, 9123, 4188, 490, 1168, 472, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 147450, "start": 1485.06, "end": 1489.58, "text": " And this is where the essay provides an incredible defense for an industry that is constantly", "tokens": [50893, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 16238, 6417, 364, 4651, 7654, 337, 364, 3518, 300, 307, 6460, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 147450, "start": 1489.58, "end": 1490.8, "text": " accused of laziness.", "tokens": [51119, 17085, 295, 19320, 1324, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 147450, "start": 1490.96, "end": 1492.7, "text": " Yeah, developers will love this section.", "tokens": [51188, 865, 11, 8849, 486, 959, 341, 3541, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 147450, "start": 1493.04, "end": 1497.66, "text": " The author talks about the common reality of a dormant, non-propagating software defect.", "tokens": [51292, 440, 3793, 6686, 466, 264, 2689, 4103, 295, 257, 12521, 394, 11, 2107, 12, 79, 1513, 559, 990, 4722, 16445, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 147450, "start": 1498.42, "end": 1499.26, "text": " A simple bug.", "tokens": [51561, 316, 2199, 7426, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 147450, "start": 1499.46, "end": 1499.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51613, 1779, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 147450, "start": 1499.74, "end": 1504.4, "text": " For a strictly dormant bug, like a UI glitch or a minor logging error,", "tokens": [51627, 1171, 257, 20792, 12521, 394, 7426, 11, 411, 257, 15682, 23552, 420, 257, 6696, 27991, 6713, 11, 51860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17507482576770944, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686473166757643e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 150450, "start": 1504.5, "end": 1507.66, "text": " the compounding rate, Delta, is essentially zero.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 11, 18183, 11, 307, 4476, 4018, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 150450, "start": 1508.16, "end": 1511.28, "text": " It does not actively worsen our spread while left unaddressed.", "tokens": [50548, 467, 775, 406, 13022, 469, 6748, 527, 3974, 1339, 1411, 517, 25224, 3805, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 150450, "start": 1511.76, "end": 1516.74, "text": " But to understand the deferral dynamic, we have to look at the overheads in modern software", "tokens": [50728, 583, 281, 1223, 264, 25704, 2155, 8546, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 19922, 82, 294, 4363, 4722, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 150450, "start": 1516.74, "end": 1517.24, "text": " engineering.", "tokens": [50977, 7043, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 150450, "start": 1517.76, "end": 1520.92, "text": " The standard cost of maintenance, Kappa M, is incredibly high.", "tokens": [51028, 440, 3832, 2063, 295, 11258, 11, 591, 25637, 376, 11, 307, 6252, 1090, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 150450, "start": 1521.06, "end": 1521.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51193, 1779, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17935373908595034, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.894339286129254e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 152126, "start": 1521.26, "end": 1524.64, "text": " Maintaining the capacity to fix code continuously is exhausting.", "tokens": [50365, 376, 5114, 3686, 264, 6042, 281, 3191, 3089, 15684, 307, 34076, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051121496818435, "compression_ratio": 1.5022831050228311, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298406851564251e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 152126, "start": 1524.86, "end": 1530.1, "text": " You have continuous integration pipelines, automated testing servers that run 247, scheduled", "tokens": [50545, 509, 362, 10957, 10980, 40168, 11, 18473, 4997, 15909, 300, 1190, 4022, 22, 11, 15678, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051121496818435, "compression_ratio": 1.5022831050228311, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298406851564251e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 152126, "start": 1530.1, "end": 1533.86, "text": " mandatory code reviews, standing monitoring systems like Datadog.", "tokens": [50807, 22173, 3089, 10229, 11, 4877, 11028, 3652, 411, 9315, 345, 664, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051121496818435, "compression_ratio": 1.5022831050228311, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298406851564251e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 152126, "start": 1533.92, "end": 1534.8, "text": " It's a huge operation.", "tokens": [50998, 467, 311, 257, 2603, 6916, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051121496818435, "compression_ratio": 1.5022831050228311, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298406851564251e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 152126, "start": 1534.92, "end": 1539.68, "text": " And the engineering organization pays for all of that constantly, unconditionally.", "tokens": [51048, 400, 264, 7043, 4475, 10604, 337, 439, 295, 300, 6460, 11, 34959, 15899, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051121496818435, "compression_ratio": 1.5022831050228311, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298406851564251e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 153968, "start": 1539.68, "end": 1543.88, "text": " But the cost of initiating a repair event, Kappa R, is comparatively trivial.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 2063, 295, 6265, 990, 257, 10535, 2280, 11, 591, 25637, 497, 11, 307, 6311, 19020, 26703, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408831669734074, "compression_ratio": 1.463855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279228821028616e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 153968, "start": 1544.68, "end": 1549.54, "text": " In many systems, initiating a fix is as simple as opening a JIRA ticket or pushing a quick", "tokens": [50615, 682, 867, 3652, 11, 6265, 990, 257, 3191, 307, 382, 2199, 382, 5193, 257, 50172, 3750, 10550, 420, 7380, 257, 1702, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408831669734074, "compression_ratio": 1.463855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279228821028616e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 153968, "start": 1549.54, "end": 1551.2, "text": " hot fix to a staging environment.", "tokens": [50858, 2368, 3191, 281, 257, 41085, 2823, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408831669734074, "compression_ratio": 1.463855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279228821028616e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 153968, "start": 1551.5, "end": 1553.96, "text": " It's organizationally cheap to initiate.", "tokens": [50956, 467, 311, 4475, 379, 7084, 281, 31574, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408831669734074, "compression_ratio": 1.463855421686747, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279228821028616e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 155396, "start": 1553.96, "end": 1558.1200000000001, "text": " So we have a scenario where Kappa R is significantly less than Kappa M.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 321, 362, 257, 9005, 689, 591, 25637, 497, 307, 10591, 1570, 813, 591, 25637, 376, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 155396, "start": 1559.28, "end": 1563.88, "text": " And as we learned from the immediate threshold in question one, when the initiation overhead", "tokens": [50631, 400, 382, 321, 3264, 490, 264, 11629, 14678, 294, 1168, 472, 11, 562, 264, 43569, 19922, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 155396, "start": 1563.88, "end": 1569.08, "text": " is cheaper than the standing overhead, a genuine deferral window exists unconditionally.", "tokens": [50861, 307, 12284, 813, 264, 4877, 19922, 11, 257, 16699, 25704, 2155, 4910, 8198, 34959, 15899, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 155396, "start": 1569.74, "end": 1575.1200000000001, "text": " The math proves that in a low Delta software environment, batching fixes is not just an excuse.", "tokens": [51154, 440, 5221, 25019, 300, 294, 257, 2295, 18183, 4722, 2823, 11, 15245, 278, 32539, 307, 406, 445, 364, 8960, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 155396, "start": 1575.3600000000001, "end": 1577.2, "text": " It's the economically correct choice.", "tokens": [51435, 467, 311, 264, 26811, 3006, 3922, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 155396, "start": 1577.54, "end": 1577.66, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51544, 3153, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14180630186329718, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.56740679463363e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 157766, "start": 1577.66, "end": 1583.98, "text": " The standing overhead required to maintain continuous real-time bug eradication would vastly outweigh", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4877, 19922, 4739, 281, 6909, 10957, 957, 12, 3766, 7426, 33078, 8758, 576, 41426, 484, 826, 910, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 157766, "start": 1583.98, "end": 1588.28, "text": " the cost of simply letting the dormant bugs sit there and fixing them in a discontinuous", "tokens": [50681, 264, 2063, 295, 2935, 8295, 264, 12521, 394, 15120, 1394, 456, 293, 19442, 552, 294, 257, 31420, 12549, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 157766, "start": 1588.28, "end": 1589.0, "text": " sprint later.", "tokens": [50896, 25075, 1780, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 157766, "start": 1589.3000000000002, "end": 1591.5800000000002, "text": " We'll fix it later is mathematically optimal.", "tokens": [50947, 492, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 307, 44003, 16252, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 157766, "start": 1591.72, "end": 1592.18, "text": " I love that.", "tokens": [51068, 286, 959, 300, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 157766, "start": 1592.28, "end": 1592.5400000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51096, 1079, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 157766, "start": 1592.78, "end": 1596.26, "text": " But the text immediately follows that with a massive critical caveat.", "tokens": [51121, 583, 264, 2487, 4258, 10002, 300, 365, 257, 5994, 4924, 43012, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 157766, "start": 1596.44, "end": 1597.48, "text": " Ah, there's always a catch.", "tokens": [51304, 2438, 11, 456, 311, 1009, 257, 3745, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 157766, "start": 1597.8400000000001, "end": 1602.8400000000001, "text": " That entire mathematical justification relies entirely on the assumption that Delta is actually", "tokens": [51374, 663, 2302, 18894, 31591, 30910, 7696, 322, 264, 15302, 300, 18183, 307, 767, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 157766, "start": 1602.8400000000001, "end": 1603.22, "text": " zero.", "tokens": [51624, 4018, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136981414245055, "compression_ratio": 1.6595744680851063, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691671695338473e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 160322, "start": 1603.22, "end": 1609.82, "text": " If the engineering team misjudges Delta, the entire logic of deferral instantly collapses.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 7043, 1469, 3346, 9218, 2880, 18183, 11, 264, 2302, 9952, 295, 25704, 2155, 13518, 48765, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 160322, "start": 1610.74, "end": 1613.44, "text": " The text mentions the concept of a blast radius.", "tokens": [50741, 440, 2487, 23844, 264, 3410, 295, 257, 12035, 15845, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 160322, "start": 1614.04, "end": 1616.64, "text": " Let's use a real historical example to ground this.", "tokens": [50906, 961, 311, 764, 257, 957, 8584, 1365, 281, 2727, 341, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 160322, "start": 1617.52, "end": 1620.34, "text": " Think about something like the heart bleed bug from a decade ago.", "tokens": [51080, 6557, 466, 746, 411, 264, 1917, 28385, 7426, 490, 257, 10378, 2057, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 160322, "start": 1620.42, "end": 1621.7, "text": " That's a perfect example.", "tokens": [51225, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 1365, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 160322, "start": 1621.9, "end": 1626.56, "text": " For a long time, it might have looked like a dormant piece of inefficient code, a low priority.", "tokens": [51299, 1171, 257, 938, 565, 11, 309, 1062, 362, 2956, 411, 257, 12521, 394, 2522, 295, 43495, 3089, 11, 257, 2295, 9365, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17237028162530127, "compression_ratio": 1.546938775510204, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735413189457703e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 162656, "start": 1626.56, "end": 1631.6799999999998, "text": " But the moment a vulnerability like that is discovered and exploited by malicious actors,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 1623, 257, 24210, 411, 300, 307, 6941, 293, 40918, 538, 33496, 10037, 11, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 162656, "start": 1631.94, "end": 1633.82, "text": " it has a massive blast radius.", "tokens": [50634, 309, 575, 257, 5994, 12035, 15845, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 162656, "start": 1634.32, "end": 1639.62, "text": " It starts silently corrupting data, leaking passwords, compromising downstream systems.", "tokens": [50753, 467, 3719, 40087, 17366, 278, 1412, 11, 32856, 33149, 11, 11482, 3436, 30621, 3652, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 162656, "start": 1639.72, "end": 1641.56, "text": " Suddenly, Delta is no longer zero.", "tokens": [51023, 21194, 11, 18183, 307, 572, 2854, 4018, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 162656, "start": 1641.8, "end": 1642.6799999999998, "text": " It's astronomical.", "tokens": [51127, 467, 311, 49035, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 162656, "start": 1643.04, "end": 1646.3799999999999, "text": " And this is the brilliant reframing the author offers for software management.", "tokens": [51189, 400, 341, 307, 264, 10248, 1895, 2356, 278, 264, 3793, 7736, 337, 4722, 4592, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16822153482681665, "compression_ratio": 1.4761904761904763, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794578102010237e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 164638, "start": 1646.38, "end": 1651.94, "text": " The caution here is that when a developer says, we'll fix it later, they think they're making", "tokens": [50365, 440, 23585, 510, 307, 300, 562, 257, 10754, 1619, 11, 321, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 11, 436, 519, 436, 434, 1455, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 164638, "start": 1651.94, "end": 1653.98, "text": " a claim about severity or priority.", "tokens": [50643, 257, 3932, 466, 35179, 420, 9365, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 164638, "start": 1654.5600000000002, "end": 1659.14, "text": " But structurally, they are actually making a hidden mathematical claim about the Delta", "tokens": [50774, 583, 6594, 6512, 11, 436, 366, 767, 1455, 257, 7633, 18894, 3932, 466, 264, 18183, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 164638, "start": 1659.14, "end": 1659.72, "text": " parameter.", "tokens": [51003, 13075, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 164638, "start": 1660.1200000000001, "end": 1665.94, "text": " If you apply the deferral rules of a dormant zero Delta bug to an active compounding vulnerability", "tokens": [51052, 759, 291, 3079, 264, 25704, 2155, 4474, 295, 257, 12521, 394, 4018, 18183, 7426, 281, 364, 4967, 14154, 278, 24210, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 164638, "start": 1665.94, "end": 1669.2600000000002, "text": " with a blast radius, your system will be destroyed.", "tokens": [51343, 365, 257, 12035, 15845, 11, 428, 1185, 486, 312, 8937, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 164638, "start": 1669.92, "end": 1671.6000000000001, "text": " You aren't arguing about priority.", "tokens": [51542, 509, 3212, 380, 19697, 466, 9365, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 164638, "start": 1671.96, "end": 1673.9, "text": " You're arguing about whether the bug is breeding.", "tokens": [51644, 509, 434, 19697, 466, 1968, 264, 7426, 307, 26051, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1592488331837697, "compression_ratio": 1.6714801444043321, "no_speech_prob": 2.193153211121901e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 167390, "start": 1673.9, "end": 1677.48, "text": " That reframing alone is worth the price of admission.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 1895, 2356, 278, 3312, 307, 3163, 264, 3218, 295, 24668, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 167390, "start": 1678.5800000000002, "end": 1683.0600000000002, "text": " Let's move to the third arena, where things get very heavy, literally, physical infrastructure.", "tokens": [50599, 961, 311, 1286, 281, 264, 2636, 18451, 11, 689, 721, 483, 588, 4676, 11, 3736, 11, 4001, 6896, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 167390, "start": 1683.64, "end": 1686.24, "text": " Bridges, water systems, electrical grids.", "tokens": [50852, 30552, 2880, 11, 1281, 3652, 11, 12147, 677, 3742, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 167390, "start": 1686.94, "end": 1691.18, "text": " The text states that in infrastructure, the governing parameter that dictates everything", "tokens": [51017, 440, 2487, 4368, 300, 294, 6896, 11, 264, 30054, 13075, 300, 12569, 1024, 1203, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 167390, "start": 1691.18, "end": 1694.0800000000002, "text": " is P, the convexity of correction cost.", "tokens": [51229, 307, 430, 11, 264, 42432, 507, 295, 19984, 2063, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 167390, "start": 1694.76, "end": 1699.6000000000001, "text": " To understand how POP dominates physical infrastructure, we have to look at the nature of physical materials", "tokens": [51408, 1407, 1223, 577, 430, 12059, 8859, 1024, 4001, 6896, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 3687, 295, 4001, 5319, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 167390, "start": 1699.6000000000001, "end": 1700.52, "text": " and urban integration.", "tokens": [51650, 293, 9681, 10980, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 167390, "start": 1701.14, "end": 1703.0400000000002, "text": " Let's take a failing highway bridge.", "tokens": [51727, 961, 311, 747, 257, 18223, 17205, 7283, 13, 51822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 167390, "start": 1703.0400000000002, "end": 1703.2800000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51822, 1033, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19750505335190716, "compression_ratio": 1.71875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841736780540904e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 170328, "start": 1703.28, "end": 1707.96, "text": " Replacing a handful of minor, slowly rusting rivets is a linear cost.", "tokens": [50365, 47762, 5615, 257, 16458, 295, 6696, 11, 5692, 367, 11712, 28745, 1385, 307, 257, 8213, 2063, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 170328, "start": 1708.1, "end": 1709.1399999999999, "text": " It's relatively cheap.", "tokens": [50606, 467, 311, 7226, 7084, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 170328, "start": 1709.6, "end": 1714.6399999999999, "text": " But if you defer that maintenance until the structural integrity deteriorates past a critical", "tokens": [50681, 583, 498, 291, 25704, 300, 11258, 1826, 264, 15067, 16000, 26431, 1024, 1791, 257, 4924, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 170328, "start": 1714.6399999999999, "end": 1717.98, "text": " threshold, you can no longer just replace the bad steel.", "tokens": [50933, 14678, 11, 291, 393, 572, 2854, 445, 7406, 264, 1578, 8269, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 170328, "start": 1718.08, "end": 1718.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51105, 1779, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 170328, "start": 1718.3999999999999, "end": 1722.06, "text": " Because physics doesn't let you swap out the foundation while cars are driving on it.", "tokens": [51121, 1436, 10649, 1177, 380, 718, 291, 18135, 484, 264, 7030, 1339, 5163, 366, 4840, 322, 309, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 170328, "start": 1722.2, "end": 1724.62, "text": " You have to tear down and replace the entire bridge.", "tokens": [51311, 509, 362, 281, 12556, 760, 293, 7406, 264, 2302, 7283, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 170328, "start": 1725.0, "end": 1729.62, "text": " And the cost of that total replacement is not just the linear cost of more steel.", "tokens": [51451, 400, 264, 2063, 295, 300, 3217, 14419, 307, 406, 445, 264, 8213, 2063, 295, 544, 8269, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12506695797568873, "compression_ratio": 1.6526315789473685, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303720104718142e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 172962, "start": 1729.62, "end": 1732.1799999999998, "text": " The cost explodes exponentially.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2063, 42610, 37330, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25887171427408856, "compression_ratio": 1.05, "no_speech_prob": 1.80027358038376e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 172962, "start": 1732.1799999999998, "end": 1735.26, "text": " You have staggering environmental review processes.", "tokens": [50493, 509, 362, 42974, 8303, 3131, 7555, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25887171427408856, "compression_ratio": 1.05, "no_speech_prob": 1.80027358038376e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 173526, "start": 1735.26, "end": 1739.08, "text": " You have massive service disruptions that halt local commerce.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 5994, 2643, 14124, 626, 300, 12479, 2654, 26320, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22915283838907877, "compression_ratio": 0.96875, "no_speech_prob": 2.028039845433649e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 173908, "start": 1739.08, "end": 1744.04, "text": " You have emergency financing costs, political battles, total redesigns.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 7473, 22286, 5497, 11, 3905, 14648, 11, 3217, 39853, 82, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14941158481672698, "compression_ratio": 1.4078947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.821494777926036e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 173908, "start": 1744.04, "end": 1748.9199999999998, "text": " That explosion of secondary and tertiary costs is what strongly convex repair costs looks like", "tokens": [50613, 663, 15673, 295, 11396, 293, 38726, 29104, 5497, 307, 437, 10613, 42432, 10535, 5497, 1542, 411, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14941158481672698, "compression_ratio": 1.4078947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.821494777926036e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 173908, "start": 1748.9199999999998, "end": 1749.54, "text": " in the real world.", "tokens": [50857, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14941158481672698, "compression_ratio": 1.4078947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.821494777926036e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 173908, "start": 1749.6399999999999, "end": 1751.08, "text": " That's a massive P variable.", "tokens": [50893, 663, 311, 257, 5994, 430, 7006, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14941158481672698, "compression_ratio": 1.4078947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.821494777926036e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 175108, "start": 1751.08, "end": 1757.1599999999999, "text": " And the mathematical equations in the crossover theorem show exactly what happens when P is overwhelmingly large.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 18894, 11787, 294, 264, 33837, 20904, 855, 2293, 437, 2314, 562, 430, 307, 42926, 2416, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1432699983770197, "compression_ratio": 1.3818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 2.1757626082752335e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 175108, "start": 1757.6999999999998, "end": 1762.9399999999998, "text": " A massive P ruthlessly compresses the deferral timeline, your T1, down toward a value of 1.", "tokens": [50696, 316, 5994, 430, 38225, 12048, 14778, 279, 264, 25704, 2155, 12933, 11, 428, 314, 16, 11, 760, 7361, 257, 2158, 295, 502, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1432699983770197, "compression_ratio": 1.3818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 2.1757626082752335e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 175108, "start": 1763.02, "end": 1763.74, "text": " It shrinks the window.", "tokens": [50962, 467, 9884, 16431, 264, 4910, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1432699983770197, "compression_ratio": 1.3818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 2.1757626082752335e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 176374, "start": 1763.74, "end": 1770.1, "text": " A strongly convex repair cost punishes accumulated deviation almost immediately, regardless of", "tokens": [50365, 316, 10613, 42432, 10535, 2063, 9842, 279, 31346, 25163, 1920, 4258, 11, 10060, 295, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 176374, "start": 1770.1, "end": 1772.2, "text": " how slow the delta compounding actually is.", "tokens": [50683, 577, 2964, 264, 8289, 14154, 278, 767, 307, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 176374, "start": 1772.58, "end": 1776.54, "text": " So even if the rust on the bridge is growing incredibly slowly, a very low delta, because", "tokens": [50807, 407, 754, 498, 264, 15259, 322, 264, 7283, 307, 4194, 6252, 5692, 11, 257, 588, 2295, 8289, 11, 570, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 176374, "start": 1776.54, "end": 1781.58, "text": " the ultimate cost of a bridge collapse is astronomically exponential, a high P, you simply do not have", "tokens": [51005, 264, 9705, 2063, 295, 257, 7283, 15584, 307, 26302, 984, 21510, 11, 257, 1090, 430, 11, 291, 2935, 360, 406, 362, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 176374, "start": 1781.58, "end": 1782.92, "text": " the luxury of a deferral window.", "tokens": [51257, 264, 15558, 295, 257, 25704, 2155, 4910, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 176374, "start": 1783.38, "end": 1784.6, "text": " The math forces your hand.", "tokens": [51347, 440, 5221, 5874, 428, 1011, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 176374, "start": 1784.94, "end": 1786.72, "text": " You have to inspect and maintain continuously.", "tokens": [51425, 509, 362, 281, 15018, 293, 6909, 15684, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 176374, "start": 1787.2, "end": 1789.74, "text": " You must choose M sub T over rho sub T.", "tokens": [51538, 509, 1633, 2826, 376, 1422, 314, 670, 20293, 1422, 314, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14336465534410978, "compression_ratio": 1.614864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 2.032505240501248e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 178974, "start": 1789.74, "end": 1790.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 178974, "start": 1791.0, "end": 1795.1200000000001, "text": " Modern infrastructure maintenance schedules, with their mandated continuous inspections,", "tokens": [50428, 19814, 6896, 11258, 28078, 11, 365, 641, 47563, 10957, 46544, 11, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 178974, "start": 1795.48, "end": 1800.8, "text": " are essentially a vast institutional recognition of the dominance of the P parameter.", "tokens": [50652, 366, 4476, 257, 8369, 18391, 11150, 295, 264, 34987, 295, 264, 430, 13075, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 178974, "start": 1801.04, "end": 1805.44, "text": " Which brings us to the fourth and final arena, the grand finale of the real world applications.", "tokens": [50930, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 6409, 293, 2572, 18451, 11, 264, 2697, 23510, 295, 264, 957, 1002, 5821, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 178974, "start": 1806.5, "end": 1807.76, "text": " Fiscal reachability.", "tokens": [51203, 479, 14616, 2524, 2310, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 178974, "start": 1807.96, "end": 1809.52, "text": " This one is intense.", "tokens": [51276, 639, 472, 307, 9447, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 178974, "start": 1809.72, "end": 1812.6, "text": " The text looks at national economies and sovereign budgets.", "tokens": [51364, 440, 2487, 1542, 412, 4048, 23158, 293, 28756, 26708, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 178974, "start": 1813.06, "end": 1815.44, "text": " And the author calls this the master interaction.", "tokens": [51531, 400, 264, 3793, 5498, 341, 264, 4505, 9285, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21687528138519616, "compression_ratio": 1.6264150943396227, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056377569687255e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 181544, "start": 1815.44, "end": 1820.74, "text": " Because unlike the previous three examples where one parameter dominates, in a sovereign", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 8343, 264, 3894, 1045, 5110, 689, 472, 13075, 8859, 1024, 11, 294, 257, 28756, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 181544, "start": 1820.74, "end": 1825.8, "text": " economy, all four variables are playing out simultaneously at a massive scale.", "tokens": [50630, 5010, 11, 439, 1451, 9102, 366, 2433, 484, 16561, 412, 257, 5994, 4373, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 181544, "start": 1826.24, "end": 1830.98, "text": " This is where the framework proves its ultimate utility, because a macroeconomy forces you to", "tokens": [50905, 639, 307, 689, 264, 8388, 25019, 1080, 9705, 14877, 11, 570, 257, 18887, 68, 2291, 88, 5874, 291, 281, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 181544, "start": 1830.98, "end": 1833.8600000000001, "text": " balance every single mathematical force we've discussed.", "tokens": [51142, 4772, 633, 2167, 18894, 3464, 321, 600, 7152, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 181544, "start": 1834.3400000000001, "end": 1835.3200000000002, "text": " Let's map the variables.", "tokens": [51310, 961, 311, 4471, 264, 9102, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 181544, "start": 1835.9, "end": 1840.72, "text": " In a national economy, the standing maintenance overhead, kappa M, is represented by the massive", "tokens": [51388, 682, 257, 4048, 5010, 11, 264, 4877, 11258, 19922, 11, 350, 25637, 376, 11, 307, 10379, 538, 264, 5994, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 181544, "start": 1840.72, "end": 1842.0, "text": " continuous bureaucracy.", "tokens": [51629, 10957, 44671, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13713137938244507, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 2.0604806923174568e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 184200, "start": 1842.0, "end": 1846.5, "text": " The standing armies of tax auditors, the central bank monitoring systems, the endless reporting", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4877, 28217, 295, 3366, 2379, 9862, 11, 264, 5777, 3765, 11028, 3652, 11, 264, 16144, 10031, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 184200, "start": 1846.5, "end": 1851.7, "text": " requirements, the regulatory agencies, you pay for that massive bureaucracy unconditionally", "tokens": [50590, 7728, 11, 264, 18260, 9504, 11, 291, 1689, 337, 300, 5994, 44671, 34959, 15899, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 184200, "start": 1851.7, "end": 1853.1, "text": " every single day.", "tokens": [50850, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 184200, "start": 1853.42, "end": 1853.68, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [50936, 12753, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 184200, "start": 1854.02, "end": 1856.3, "text": " And opposed to that, what is kappa R?", "tokens": [50966, 400, 8851, 281, 300, 11, 437, 307, 350, 25637, 497, 30, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 184200, "start": 1856.74, "end": 1863.46, "text": " It's the initiation cost of a discontinuous economic repair, a bailout, a massive stimulus", "tokens": [51102, 467, 311, 264, 43569, 2063, 295, 257, 31420, 12549, 4836, 10535, 11, 257, 19313, 346, 11, 257, 5994, 21366, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 184200, "start": 1863.46, "end": 1865.42, "text": " package, a central bank crisis facility.", "tokens": [51438, 7372, 11, 257, 5777, 3765, 5869, 8973, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 184200, "start": 1865.64, "end": 1870.54, "text": " And crucially, kappa R in a political system is incredibly prohibitively high.", "tokens": [51547, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 350, 25637, 497, 294, 257, 3905, 1185, 307, 6252, 16015, 2187, 356, 1090, 13, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13237169626596812, "compression_ratio": 1.6245614035087719, "no_speech_prob": 1.876098668779358e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 187054, "start": 1870.54, "end": 1872.32, "text": " Oh, massively high.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 29379, 1090, 13, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 187054, "start": 1872.46, "end": 1877.3999999999999, "text": " The political capital, the institutional friction, and the legislative warfare required to invoke", "tokens": [50461, 440, 3905, 4238, 11, 264, 18391, 17710, 11, 293, 264, 21331, 24490, 4739, 281, 41117, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 187054, "start": 1877.3999999999999, "end": 1880.36, "text": " crisis powers represent a massive shock overhead.", "tokens": [50708, 5869, 8674, 2906, 257, 5994, 5588, 19922, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 187054, "start": 1880.62, "end": 1885.1399999999999, "text": " So we have extremely high standing overhead and extremely high initiation overhead.", "tokens": [50869, 407, 321, 362, 4664, 1090, 4877, 19922, 293, 4664, 1090, 43569, 19922, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 187054, "start": 1885.58, "end": 1887.52, "text": " But then we introduce the other two forces.", "tokens": [51117, 583, 550, 321, 5366, 264, 661, 732, 5874, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 187054, "start": 1887.74, "end": 1892.92, "text": " We add our compounding delta, which in a sovereign economy is literal compound interest on national", "tokens": [51225, 492, 909, 527, 14154, 278, 8289, 11, 597, 294, 257, 28756, 5010, 307, 20411, 14154, 1179, 322, 4048, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 187054, "start": 1892.92, "end": 1898.06, "text": " debt, but also more dangerously, the compounding loss of institutional credibility in the bond markets.", "tokens": [51484, 7831, 11, 457, 611, 544, 4330, 5098, 11, 264, 14154, 278, 4470, 295, 18391, 28852, 294, 264, 6086, 8383, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1189028208072369, "compression_ratio": 1.7447552447552448, "no_speech_prob": 1.86833860015001e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 189806, "start": 1898.06, "end": 1903.34, "text": " And finally, we have the large P. The ultimate cost of correcting a full-blown sovereign debt", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 362, 264, 2416, 430, 13, 440, 9705, 2063, 295, 47032, 257, 1577, 12, 5199, 648, 28756, 7831, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 189806, "start": 1903.34, "end": 1909.82, "text": " default or a hyperinflationary spiral is strongly convex. It doesn't just cost money. It devastates", "tokens": [50629, 7576, 420, 257, 9848, 27850, 399, 822, 25165, 307, 10613, 42432, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 2063, 1460, 13, 467, 13959, 1024, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 189806, "start": 1909.82, "end": 1912.78, "text": " the societal fabric and destroys decades of wealth generation.", "tokens": [50953, 264, 33472, 7253, 293, 36714, 7878, 295, 7203, 5125, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 189806, "start": 1912.8799999999999, "end": 1913.6, "text": " Yeah, it's catastrophic.", "tokens": [51106, 865, 11, 309, 311, 34915, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 189806, "start": 1913.84, "end": 1918.6399999999999, "text": " So when you lock all four of these massive forces into the equations of the core theorem,", "tokens": [51154, 407, 562, 291, 4017, 439, 1451, 295, 613, 5994, 5874, 666, 264, 11787, 295, 264, 4965, 20904, 11, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 189806, "start": 1919.06, "end": 1925.1399999999999, "text": " the optimal deferral threshold, T star, becomes what the author terms a policy horizon.", "tokens": [51415, 264, 16252, 25704, 2155, 14678, 11, 314, 3543, 11, 3643, 437, 264, 3793, 2115, 257, 3897, 18046, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09353221228363318, "compression_ratio": 1.5612244897959184, "no_speech_prob": 2.1795664231771816e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 192514, "start": 1925.14, "end": 1931.96, "text": " A policy horizon. The exact mathematical point in time past which continuous painful stabilization", "tokens": [50365, 316, 3897, 18046, 13, 440, 1900, 18894, 935, 294, 565, 1791, 597, 10957, 11697, 35476, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 192514, "start": 1931.96, "end": 1937.66, "text": " isn't just the prudent thing to do. It is strictly unarguably cheaper than trying to execute a", "tokens": [50706, 1943, 380, 445, 264, 582, 24064, 551, 281, 360, 13, 467, 307, 20792, 517, 289, 2794, 1188, 12284, 813, 1382, 281, 14483, 257, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 192514, "start": 1937.66, "end": 1939.16, "text": " discontinuous bailout later.", "tokens": [50991, 31420, 12549, 19313, 346, 1780, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 192514, "start": 1939.5400000000002, "end": 1944.0600000000002, "text": " Exactly. And the author uses this fiscal arena to deliver their ultimate warning,", "tokens": [51085, 7587, 13, 400, 264, 3793, 4960, 341, 15897, 18451, 281, 4239, 641, 9705, 9164, 11, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 192514, "start": 1944.64, "end": 1947.18, "text": " circling all the way back to the danger of the static few.", "tokens": [51340, 3510, 1688, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 264, 4330, 295, 264, 13437, 1326, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 192514, "start": 1947.3200000000002, "end": 1949.9, "text": " Which is so critical to remember here.", "tokens": [51474, 3013, 307, 370, 4924, 281, 1604, 510, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629143965871711, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970852228878844e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 194990, "start": 1949.9, "end": 1954.5400000000002, "text": " Think about the 2008 financial crisis or the sovereign debt crises that followed in Europe.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 10389, 4669, 5869, 420, 264, 28756, 7831, 31403, 300, 6263, 294, 3315, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 194990, "start": 1955.1200000000001, "end": 1959.6000000000001, "text": " Fiscal systems possess immense institutional credibility. Because they are the sovereign,", "tokens": [50626, 479, 14616, 3652, 17490, 22920, 18391, 28852, 13, 1436, 436, 366, 264, 28756, 11, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 194990, "start": 1960.02, "end": 1964.8000000000002, "text": " they appear to have a nearly infinite nominal deferral tolerance. They look like they can run", "tokens": [50871, 436, 4204, 281, 362, 257, 6217, 13785, 41641, 25704, 2155, 23368, 13, 814, 574, 411, 436, 393, 1190, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 194990, "start": 1964.8000000000002, "end": 1968.0400000000002, "text": " structural deficits and defer painful structural reforms forever.", "tokens": [51110, 15067, 49616, 293, 25704, 11697, 15067, 24897, 5680, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 194990, "start": 1968.24, "end": 1970.3600000000001, "text": " Their T1 baseline looks like a century.", "tokens": [51282, 6710, 314, 16, 20518, 1542, 411, 257, 4901, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 194990, "start": 1970.7800000000002, "end": 1977.4, "text": " It does. But as the perturbation equation proved, systems with a massively large static baseline", "tokens": [51409, 467, 775, 13, 583, 382, 264, 40468, 399, 5367, 14617, 11, 3652, 365, 257, 29379, 2416, 13437, 20518, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09263317925589425, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.839637600239974e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 197740, "start": 1977.4, "end": 1983.26, "text": " are precisely the systems whose effective threshold erodes the fastest under a rising delta.", "tokens": [50365, 366, 13402, 264, 3652, 6104, 4942, 14678, 1189, 4789, 264, 14573, 833, 257, 11636, 8289, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 197740, "start": 1983.92, "end": 1989.5400000000002, "text": " The structural drift of mounting debt and eroding credibility silently destroys the illusion of", "tokens": [50691, 440, 15067, 19699, 295, 22986, 7831, 293, 1189, 8616, 28852, 40087, 36714, 264, 18854, 295, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 197740, "start": 1989.5400000000002, "end": 1990.0400000000002, "text": " stability.", "tokens": [50972, 11826, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 197740, "start": 1990.5600000000002, "end": 1995.9, "text": " The math comes for everyone, even empires. A sovereign nation thinks it has 50 years to fix its pension", "tokens": [51023, 440, 5221, 1487, 337, 1518, 11, 754, 4012, 3145, 13, 316, 28756, 4790, 7309, 309, 575, 2625, 924, 281, 3191, 1080, 21927, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 197740, "start": 1995.9, "end": 1999.5800000000002, "text": " prices, but the compounding rate means the window might actually close in five.", "tokens": [51290, 7901, 11, 457, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 1355, 264, 4910, 1062, 767, 1998, 294, 1732, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 197740, "start": 1999.7800000000002, "end": 2003.9, "text": " It's chilling to see the math applied at that scale. So we've dismantled our assumptions,", "tokens": [51484, 467, 311, 31047, 281, 536, 264, 5221, 6456, 412, 300, 4373, 13, 407, 321, 600, 30506, 1493, 527, 17695, 11, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09588783809116909, "compression_ratio": 1.61986301369863, "no_speech_prob": 2.593865443614729e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 200390, "start": 2003.9, "end": 2009.3000000000002, "text": " built a new theorem, and applied it to the physical world. What does this all mean for the broader", "tokens": [50365, 3094, 257, 777, 20904, 11, 293, 6456, 309, 281, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 708, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 264, 13227, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 200390, "start": 2009.3000000000002, "end": 2012.5600000000002, "text": " world of system theory? Because this essay doesn't exist in a vacuum.", "tokens": [50635, 1002, 295, 1185, 5261, 30, 1436, 341, 16238, 1177, 380, 2514, 294, 257, 14224, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 200390, "start": 2012.9, "end": 2014.6200000000001, "text": " No, it builds on existing work.", "tokens": [50815, 883, 11, 309, 15182, 322, 6741, 589, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 200390, "start": 2014.96, "end": 2020.5, "text": " This brings us to the fifth segment of our deep dive, redefining failure. As you mentioned earlier,", "tokens": [50918, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 9266, 9469, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 11, 38818, 1760, 7763, 13, 1018, 291, 2835, 3071, 11, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 200390, "start": 2020.6000000000001, "end": 2024.8000000000002, "text": " this 2026 essay by Fliction is actually a companion to an earlier work.", "tokens": [51200, 341, 945, 10880, 16238, 538, 3235, 4105, 307, 767, 257, 22363, 281, 364, 3071, 589, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 200390, "start": 2025.0800000000002, "end": 2031.2, "text": " Yes. The text explicitly contextualizes itself within a broader theoretical framework established", "tokens": [51424, 1079, 13, 440, 2487, 20803, 35526, 5660, 2564, 1951, 257, 13227, 20864, 8388, 7545, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10541151204240432, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 3.1292050114289927e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 203120, "start": 2031.2, "end": 2037.42, "text": " in an earlier paper called Recursive Continuation. To fully grasp Fliction's achievement, we have to", "tokens": [50365, 294, 364, 3071, 3035, 1219, 9647, 2156, 488, 14674, 16073, 13, 1407, 4498, 21743, 3235, 4105, 311, 15838, 11, 321, 362, 281, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078951228748669, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.694507490053454e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 203120, "start": 2037.42, "end": 2041.56, "text": " understand what that older paper solved, and more importantly, what it failed to solve.", "tokens": [50676, 1223, 437, 300, 4906, 3035, 13041, 11, 293, 544, 8906, 11, 437, 309, 7612, 281, 5039, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078951228748669, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.694507490053454e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 203120, "start": 2041.7, "end": 2047.2, "text": " Let's lay that groundwork. The older text, Recursive Continuation, established a concept called", "tokens": [50890, 961, 311, 2360, 300, 2727, 1902, 13, 440, 4906, 2487, 11, 9647, 2156, 488, 14674, 16073, 11, 7545, 257, 3410, 1219, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078951228748669, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.694507490053454e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 203120, "start": 2047.2, "end": 2054.26, "text": " Repair Capacity, or R-sub-T. It mathematically proved that for any system to survive over time,", "tokens": [51165, 3696, 1246, 8363, 19008, 11, 420, 497, 12, 30131, 12, 51, 13, 467, 44003, 14617, 300, 337, 604, 1185, 281, 7867, 670, 565, 11, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078951228748669, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.694507490053454e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 203120, "start": 2054.26, "end": 2060.76, "text": " its total available repair capacity must fundamentally keep pace with its cumulative maintenance burden.", "tokens": [51518, 1080, 3217, 2435, 10535, 6042, 1633, 17879, 1066, 11638, 365, 1080, 38379, 11258, 12578, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10078951228748669, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.694507490053454e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 206120, "start": 2061.2, "end": 2067.3599999999997, "text": " If burden exceeds capacity, the system dies. It was a vital contribution, but it had a massive blind", "tokens": [50365, 759, 12578, 43305, 6042, 11, 264, 1185, 2714, 13, 467, 390, 257, 11707, 13150, 11, 457, 309, 632, 257, 5994, 6865, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08996266833806442, "compression_ratio": 1.7412587412587412, "no_speech_prob": 2.916325817989285e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 206120, "start": 2067.3599999999997, "end": 2072.24, "text": " spot. A blind spot. Yeah. It proved that a system needs capacity to survive, but it couldn't", "tokens": [50673, 4008, 13, 316, 6865, 4008, 13, 865, 13, 467, 14617, 300, 257, 1185, 2203, 6042, 281, 7867, 11, 457, 309, 2809, 380, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08996266833806442, "compression_ratio": 1.7412587412587412, "no_speech_prob": 2.916325817989285e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 206120, "start": 2072.24, "end": 2077.2799999999997, "text": " mathematically answer how that capacity should be spent across time. It treated R-sub-T as one", "tokens": [50917, 44003, 1867, 577, 300, 6042, 820, 312, 4418, 2108, 565, 13, 467, 8668, 497, 12, 30131, 12, 51, 382, 472, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08996266833806442, "compression_ratio": 1.7412587412587412, "no_speech_prob": 2.916325817989285e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 206120, "start": 2077.2799999999997, "end": 2082.64, "text": " undifferentiated lump sum. It couldn't tell you whether a system should spend its capacity as a slow,", "tokens": [51169, 674, 15790, 72, 770, 25551, 2408, 13, 467, 2809, 380, 980, 291, 1968, 257, 1185, 820, 3496, 1080, 6042, 382, 257, 2964, 11, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08996266833806442, "compression_ratio": 1.7412587412587412, "no_speech_prob": 2.916325817989285e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 206120, "start": 2082.64, "end": 2088.2599999999998, "text": " continuous trickle of daily maintenance, or hoard it for massive, discontinuous shocks of emergency repair.", "tokens": [51437, 10957, 4282, 306, 295, 5212, 11258, 11, 420, 45940, 309, 337, 5994, 11, 31420, 12549, 37066, 295, 7473, 10535, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08996266833806442, "compression_ratio": 1.7412587412587412, "no_speech_prob": 2.916325817989285e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 208826, "start": 2088.26, "end": 2093.2400000000002, "text": " And because it couldn't differentiate the timing, it struggled to define failure accurately.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 309, 2809, 380, 23203, 264, 10822, 11, 309, 19023, 281, 6964, 7763, 20095, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13925481093557257, "compression_ratio": 1.6751054852320675, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 208826, "start": 2094.42, "end": 2100.1200000000003, "text": " The older text identified four distinct failure modes of repair. Under-repair, over-repair,", "tokens": [50673, 440, 4906, 2487, 9234, 1451, 10644, 7763, 14068, 295, 10535, 13, 6974, 12, 19919, 1246, 11, 670, 12, 19919, 1246, 11, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13925481093557257, "compression_ratio": 1.6751054852320675, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 208826, "start": 2100.6000000000004, "end": 2104.38, "text": " misrepair, and the one we care about today. Repair Delay.", "tokens": [50982, 3346, 19919, 1246, 11, 293, 264, 472, 321, 1127, 466, 965, 13, 3696, 1246, 5831, 320, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13925481093557257, "compression_ratio": 1.6751054852320675, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 208826, "start": 2104.5800000000004, "end": 2107.3, "text": " And how did that older text define repair delay?", "tokens": [51181, 400, 577, 630, 300, 4906, 2487, 6964, 10535, 8577, 30, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13925481093557257, "compression_ratio": 1.6751054852320675, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 208826, "start": 2107.6400000000003, "end": 2112.7400000000002, "text": " It defined it qualitatively. It basically said that repair delay is any interval between the detection of", "tokens": [51334, 467, 7642, 309, 31312, 356, 13, 467, 1936, 848, 300, 10535, 8577, 307, 604, 15035, 1296, 264, 17784, 295, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13925481093557257, "compression_ratio": 1.6751054852320675, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 211274, "start": 2112.74, "end": 2118.04, "text": " a fault and its correction that is long enough for the fault to compound. It essentially argued that", "tokens": [50365, 257, 7441, 293, 1080, 19984, 300, 307, 938, 1547, 337, 264, 7441, 281, 14154, 13, 467, 4476, 20219, 300, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927859789059486, "compression_ratio": 1.6294642857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678750394683028e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 211274, "start": 2118.04, "end": 2122.9599999999996, "text": " any delay that allows for compounding is a failure of the system. And that qualitative definition is", "tokens": [50630, 604, 8577, 300, 4045, 337, 14154, 278, 307, 257, 7763, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 400, 300, 31312, 7123, 307, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927859789059486, "compression_ratio": 1.6294642857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678750394683028e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 211274, "start": 2122.9599999999996, "end": 2129.02, "text": " exactly what Flickstein's new crossover theorem completely upends. The text argues forcefully that", "tokens": [50876, 2293, 437, 3235, 618, 9089, 311, 777, 33837, 20904, 2584, 493, 2581, 13, 440, 2487, 38218, 3464, 2277, 300, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927859789059486, "compression_ratio": 1.6294642857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678750394683028e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 211274, "start": 2129.02, "end": 2132.8199999999997, "text": " repair delay is not qualitatively bad by default. Which is huge.", "tokens": [51179, 10535, 8577, 307, 406, 31312, 356, 1578, 538, 7576, 13, 3013, 307, 2603, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927859789059486, "compression_ratio": 1.6294642857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678750394683028e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 213282, "start": 2132.82, "end": 2138.2400000000002, "text": " It really is. Delay is only a mathematical failure mode if it extends past that rigorously", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 5831, 320, 307, 787, 257, 18894, 7763, 4391, 498, 309, 26448, 1791, 300, 42191, 5098, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09585343236508577, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.3984226063533676e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 213282, "start": 2138.2400000000002, "end": 2143.94, "text": " computable threshold, T-star. If the delay is shorter than T-star, the text argues it isn't a failure", "tokens": [50636, 2807, 712, 14678, 11, 314, 12, 9710, 13, 759, 264, 8577, 307, 11639, 813, 314, 12, 9710, 11, 264, 2487, 38218, 309, 1943, 380, 257, 7763, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09585343236508577, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.3984226063533676e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 213282, "start": 2143.94, "end": 2149.88, "text": " at all. It's the economically correct exercise of the deferral window. It completely removes the moral", "tokens": [50921, 412, 439, 13, 467, 311, 264, 26811, 3006, 5380, 295, 264, 25704, 2155, 4910, 13, 467, 2584, 30445, 264, 9723, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09585343236508577, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.3984226063533676e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 213282, "start": 2149.88, "end": 2155.42, "text": " judgment from procrastination and replaces it with a strict geometric boundary. The author proves that", "tokens": [51218, 12216, 490, 39306, 2486, 293, 46734, 309, 365, 257, 10910, 33246, 12866, 13, 440, 3793, 25019, 300, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09585343236508577, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.3984226063533676e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 213282, "start": 2155.42, "end": 2161.7200000000003, "text": " delay is not intrinsically a defect of a recursive system. Up to a mathematically definable point,", "tokens": [51495, 8577, 307, 406, 28621, 984, 257, 16445, 295, 257, 20560, 488, 1185, 13, 5858, 281, 257, 44003, 1561, 712, 935, 11, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09585343236508577, "compression_ratio": 1.7079037800687284, "no_speech_prob": 2.3984226063533676e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 216172, "start": 2161.72, "end": 2168.4199999999996, "text": " hoarding capacity and allowing a problem to compound is actually the optimal survival strategy of a", "tokens": [50365, 45940, 278, 6042, 293, 8293, 257, 1154, 281, 14154, 307, 767, 264, 16252, 12559, 5206, 295, 257, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07864848386894152, "compression_ratio": 1.6102941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612951469873293e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 216172, "start": 2168.4199999999996, "end": 2173.9399999999996, "text": " rational system. Honestly, there's something deeply relieving about this framing. It means that when I", "tokens": [50700, 15090, 1185, 13, 12348, 11, 456, 311, 746, 8760, 21680, 798, 466, 341, 28971, 13, 467, 1355, 300, 562, 286, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07864848386894152, "compression_ratio": 1.6102941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612951469873293e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 216172, "start": 2173.9399999999996, "end": 2180.8599999999997, "text": " look at a lingering problem, whether it's a leaky faucet, a strained relationship, or a delayed project at", "tokens": [50976, 574, 412, 257, 49542, 1154, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 257, 476, 15681, 49567, 302, 11, 257, 2148, 2001, 2480, 11, 420, 257, 20268, 1716, 412, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07864848386894152, "compression_ratio": 1.6102941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612951469873293e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 216172, "start": 2180.8599999999997, "end": 2186.8599999999997, "text": " work, my decision to not fix it right this second isn't necessarily a failure of character.", "tokens": [51322, 589, 11, 452, 3537, 281, 406, 3191, 309, 558, 341, 1150, 1943, 380, 4725, 257, 7763, 295, 2517, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07864848386894152, "compression_ratio": 1.6102941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612951469873293e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 216172, "start": 2187.04, "end": 2188.54, "text": " Right. It's not you just being lazy.", "tokens": [51631, 1779, 13, 467, 311, 406, 291, 445, 885, 14847, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07864848386894152, "compression_ratio": 1.6102941176470589, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612951469873293e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 218854, "start": 2188.54, "end": 2193.94, "text": " It gives us mathematical permission to not fix everything immediately. It proves that systems", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2709, 505, 18894, 11226, 281, 406, 3191, 1203, 4258, 13, 467, 25019, 300, 3652, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05659312532659162, "compression_ratio": 1.6993006993006994, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776620682263597e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 218854, "start": 2193.94, "end": 2198.36, "text": " require deferral to manage their overheads efficiently. It does offer that relief, but I", "tokens": [50635, 3651, 25704, 2155, 281, 3067, 641, 19922, 82, 19621, 13, 467, 775, 2626, 300, 10915, 11, 457, 286, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05659312532659162, "compression_ratio": 1.6993006993006994, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776620682263597e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 218854, "start": 2198.36, "end": 2202.32, "text": " would temper that enthusiasm just slightly. Oh, come on. Let me have this. Sorry. I have to be the", "tokens": [50856, 576, 3393, 300, 23417, 445, 4748, 13, 876, 11, 808, 322, 13, 961, 385, 362, 341, 13, 4919, 13, 286, 362, 281, 312, 264, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05659312532659162, "compression_ratio": 1.6993006993006994, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776620682263597e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 218854, "start": 2202.32, "end": 2208.3, "text": " voice of reason. Yes, the text proves that delay is optimal, but it is only optimal if you have", "tokens": [51054, 3177, 295, 1778, 13, 1079, 11, 264, 2487, 25019, 300, 8577, 307, 16252, 11, 457, 309, 307, 787, 16252, 498, 291, 362, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05659312532659162, "compression_ratio": 1.6993006993006994, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776620682263597e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 218854, "start": 2208.3, "end": 2215.94, "text": " flawlessly calculated the boundary. Ah, the boundary. The boundary is unforgiving. The microsecond you cross", "tokens": [51353, 13717, 12048, 15598, 264, 12866, 13, 2438, 11, 264, 12866, 13, 440, 12866, 307, 31411, 15441, 13, 440, 3123, 37841, 18882, 291, 3278, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05659312532659162, "compression_ratio": 1.6993006993006994, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776620682263597e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 221594, "start": 2215.94, "end": 2223.34, "text": " T star. The strategy inverts. What was optimal becomes catastrophic. And as we discussed with the", "tokens": [50365, 314, 3543, 13, 440, 5206, 28653, 1373, 13, 708, 390, 16252, 3643, 34915, 13, 400, 382, 321, 7152, 365, 264, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08606964608897334, "compression_ratio": 1.393103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245693162774243e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 221594, "start": 2223.34, "end": 2229.16, "text": " static view, if you are wrong about your compounding rate delta or wrong about the exponential convexity", "tokens": [50735, 13437, 1910, 11, 498, 291, 366, 2085, 466, 428, 14154, 278, 3314, 8289, 420, 2085, 466, 264, 21510, 42432, 507, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08606964608897334, "compression_ratio": 1.393103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245693162774243e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 222916, "start": 2229.16, "end": 2236.3399999999997, "text": " of P, that optimal strategy becomes a death sentence. The math gives us permission to delay, but it demands", "tokens": [50365, 295, 430, 11, 300, 16252, 5206, 3643, 257, 2966, 8174, 13, 440, 5221, 2709, 505, 11226, 281, 8577, 11, 457, 309, 15107, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17329947153727213, "compression_ratio": 1.5485074626865671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248865538330936e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 222916, "start": 2236.3399999999997, "end": 2242.7799999999997, "text": " absolute precision in return, which perfectly sets up our final segment, the frontier and open problems.", "tokens": [50724, 8236, 18356, 294, 2736, 11, 597, 6239, 6352, 493, 527, 2572, 9469, 11, 264, 35853, 293, 1269, 2740, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17329947153727213, "compression_ratio": 1.5485074626865671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248865538330936e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 222916, "start": 2242.98, "end": 2247.8799999999997, "text": " Because the work isn't done. Right. As brilliant and exhaustive as this crossover theorem is,", "tokens": [51056, 1436, 264, 589, 1943, 380, 1096, 13, 1779, 13, 1018, 10248, 293, 14687, 488, 382, 341, 33837, 20904, 307, 11, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17329947153727213, "compression_ratio": 1.5485074626865671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248865538330936e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 222916, "start": 2248.2799999999997, "end": 2253.56, "text": " Flexion is intellectually honest enough to admit that the maths currently has limits. The essay concludes by", "tokens": [51321, 29208, 313, 307, 46481, 3245, 1547, 281, 9796, 300, 264, 36287, 4362, 575, 10406, 13, 440, 16238, 24643, 538, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17329947153727213, "compression_ratio": 1.5485074626865671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248865538330936e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 225356, "start": 2253.56, "end": 2258.68, "text": " listing four specific open problems that remain unsolved in the framework. This section is", "tokens": [50365, 22161, 1451, 2685, 1269, 2740, 300, 6222, 2693, 29110, 294, 264, 8388, 13, 639, 3541, 307, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06761017867497035, "compression_ratio": 1.6466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897996031271177e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 225356, "start": 2258.68, "end": 2263.22, "text": " fascinating because it outlines the edges of our current theoretical understanding. It's really a", "tokens": [50621, 10343, 570, 309, 40125, 264, 8819, 295, 527, 2190, 20864, 3701, 13, 467, 311, 534, 257, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06761017867497035, "compression_ratio": 1.6466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897996031271177e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 225356, "start": 2263.22, "end": 2268.22, "text": " roadmap for the next decade of systems research. So what's the first one? The first open problem the", "tokens": [50848, 35738, 337, 264, 958, 10378, 295, 3652, 2132, 13, 407, 437, 311, 264, 700, 472, 30, 440, 700, 1269, 1154, 264, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06761017867497035, "compression_ratio": 1.6466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897996031271177e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 225356, "start": 2268.22, "end": 2272.7999999999997, "text": " author highlights is the assumption of non-constant delta and an A-day. Right. Throughout the paper,", "tokens": [51098, 3793, 14254, 307, 264, 15302, 295, 2107, 12, 25279, 394, 8289, 293, 364, 316, 12, 810, 13, 1779, 13, 22775, 264, 3035, 11, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06761017867497035, "compression_ratio": 1.6466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897996031271177e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 225356, "start": 2272.92, "end": 2279.22, "text": " the equations assume that the compounding rate, delta, is a fixed, steady number. But real life isn't a", "tokens": [51333, 264, 11787, 6552, 300, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 11, 8289, 11, 307, 257, 6806, 11, 13211, 1230, 13, 583, 957, 993, 1943, 380, 257, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06761017867497035, "compression_ratio": 1.6466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897996031271177e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 227922, "start": 2279.22, "end": 2285.22, "text": " clean constant equation. Exactly. If we go back to the national economy example, the loss of fiscal", "tokens": [50365, 2541, 5754, 5367, 13, 7587, 13, 759, 321, 352, 646, 281, 264, 4048, 5010, 1365, 11, 264, 4470, 295, 15897, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04693633444765781, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860290511482411e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 227922, "start": 2285.22, "end": 2292.3799999999997, "text": " credibility doesn't compound at a steady, predictable daily rate. It accelerates non-linearly. A run on a", "tokens": [50665, 28852, 1177, 380, 14154, 412, 257, 13211, 11, 27737, 5212, 3314, 13, 467, 10172, 1024, 2107, 12, 28263, 356, 13, 316, 1190, 322, 257, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04693633444765781, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860290511482411e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 227922, "start": 2292.3799999999997, "end": 2298.22, "text": " bank or a collapse of a currency starts incredibly slow and then happens all at once. The environment", "tokens": [51023, 3765, 420, 257, 15584, 295, 257, 13346, 3719, 6252, 2964, 293, 550, 2314, 439, 412, 1564, 13, 440, 2823, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04693633444765781, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860290511482411e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 227922, "start": 2298.22, "end": 2305.3999999999996, "text": " reacts to the decay. A fuller, more accurate model would need a delta parameter that dynamically adjusts", "tokens": [51315, 33305, 281, 264, 21039, 13, 316, 1577, 260, 11, 544, 8559, 2316, 576, 643, 257, 8289, 13075, 300, 43492, 4369, 82, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04693633444765781, "compression_ratio": 1.5606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860290511482411e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 230540, "start": 2305.4, "end": 2311.1600000000003, "text": " itself based on the accumulated deviation. The math for that dynamic interaction just does not yet", "tokens": [50365, 2564, 2361, 322, 264, 31346, 25163, 13, 440, 5221, 337, 300, 8546, 9285, 445, 775, 406, 1939, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06774054098566738, "compression_ratio": 1.6872852233676976, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170673721038202e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 230540, "start": 2311.1600000000003, "end": 2316.86, "text": " exist in this framework. The second open problem is dochastic deviation. The current math is entirely", "tokens": [50653, 2514, 294, 341, 8388, 13, 440, 1150, 1269, 1154, 307, 274, 8997, 2750, 25163, 13, 440, 2190, 5221, 307, 7696, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06774054098566738, "compression_ratio": 1.6872852233676976, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170673721038202e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 230540, "start": 2316.86, "end": 2321.62, "text": " deterministic. It assumes we possess perfect information about exactly how much damage is", "tokens": [50938, 15957, 3142, 13, 467, 37808, 321, 17490, 2176, 1589, 466, 2293, 577, 709, 4344, 307, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06774054098566738, "compression_ratio": 1.6872852233676976, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170673721038202e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 230540, "start": 2321.62, "end": 2326.36, "text": " happening at every time step. Well, what if the damage is random? What if we're operating in the fog of", "tokens": [51176, 2737, 412, 633, 565, 1823, 13, 1042, 11, 437, 498, 264, 4344, 307, 4974, 30, 708, 498, 321, 434, 7447, 294, 264, 13648, 295, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06774054098566738, "compression_ratio": 1.6872852233676976, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170673721038202e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 230540, "start": 2326.36, "end": 2332.56, "text": " war? Uncertainty about the true current state of the damage adds a massive hidden cost that this", "tokens": [51413, 1516, 30, 1156, 66, 1408, 874, 466, 264, 2074, 2190, 1785, 295, 264, 4344, 10860, 257, 5994, 7633, 2063, 300, 341, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06774054098566738, "compression_ratio": 1.6872852233676976, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170673721038202e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 233256, "start": 2332.56, "end": 2337.36, "text": " deterministic model does not yet price. It's the difference between knowing exactly how fast your", "tokens": [50365, 15957, 3142, 2316, 775, 406, 1939, 3218, 13, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 5276, 2293, 577, 2370, 428, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09357896252213238, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.415821995233435e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 233256, "start": 2337.36, "end": 2341.32, "text": " engine is losing oil versus just seeing a smudge of oil in your driveway and having to guess.", "tokens": [50605, 2848, 307, 7027, 3184, 5717, 445, 2577, 257, 899, 16032, 295, 3184, 294, 428, 38276, 293, 1419, 281, 2041, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09357896252213238, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.415821995233435e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 233256, "start": 2341.56, "end": 2347.02, "text": " The uncertainty itself drains your capacity. Yes. The author notes that introducing stochasticity", "tokens": [50815, 440, 15697, 2564, 47694, 428, 6042, 13, 1079, 13, 440, 3793, 5570, 300, 15424, 342, 8997, 2750, 507, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09357896252213238, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.415821995233435e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 233256, "start": 2347.02, "end": 2352.66, "text": " essentially introduces the concept of entropy into the repair equations. How do you calculate", "tokens": [51088, 4476, 31472, 264, 3410, 295, 30867, 666, 264, 10535, 11787, 13, 1012, 360, 291, 8873, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09357896252213238, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.415821995233435e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 233256, "start": 2352.66, "end": 2358.2599999999998, "text": " T-star when you aren't even sure if the system is inside the viability manifold? That is a massive,", "tokens": [51370,