 incredibly cheap, but triggering a crisis repair is astronomically expensive? This introduces the second scenario, which is driven entirely by the geometry of the compounding curve. Even if the emergency repair is expensive, if the problem compounds very, very slowly, I might still have a window where ignoring it is momentarily cheaper than paying the daily maintenance tax. Yes. I'll fix it later. Isn't just a symptom of human procrastination. Under the right geometric conditions, it can be the mathematically optimal choice. But the crucial, unforgiving caveat in Fliction's math is that this deferral window is always finite. It doesn't last forever. It is not a permanent state. If you wait too long, the convex cost of the crisis repair will inevitably explode past whatever you saved on maintenance. To make this tangible, let's look at how this plays out across four very different real-world domains. Let's start with biology. A biological system like an untreated infection or an escalating vascular condition. In biology, the compounding rate is extremely high. An infection doesn't just sit dormant in your arm, it actively replicates and amplifies itself. Because the problem accelerates so aggressively, the deferral window collapses almost instantly. If you have a severe infection, telling yourself, I'll fix it later, becomes catastrophic within days. The compounding curve is just too steep. Now contrast that with software maintenance. Let's say you have a dormant, non-propagating bug in an obscure part of your code base. This is the exact opposite geometry. The compounding rate is near zero. The bug just sits there. It doesn't actively infect the rest of the code or replicate itself. Meanwhile, the overhead of maintaining constant vigilance running continuous integration servers, halting development to fix every minor typo is very high. Right, it's exhausting. Therefore, deferring the fix is highly rational. You batch the minor bugs and fix them all at once later. But the danger is miscategorizing the bug. If you assume the compounding rate is zero, but it's actually a security vulnerability that hackers are actively exploiting to access more systems, the compounding rate is massive and deferring it destroys the company. Precisely. You have to understand the true compounding rate of the system you are managing. The third domain is physical infrastructure. Think of bridges, municipal water systems, or the electrical grid. A rusted beam on a bridge doesn't necessarily replicate like a biological infection, but infrastructure has a different structural tear, the sheer convexity of the crisis cost. Replacing a single rusted beam during routine maintenance is relatively cheap. But if you defer that maintenance until the beam snaps and the bridge collapses, the cost isn't just replacing the bridge. No, it's catastrophic. It's the economic devastation of rerouted traffic, the years of environmental reviews, the emergency redesigns, and the loss of life. The cost curve is so wildly convex that it demands continuous maintenance, even if the compounding rate is slow. And the fourth domain is the one that brings all these dangerous variables together at once. Massive fiscal systems. Think of a sovereign debt crisis or a massive corporate restructuring that keeps getting kicked down the road. A heavily indebted fiscal structure exhibits the worst of all parameters simultaneously. You have massive fixed overheads just to audit and comply with the system. You have incredibly high initiation costs for a crisis bailout. The structural imbalance compounds actively every day due to compounding interest and the gradual loss of institutional trust. It's just a nightmare. And the ultimate cost of a systemic crash is deeply convex, impacting the entire surrounding ecology. It is the absolute perfect storm of bad math. And this leads to an asymptotic estimate in the paper that is truly chilling. When you model all these variables interacting over time, the systems that appear to have the highest tolerance for deferring maintenance, the massive wealthy systems where the daily monitoring costs seem like a drop in the bucket compared to their vast resources, are actually the ones whose thresholds erode the absolute fastest the moment the problem begins to actively compound. Wait, if a system looks rich and stable, it actually crashes faster once it tips over? Yes. A system that believes it has a massive, luxurious runway for deferring a problem will lose that runway disproportionately fast. Deferral tolerance is eroded fastest in precisely the systems that most appear on a static reading to be able to afford the luxury of waiting. So what does this all mean for us, for you and me, managing our own lives or our own organizations? It means that mistaking a high compounding problem like an eroding company culture, a growing biological illness, or a creeping debt for a low compounding problem like a harmless software bug is the exact mechanism of catastrophic failure. Yes. We tell ourselves, I'll fix it later, because we intuitively apply the safe logic of a dormant bug to the aggressive reality of a compounding infection. And by the time we realize our error, the math has already doomed us. The window has slammed shut, and the convex cost of repair is entirely unsurvivable. It is a fundamental failure of categorization. We misjudge the geometry of the problem we are deferring, and the math shows absolutely no mercy. Wow. Okay, let's pull all of this immense ground we've covered together. We started by dismantling the illusion of the present state, realizing that our automatic skills, our computer macros, and our legal rules are actually compressed scars. They are long, messy histories of trial and error folded up for the sake of efficiency. We explored the anti-alignment theorem, proving that the closer we get to perfect efficiency, the further we get from repairability. We risk becoming brittle experts, blindingly fast in normal conditions, but entirely doomed when the environment shifts because we discarded our diagnostic history. We completely redefine boredom, not as lack of shiny objects, but as the cessation of learning and compression. And we realize that curing it requires the uncomfortable discipline of voluntary handicapping and, most importantly, the protection of unstructured time. We navigated the ecology of constraints, discovering how redundant rules can masquerade as healthy diversity while actually paralyzing a system from the inside out. And finally, we mapped out the finite, unforgiving window of, I'll fix it later. Realizing that our intuition about when to defer maintenance is dangerously flawed, especially in massive systems that look too big to fail. It is a profound reframing of how we interact with complexity at every single level. But as we wrap up, if we connect this to the bigger picture, there is one final implication that emerges when you lay all five of these essays on top of each other. An implication Fliction's math points directly toward, but that we haven't explicitly named yet. What happens when we scale this up? Consider the current trajectory of our global technological infrastructure. Look at the rise of massive, opaque artificial intelligence models. Look at the hyper-optimization of just-in-time global supply chains. If this entire corpus of work is correct, our whole civilization is currently relentlessly optimizing for inactability. We are becoming a planetary-scale, brittle expert. We are compressing all historical knowledge, all intermediate human reasoning, and all local buffers into highly efficient black box systems. We are discarding the raw, unstructured history to maximize execution speed and minimize overhead. We are driving towards the absolute minimal trace on a global scale. And if the anti-alignment theorem holds true? It means we are systematically maximizing our global repair blindness. If we hit a massive distribution shift, a novel climate event, a cascading digital failure across networks, a geopolitical fracturing, we might find that because we prioritize perfect efficiency, we have retained absolutely no trace of how to fix the modern world. We will possess the automated skill to enact civilization, but we will have entirely lost the structural representation required to repair it. We are building the ultimate automated macro for society, but we are throwing away the instructions on how it was originally coded. That is haunting. And it is exactly the kind of perspective-shifting insight we look for. Thank you for joining us today for being the crucial third voice as we unpacked all this. Do yourself a favor today. Find a moment of completely unstructured time. Sit with it. Build some raw history. Don't let an algorithm compress your experience for you. Just let it be messy. We will see you on the next Deep Dive. We will see you on the next Deep Dive.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 7.140000000000001, "text": " You know, usually when we talk about a medical diagnosis, there is this expectation of just like clinical precision.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 458, 11, 2673, 562, 321, 751, 466, 257, 4625, 15217, 11, 456, 307, 341, 14334, 295, 445, 411, 9115, 18356, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09950638668877738, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672331496128454e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 7.44, "end": 9.38, "text": " Right. Yeah. You expect a very clear answer.", "tokens": [50737, 1779, 13, 865, 13, 509, 2066, 257, 588, 1850, 1867, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09950638668877738, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672331496128454e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 9.56, "end": 15.68, "text": " Exactly. I mean, you break your arm, the x-ray shows that jagged white line right across the bone, and the doctor just points at it.", "tokens": [50843, 7587, 13, 286, 914, 11, 291, 1821, 428, 3726, 11, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 3110, 300, 6368, 3004, 2418, 1622, 558, 2108, 264, 9026, 11, 293, 264, 4631, 445, 2793, 412, 309, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09950638668877738, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672331496128454e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 15.84, "end": 24.42, "text": " And there is the problem. It is binary, it's visible, and well, it's comforting, you know, because you can point to the exact state of the failure.", "tokens": [51157, 400, 456, 307, 264, 1154, 13, 467, 307, 17434, 11, 309, 311, 8974, 11, 293, 731, 11, 309, 311, 38439, 11, 291, 458, 11, 570, 291, 393, 935, 281, 264, 1900, 1785, 295, 264, 7763, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09950638668877738, "compression_ratio": 1.619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672331496128454e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 2442, "start": 24.42, "end": 41.0, "text": " We really do crave that visibility. We want to believe that when a system fails, whether it is a bone or a car engine or even a marriage, we want to think the failure is this distinct, observable thing sitting right there in the present moment, just waiting to be identified.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 534, 360, 46875, 300, 19883, 13, 492, 528, 281, 1697, 300, 562, 257, 1185, 18199, 11, 1968, 309, 307, 257, 9026, 420, 257, 1032, 2848, 420, 754, 257, 7194, 11, 321, 528, 281, 519, 264, 7763, 307, 341, 10644, 11, 9951, 712, 551, 3798, 558, 456, 294, 264, 1974, 1623, 11, 445, 3806, 281, 312, 9234, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10482271001973284, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 6.767842579760708e-13}, {"id": 5, "seek": 2442, "start": 41.36, "end": 48.56, "text": " Yeah. But then you step into the world of like neurodevelopment or trauma or even complex organizational collapse.", "tokens": [51212, 865, 13, 583, 550, 291, 1823, 666, 264, 1002, 295, 411, 16499, 35464, 518, 420, 11407, 420, 754, 3997, 24730, 15584, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10482271001973284, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 6.767842579760708e-13}, {"id": 6, "seek": 2442, "start": 48.68000000000001, "end": 48.900000000000006, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51578, 865, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10482271001973284, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 6.767842579760708e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2442, "start": 49.1, "end": 51.64, "text": " And suddenly that x-ray machine is completely useless.", "tokens": [51599, 400, 5800, 300, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 307, 2584, 14115, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10482271001973284, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 6.767842579760708e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2442, "start": 51.64, "end": 53.08, "text": " How entirely useless.", "tokens": [51726, 1012, 7696, 14115, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10482271001973284, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 6.767842579760708e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 5308, "start": 53.08, "end": 67.53999999999999, "text": " You are looking at a diagnostic landscape that is just incredibly murky. There is no single jagged white line to point to. Because the problem isn't a broken piece, right? The problem is the entire history of how the system adapted to survive up until this point.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 27897, 9661, 300, 307, 445, 6252, 5257, 4133, 13, 821, 307, 572, 2167, 6368, 3004, 2418, 1622, 281, 935, 281, 13, 1436, 264, 1154, 1943, 380, 257, 5463, 2522, 11, 558, 30, 440, 1154, 307, 264, 2302, 2503, 295, 577, 264, 1185, 20871, 281, 7867, 493, 1826, 341, 935, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06016804808277195, "compression_ratio": 1.4371584699453552, "no_speech_prob": 1.284411054076895e-12}, {"id": 10, "seek": 6754, "start": 67.54, "end": 75.02000000000001, "text": " Which, and this is perfect, brings us to the core premise we are unpacking today. Because we walk through life assuming that things just are.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 11, 293, 341, 307, 2176, 11, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 22045, 321, 366, 26699, 278, 965, 13, 1436, 321, 1792, 807, 993, 11926, 300, 721, 445, 366, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1063961104342812, "compression_ratio": 1.2436974789915967, "no_speech_prob": 1.701551443147875e-12}, {"id": 11, "seek": 6754, "start": 75.44000000000001, "end": 75.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50760, 1779, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1063961104342812, "compression_ratio": 1.2436974789915967, "no_speech_prob": 1.701551443147875e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 7568, "start": 75.68, "end": 88.2, "text": " We look at a master pianist playing a concerto or a functioning body of constitutional law or, you know, a flawless piece of software and we see a state of being. We think we're looking at a finished product.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 574, 412, 257, 4505, 32198, 468, 2433, 257, 8543, 78, 420, 257, 18483, 1772, 295, 20176, 2101, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 45693, 2522, 295, 4722, 293, 321, 536, 257, 1785, 295, 885, 13, 492, 519, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 257, 4335, 1674, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09130064010620118, "compression_ratio": 1.4344827586206896, "no_speech_prob": 3.068965004002222e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 8820, "start": 88.2, "end": 99.9, "text": " But if we apply the lens of the five theoretical essays we're diving into today, which were written in 2026 by an author known only as Flixion, that polished state is an absolute illusion.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 321, 3079, 264, 6765, 295, 264, 1732, 20864, 35123, 321, 434, 20241, 666, 965, 11, 597, 645, 3720, 294, 945, 10880, 538, 364, 3793, 2570, 787, 382, 3235, 970, 313, 11, 300, 29079, 1785, 307, 364, 8236, 18854, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08000782012939453, "compression_ratio": 1.519047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614942486755437e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 8820, "start": 100.16, "end": 107.44, "text": " A total illusion. The overarching thesis of this entire Flixion corpus is that these systems are not made of static states at all.", "tokens": [50963, 316, 3217, 18854, 13, 440, 45501, 22288, 295, 341, 2302, 3235, 970, 313, 1181, 31624, 307, 300, 613, 3652, 366, 406, 1027, 295, 13437, 4368, 412, 439, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08000782012939453, "compression_ratio": 1.519047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614942486755437e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 10744, "start": 107.44, "end": 113.7, "text": " Every polished skill, every smooth system, every perfectly executed habit that you interact with it is actually a scar.", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 29079, 5389, 11, 633, 5508, 1185, 11, 633, 6239, 17577, 7164, 300, 291, 4648, 365, 309, 307, 767, 257, 10569, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0792904228999697, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426212603656842e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 10744, "start": 113.89999999999999, "end": 118.44, "text": " That's such a great way to put it. Yes, a scar. It is a compressed history of past mistakes.", "tokens": [50688, 663, 311, 1270, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 1079, 11, 257, 10569, 13, 467, 307, 257, 30353, 2503, 295, 1791, 8038, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0792904228999697, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426212603656842e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 10744, "start": 118.86, "end": 126.42, "text": " It is a trajectory of trial and error, of failures and micro-corrections that has been folded up so tightly that it can run efficiently in the present.", "tokens": [50936, 467, 307, 257, 21512, 295, 7308, 293, 6713, 11, 295, 20774, 293, 4532, 12, 19558, 2554, 626, 300, 575, 668, 23940, 493, 370, 21952, 300, 309, 393, 1190, 19621, 294, 264, 1974, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0792904228999697, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426212603656842e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 12642, "start": 126.42, "end": 140.0, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this. Because if Slixion is right, the way you and I measure efficiency, the way we try to cure our own boredom, and the way we decide when to fix our broken systems, it is all completely upside down.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 1436, 498, 6187, 970, 313, 307, 558, 11, 264, 636, 291, 293, 286, 3481, 10493, 11, 264, 636, 321, 853, 281, 13698, 527, 1065, 13521, 298, 11, 293, 264, 636, 321, 4536, 562, 281, 3191, 527, 5463, 3652, 11, 309, 307, 439, 2584, 14119, 760, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.050117000780607525, "compression_ratio": 1.616, "no_speech_prob": 1.2742991340949916e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 12642, "start": 140.02, "end": 151.74, "text": " It really forces a massive perspective shift. To understand how systems break, we first have to prove that our fundamental understanding of how systems exist is just, well, it's wrong.", "tokens": [51045, 467, 534, 5874, 257, 5994, 4585, 5513, 13, 1407, 1223, 577, 3652, 1821, 11, 321, 700, 362, 281, 7081, 300, 527, 8088, 3701, 295, 577, 3652, 2514, 307, 445, 11, 731, 11, 309, 311, 2085, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.050117000780607525, "compression_ratio": 1.616, "no_speech_prob": 1.2742991340949916e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 15174, "start": 151.74, "end": 165.92000000000002, "text": " So the ground floor of this entire theory attacks something we all implicitly believe. In physics, in computer science, and honestly just like walking down the street, we operate on the assumption that the present moment contains everything we need to know to predict the future.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 2727, 4123, 295, 341, 2302, 5261, 8122, 746, 321, 439, 26947, 356, 1697, 13, 682, 10649, 11, 294, 3820, 3497, 11, 293, 6095, 445, 411, 4494, 760, 264, 4838, 11, 321, 9651, 322, 264, 15302, 300, 264, 1974, 1623, 8306, 1203, 321, 643, 281, 458, 281, 6069, 264, 2027, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0788293891482883, "compression_ratio": 1.7165354330708662, "no_speech_prob": 1.636205819270653e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 15174, "start": 166.24, "end": 174.38, "text": " Right. The formal idea in physics and computer science is called state sufficiency. It is this default assumption that the present state is enough.", "tokens": [51090, 1779, 13, 440, 9860, 1558, 294, 10649, 293, 3820, 3497, 307, 1219, 1785, 459, 49086, 13, 467, 307, 341, 7576, 15302, 300, 264, 1974, 1785, 307, 1547, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0788293891482883, "compression_ratio": 1.7165354330708662, "no_speech_prob": 1.636205819270653e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 15174, "start": 174.62, "end": 174.9, "text": " Meaning?", "tokens": [51509, 19948, 30, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0788293891482883, "compression_ratio": 1.7165354330708662, "no_speech_prob": 1.636205819270653e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 17490, "start": 174.9, "end": 183.96, "text": " Meaning, if I know the exact position and momentum of a billiard ball rolling across the table right now, classical mechanics tells me I can predict exactly where it will bounce next.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 11, 498, 286, 458, 264, 1900, 2535, 293, 11244, 295, 257, 2961, 72, 515, 2594, 9439, 2108, 264, 3199, 558, 586, 11, 13735, 12939, 5112, 385, 286, 393, 6069, 2293, 689, 309, 486, 15894, 958, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05328408620690787, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073606425552999e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 17490, "start": 184.02, "end": 184.78, "text": " Right, because of math.", "tokens": [50821, 1779, 11, 570, 295, 5221, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05328408620690787, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073606425552999e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 17490, "start": 185.20000000000002, "end": 195.96, "text": " Exactly. I don't need to know who hit the ball or what path it took to get to that specific spot on the felt. The history is completely irrelevant. The present state contains all the necessary data.", "tokens": [50880, 7587, 13, 286, 500, 380, 643, 281, 458, 567, 2045, 264, 2594, 420, 437, 3100, 309, 1890, 281, 483, 281, 300, 2685, 4008, 322, 264, 2762, 13, 440, 2503, 307, 2584, 28682, 13, 440, 1974, 1785, 8306, 439, 264, 4818, 1412, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05328408620690787, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073606425552999e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 19596, "start": 195.96, "end": 206.08, "text": " But Fliction looks at complex systems and just completely rejects that. For human minds, for legal frameworks, for software architecture, states are not the ground floor.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 1542, 412, 3997, 3652, 293, 445, 2584, 8248, 82, 300, 13, 1171, 1952, 9634, 11, 337, 5089, 29834, 11, 337, 4722, 9482, 11, 4368, 366, 406, 264, 2727, 4123, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10109433612307987, "compression_ratio": 1.328125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171588807650794e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 20608, "start": 206.08, "end": 217.36, "text": " Not at all. In these papers, specifically the ones titled Against Eventless Ontology in History Before Function, Fliction argues that states are actually just equivalence classes of compressed trajectories.", "tokens": [50365, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 682, 613, 10577, 11, 4682, 264, 2306, 19841, 29995, 13222, 1832, 16980, 1793, 294, 12486, 4546, 11166, 882, 11, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 4368, 366, 767, 445, 9052, 655, 5359, 295, 30353, 18257, 2083, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06059753442112403, "compression_ratio": 1.5020242914979758, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359653432287957e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 20608, "start": 217.70000000000002, "end": 227.46, "text": " Which is a very dense way of saying that the polished state we are looking at only exists because a really long, messy history was squashed down into a usable form.", "tokens": [50946, 3013, 307, 257, 588, 18011, 636, 295, 1566, 300, 264, 29079, 1785, 321, 366, 1237, 412, 787, 8198, 570, 257, 534, 938, 11, 16191, 2503, 390, 2339, 12219, 760, 666, 257, 29975, 1254, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06059753442112403, "compression_ratio": 1.5020242914979758, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359653432287957e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 22746, "start": 227.46, "end": 236.92000000000002, "text": " Yes. History has to come before function. You literally cannot separate a complex capability from the history that generated it. The history is the actual material the capability is mad at.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 12486, 575, 281, 808, 949, 2445, 13, 509, 3736, 2644, 4994, 257, 3997, 13759, 490, 264, 2503, 300, 10833, 309, 13, 440, 2503, 307, 264, 3539, 2527, 264, 13759, 307, 5244, 412, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08653214344611534, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252717708649777e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 22746, "start": 237.28, "end": 250.76000000000002, "text": " Okay, let's ground this. Because when I first read about this whole squashed down histories concept, my mind immediately went to a very mundane, incredibly frustrating experience I had last week trying to automate a task on my computer.", "tokens": [50856, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 2727, 341, 13, 1436, 562, 286, 700, 1401, 466, 341, 1379, 2339, 12219, 760, 30631, 3410, 11, 452, 1575, 4258, 1437, 281, 257, 588, 43497, 11, 6252, 16522, 1752, 286, 632, 1036, 1243, 1382, 281, 31605, 257, 5633, 322, 452, 3820, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08653214344611534, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252717708649777e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 22746, "start": 251.20000000000002, "end": 256.62, "text": " And the text actually uses a really similar example of a text expansion macro.", "tokens": [51552, 400, 264, 2487, 767, 4960, 257, 534, 2531, 1365, 295, 257, 2487, 11260, 18887, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08653214344611534, "compression_ratio": 1.6611842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252717708649777e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 25662, "start": 256.62, "end": 261.68, "text": " Oh, the PDF formatting example. It perfectly illustrates this illusion of the present state.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 264, 17752, 39366, 1365, 13, 467, 6239, 41718, 341, 18854, 295, 264, 1974, 1785, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 25662, "start": 261.88, "end": 269.3, "text": " Right. So imagine you have a folder of scanned receipts and you want to convert them into a single, searchable PDF document.", "tokens": [50628, 1779, 13, 407, 3811, 291, 362, 257, 10820, 295, 45089, 2268, 48908, 293, 291, 528, 281, 7620, 552, 666, 257, 2167, 11, 3164, 712, 17752, 4166, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 25662, "start": 269.4, "end": 270.18, "text": " Sounds easy enough.", "tokens": [51004, 14576, 1858, 1547, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 25662, "start": 270.3, "end": 270.88, "text": " You would think.", "tokens": [51049, 509, 576, 519, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 25662, "start": 270.96, "end": 271.22, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51082, 865, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 25662, "start": 271.4, "end": 280.06, "text": " But the first time you tried to do this using command line tools, it is an absolute disaster. You string some code together to combine the images and you run it. It fails.", "tokens": [51104, 583, 264, 700, 565, 291, 3031, 281, 360, 341, 1228, 5622, 1622, 3873, 11, 309, 307, 364, 8236, 11293, 13, 509, 6798, 512, 3089, 1214, 281, 10432, 264, 5267, 293, 291, 1190, 309, 13, 467, 18199, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 25662, "start": 280.36, "end": 280.8, "text": " Naturally.", "tokens": [51552, 34304, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 25662, "start": 280.9, "end": 282.8, "text": " You realize half the receipts are upside down.", "tokens": [51579, 509, 4325, 1922, 264, 2268, 48908, 366, 14119, 760, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09626778689297763, "compression_ratio": 1.6442953020134228, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674015904632022e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 28280, "start": 282.8, "end": 293.62, "text": " Yeah. So you spend 10 minutes searching forums to find a piece of code that auto-orients images based on their text. You add that in. It works, but the text isn't searchable.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 407, 291, 3496, 1266, 2077, 10808, 26998, 281, 915, 257, 2522, 295, 3089, 300, 8399, 12, 284, 2448, 5267, 2361, 322, 641, 2487, 13, 509, 909, 300, 294, 13, 467, 1985, 11, 457, 264, 2487, 1943, 380, 3164, 712, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07049177714756556, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253350220209796e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 28280, "start": 293.74, "end": 295.18, "text": " Right. So you have to go back again.", "tokens": [50912, 1779, 13, 407, 291, 362, 281, 352, 646, 797, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07049177714756556, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253350220209796e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 28280, "start": 295.5, "end": 307.58000000000004, "text": " Exactly. You go back, you find an optical character recognition tool, an OCR, and you bolt that onto your script. Finally, after 30 minutes of errors, syntax mistakes, and just pure frustration, it works.", "tokens": [51000, 7587, 13, 509, 352, 646, 11, 291, 915, 364, 20674, 2517, 11150, 2290, 11, 364, 422, 18547, 11, 293, 291, 13436, 300, 3911, 428, 5755, 13, 6288, 11, 934, 2217, 2077, 295, 13603, 11, 28431, 8038, 11, 293, 445, 6075, 20491, 11, 309, 1985, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07049177714756556, "compression_ratio": 1.5877862595419847, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253350220209796e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 30758, "start": 307.58, "end": 319.74, "text": " And that 30 minutes of frustration is the raw material. That is the history. It is the trajectory of attempts, the dead ends, the realization that orientation has to happen before character recognition.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 2217, 2077, 295, 20491, 307, 264, 8936, 2527, 13, 663, 307, 264, 2503, 13, 467, 307, 264, 21512, 295, 15257, 11, 264, 3116, 5314, 11, 264, 25138, 300, 14764, 575, 281, 1051, 949, 2517, 11150, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08072235470726377, "compression_ratio": 1.4532374100719425, "no_speech_prob": 1.591851975756009e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 31974, "start": 319.74, "end": 324.48, "text": " But I am never, ever going to type out that massive block of code again.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 286, 669, 1128, 11, 1562, 516, 281, 2010, 484, 300, 5994, 3461, 295, 3089, 797, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 31974, "start": 324.56, "end": 325.16, "text": " Of course not.", "tokens": [50606, 2720, 1164, 406, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 31974, "start": 325.38, "end": 332.12, "text": " So I take that final perfect string of commands and I save it as a simple keyboard shortcut, a macro. Let's call it howtopdf.", "tokens": [50647, 407, 286, 747, 300, 2572, 2176, 6798, 295, 16901, 293, 286, 3155, 309, 382, 257, 2199, 10186, 24822, 11, 257, 18887, 13, 961, 311, 818, 309, 577, 19337, 45953, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 31974, "start": 332.62, "end": 338.2, "text": " Now, whenever I type those letters and hit enter, the computer instantly reads, rotates, and binds my images.", "tokens": [51009, 823, 11, 5699, 286, 2010, 729, 7825, 293, 2045, 3242, 11, 264, 3820, 13518, 15700, 11, 42133, 11, 293, 41515, 452, 5267, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 31974, "start": 338.36, "end": 339.18, "text": " It looks like magic.", "tokens": [51296, 467, 1542, 411, 5585, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 31974, "start": 339.44, "end": 339.90000000000003, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51350, 467, 775, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 31974, "start": 340.04, "end": 340.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51380, 865, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 31974, "start": 340.36, "end": 347.68, "text": " To someone watching me do this today or even to me a year from now, you just press a button and the result appears. It looks like a self-contained prison state.", "tokens": [51396, 1407, 1580, 1976, 385, 360, 341, 965, 420, 754, 281, 385, 257, 1064, 490, 586, 11, 291, 445, 1886, 257, 2960, 293, 264, 1874, 7038, 13, 467, 1542, 411, 257, 2698, 12, 9000, 3563, 6168, 1785, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11411721757847629, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968993906355204e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 34768, "start": 347.68, "end": 353.08, "text": " But underneath that single button press is the entire discarded history of your trial and error.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 7223, 300, 2167, 2960, 1886, 307, 264, 2302, 45469, 2503, 295, 428, 7308, 293, 6713, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13235706506773484, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724426105477972e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 34768, "start": 353.40000000000003, "end": 361.64, "text": " And this introduces a massive structural asymmetry in how we operate, because there is a huge gulf between enacting a function and representing it.", "tokens": [50651, 400, 341, 31472, 257, 5994, 15067, 37277, 9889, 294, 577, 321, 9651, 11, 570, 456, 307, 257, 2603, 290, 5757, 1296, 25909, 278, 257, 2445, 293, 13460, 309, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13235706506773484, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724426105477972e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 34768, "start": 362.04, "end": 365.2, "text": " The structural asymmetry between doing and explaining.", "tokens": [51083, 440, 15067, 37277, 9889, 1296, 884, 293, 13468, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13235706506773484, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724426105477972e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 34768, "start": 365.36, "end": 371.06, "text": " Exactly. When you trigger that macro, you are enacting the skill perfectly. The function executes.", "tokens": [51249, 7587, 13, 1133, 291, 7875, 300, 18887, 11, 291, 366, 25909, 278, 264, 5389, 6239, 13, 440, 2445, 4454, 1819, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13235706506773484, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724426105477972e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 37106, "start": 371.06, "end": 378.46, "text": " Yes. But if a co-worker walks up and asks you why the auto-orient flag needs to execute before the character recognition pipeline...", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 583, 498, 257, 598, 12, 49402, 12896, 493, 293, 8962, 291, 983, 264, 8399, 12, 19521, 7166, 2203, 281, 14483, 949, 264, 2517, 11150, 15517, 485, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727303835810447, "compression_ratio": 1.5524475524475525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552044244429575e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 37106, "start": 378.46, "end": 388.28, "text": " I would stare at them blankly. I mean, I know it works, but I have completely forgotten the underlying logic because I deleted the messy history to make the tool fast and efficient.", "tokens": [50735, 286, 576, 22432, 412, 552, 8247, 356, 13, 286, 914, 11, 286, 458, 309, 1985, 11, 457, 286, 362, 2584, 11832, 264, 14217, 9952, 570, 286, 22981, 264, 16191, 2503, 281, 652, 264, 2290, 2370, 293, 7148, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727303835810447, "compression_ratio": 1.5524475524475525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552044244429575e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 37106, "start": 388.56, "end": 396.06, "text": " What's fascinating here is that this provides a mathematical explanation for Michael Polanyi's famous concept of tacit knowledge.", "tokens": [51240, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 300, 341, 6417, 257, 18894, 10835, 337, 5116, 3635, 1325, 72, 311, 4618, 3410, 295, 25018, 270, 3601, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727303835810447, "compression_ratio": 1.5524475524475525, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552044244429575e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 39606, "start": 396.06, "end": 398.48, "text": " The idea that we know more than we can tell.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1558, 300, 321, 458, 544, 813, 321, 393, 980, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08683946762961903, "compression_ratio": 1.5497835497835497, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492860900440109e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 39606, "start": 398.62, "end": 409.32, "text": " Right. Think about riding a bicycle. We can ride a bike perfectly. We can dynamically shift our center of mass to counteract gravity as we lean into a turn. We enact the physics flawlessly.", "tokens": [50493, 1779, 13, 6557, 466, 9546, 257, 20888, 13, 492, 393, 5077, 257, 5656, 6239, 13, 492, 393, 43492, 5513, 527, 3056, 295, 2758, 281, 5682, 578, 12110, 382, 321, 11659, 666, 257, 1261, 13, 492, 25909, 264, 10649, 13717, 12048, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08683946762961903, "compression_ratio": 1.5497835497835497, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492860900440109e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 39606, "start": 409.66, "end": 415.7, "text": " But if we had to stop and write the actual equations on a whiteboard for how we keep our balance, we would fail completely.", "tokens": [51045, 583, 498, 321, 632, 281, 1590, 293, 2464, 264, 3539, 11787, 322, 257, 2418, 3787, 337, 577, 321, 1066, 527, 4772, 11, 321, 576, 3061, 2584, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08683946762961903, "compression_ratio": 1.5497835497835497, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492860900440109e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 41570, "start": 415.7, "end": 433.88, "text": " We would. And the knowledge isn't hidden in some mystical subconscious realm. It's just that the process of mastering the bicycle literally discarded the intermediate cognitive steps. We traded the ability to hold a symbolic representation of the skill for the ability to enact it instantly.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 576, 13, 400, 264, 3601, 1943, 380, 7633, 294, 512, 40565, 27389, 15355, 13, 467, 311, 445, 300, 264, 1399, 295, 49382, 264, 20888, 3736, 45469, 264, 19376, 15605, 4439, 13, 492, 27157, 264, 3485, 281, 1797, 257, 25755, 10290, 295, 264, 5389, 337, 264, 3485, 281, 25909, 309, 13518, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07473732500660177, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553878272832946e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 41570, "start": 434.32, "end": 445.14, "text": " We traded visibility for speed. And this brings us to what Flickshen calls the anti-alignment theorem. And honestly, it is one of the most sobering concepts in these papers.", "tokens": [51296, 492, 27157, 19883, 337, 3073, 13, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 5498, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 13, 400, 6095, 11, 309, 307, 472, 295, 264, 881, 26212, 278, 10392, 294, 613, 10577, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07473732500660177, "compression_ratio": 1.6787003610108304, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553878272832946e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 44514, "start": 445.14, "end": 445.91999999999996, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07083345714368318, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.3097436546774532e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 44514, "start": 446.0, "end": 450.91999999999996, "text": " Because it mathematically proves that this trade-off comes with a devastating cost.", "tokens": [50408, 1436, 309, 44003, 25019, 300, 341, 4923, 12, 4506, 1487, 365, 257, 21280, 2063, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07083345714368318, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.3097436546774532e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 44514, "start": 451.7, "end": 462.08, "text": " I actually had to put the text down and walk away when I read this part. I mean, I spend so much of my life trying to optimize my routines, clear out the friction, and make my work processes as minimal and efficient as possible.", "tokens": [50693, 286, 767, 632, 281, 829, 264, 2487, 760, 293, 1792, 1314, 562, 286, 1401, 341, 644, 13, 286, 914, 11, 286, 3496, 370, 709, 295, 452, 993, 1382, 281, 19719, 452, 33827, 11, 1850, 484, 264, 17710, 11, 293, 652, 452, 589, 7555, 382, 13206, 293, 7148, 382, 1944, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07083345714368318, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.3097436546774532e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 44514, "start": 462.12, "end": 464.18, "text": " We all do. That is the modern ideal.", "tokens": [51214, 492, 439, 360, 13, 663, 307, 264, 4363, 7157, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07083345714368318, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.3097436546774532e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 44514, "start": 464.44, "end": 469.36, "text": " Right. But the anti-alignment theorem essentially says that by doing that, I am digging my own grave.", "tokens": [51330, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 4476, 1619, 300, 538, 884, 300, 11, 286, 669, 17343, 452, 1065, 12525, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07083345714368318, "compression_ratio": 1.6202090592334495, "no_speech_prob": 1.3097436546774532e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 46936, "start": 469.36, "end": 483.92, "text": " The math is unforgiving on this. If you compress your history to make your macro or your business operation or even your morning routine as hyper-efficient as possible, you reach what is called the minimal generating history, the absolute fastest way to execute the task.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 307, 31411, 15441, 322, 341, 13, 759, 291, 14778, 428, 2503, 281, 652, 428, 18887, 420, 428, 1606, 6916, 420, 754, 428, 2446, 9927, 382, 9848, 12, 68, 7816, 382, 1944, 11, 291, 2524, 437, 307, 1219, 264, 13206, 17746, 2503, 11, 264, 8236, 14573, 636, 281, 14483, 264, 5633, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.030058245909841436, "compression_ratio": 1.5485714285714285, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145465618813468e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 48392, "start": 483.92, "end": 493.2, "text": " But the theorem proves that this hyper-efficient state is mathematically guaranteed to be the absolute worst possible state for diagnosing a failure.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 20904, 25019, 300, 341, 9848, 12, 68, 7816, 1785, 307, 44003, 18031, 281, 312, 264, 8236, 5855, 1944, 1785, 337, 7234, 6110, 257, 7763, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04726842641830444, "compression_ratio": 1.6411483253588517, "no_speech_prob": 1.655243758898195e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 48392, "start": 494.88, "end": 506.18, "text": " Wait, wait. So if I streamline my life, my code, or my business to be as hyper-efficient as possible, am I mathematically guaranteeing that when it inevitably breaks, I won't be able to fix it?", "tokens": [50913, 3802, 11, 1699, 13, 407, 498, 286, 47141, 452, 993, 11, 452, 3089, 11, 420, 452, 1606, 281, 312, 382, 9848, 12, 68, 7816, 382, 1944, 11, 669, 286, 44003, 10815, 278, 300, 562, 309, 28171, 9857, 11, 286, 1582, 380, 312, 1075, 281, 3191, 309, 30, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04726842641830444, "compression_ratio": 1.6411483253588517, "no_speech_prob": 1.655243758898195e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 50618, "start": 506.18, "end": 515.02, "text": " Yes. That is exactly what the retention lattice models in the paper show. Minimizing storage costs, getting rid of the friction, strictly maximizes repair entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 264, 22871, 34011, 5245, 294, 264, 3035, 855, 13, 2829, 332, 3319, 6725, 5497, 11, 1242, 3973, 295, 264, 17710, 11, 20792, 5138, 5660, 10535, 30867, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10646675572250829, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236273393463452e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 50618, "start": 515.1800000000001, "end": 516.82, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50815, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10646675572250829, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236273393463452e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 50618, "start": 517.02, "end": 527.26, "text": " Let's visualize it as a spectrum, like a trade-off scale. On one end, you have the full, uncompressed history. You kept every sticky note, every failed piece of code, every manual, intermediate step.", "tokens": [50907, 961, 311, 23273, 309, 382, 257, 11143, 11, 411, 257, 4923, 12, 4506, 4373, 13, 1282, 472, 917, 11, 291, 362, 264, 1577, 11, 8585, 79, 3805, 2503, 13, 509, 4305, 633, 14470, 3637, 11, 633, 7612, 2522, 295, 3089, 11, 633, 9688, 11, 19376, 1823, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10646675572250829, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236273393463452e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 50618, "start": 527.34, "end": 528.14, "text": " It's super messy.", "tokens": [51423, 467, 311, 1687, 16191, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10646675572250829, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236273393463452e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 52814, "start": 528.14, "end": 538.1, "text": " Very messy. But if your system breaks, your repair entropy, your diagnostic uncertainty is near zero. You can just look at your messy pile of notes and pinpoint exactly which step failed.", "tokens": [50365, 4372, 16191, 13, 583, 498, 428, 1185, 9857, 11, 428, 10535, 30867, 11, 428, 27897, 15697, 307, 2651, 4018, 13, 509, 393, 445, 574, 412, 428, 16191, 14375, 295, 5570, 293, 40837, 2293, 597, 1823, 7612, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08111644846148196, "compression_ratio": 1.732258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839926162912853e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 52814, "start": 538.18, "end": 541.62, "text": " Right. But it takes forever to run the system that way. It is terribly inefficient.", "tokens": [50867, 1779, 13, 583, 309, 2516, 5680, 281, 1190, 264, 1185, 300, 636, 13, 467, 307, 22903, 43495, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08111644846148196, "compression_ratio": 1.732258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839926162912853e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 52814, "start": 542.08, "end": 550.3, "text": " Exactly. So on the other end of the scale, you have discarded everything except the bare minimum required to execute the function. You've achieved perfect efficiency.", "tokens": [51062, 7587, 13, 407, 322, 264, 661, 917, 295, 264, 4373, 11, 291, 362, 45469, 1203, 3993, 264, 6949, 7285, 4739, 281, 14483, 264, 2445, 13, 509, 600, 11042, 2176, 10493, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08111644846148196, "compression_ratio": 1.732258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839926162912853e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 52814, "start": 550.8, "end": 555.42, "text": " But by optimizing away all that friction, you have strictly maximized your diagnostic uncertainty.", "tokens": [51498, 583, 538, 40425, 1314, 439, 300, 17710, 11, 291, 362, 20792, 5138, 1602, 428, 27897, 15697, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08111644846148196, "compression_ratio": 1.732258064516129, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839926162912853e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 55542, "start": 555.42, "end": 570.1999999999999, "text": " Because if my PDF macro suddenly stops working next year, and all I have is that final code block, I don't know why it broke. Did the image format change? Did the operating system update and break the character recognition?", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 452, 17752, 18887, 5800, 10094, 1364, 958, 1064, 11, 293, 439, 286, 362, 307, 300, 2572, 3089, 3461, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 983, 309, 6902, 13, 2589, 264, 3256, 7877, 1319, 30, 2589, 264, 7447, 1185, 5623, 293, 1821, 264, 2517, 11150, 30, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11728715896606445, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228745777779885e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 55542, "start": 570.3399999999999, "end": 571.0799999999999, "text": " You have no idea.", "tokens": [51111, 509, 362, 572, 1558, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11728715896606445, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228745777779885e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 55542, "start": 571.64, "end": 578.8399999999999, "text": " Because I deleted the history of why I chose those specific tools, I am flying blind. I cannot repair it.", "tokens": [51176, 1436, 286, 22981, 264, 2503, 295, 983, 286, 5111, 729, 2685, 3873, 11, 286, 669, 7137, 6865, 13, 286, 2644, 10535, 309, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11728715896606445, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228745777779885e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 55542, "start": 579.16, "end": 584.48, "text": " Inactability and repairability are mathematically intentioned. They are structurally anti-aligned.", "tokens": [51552, 682, 578, 2310, 293, 10535, 2310, 366, 44003, 7789, 292, 13, 814, 366, 6594, 6512, 6061, 12, 304, 16690, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11728715896606445, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228745777779885e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 58448, "start": 584.48, "end": 591.62, "text": " You cannot push a system toward maximum efficiency without simultaneously blinding your future self to the mechanics of your own system.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2644, 2944, 257, 1185, 7361, 6674, 10493, 1553, 16561, 6865, 278, 428, 2027, 2698, 281, 264, 12939, 295, 428, 1065, 1185, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07760547482690146, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.2744138426848406e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 58448, "start": 591.82, "end": 598.36, "text": " That reframes the entire concept of human expertise for me. I mean, we look up to experts because they are fast, right? Because they are efficient.", "tokens": [50732, 663, 13334, 1632, 264, 2302, 3410, 295, 1952, 11769, 337, 385, 13, 286, 914, 11, 321, 574, 493, 281, 8572, 570, 436, 366, 2370, 11, 558, 30, 1436, 436, 366, 7148, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07760547482690146, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.2744138426848406e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 58448, "start": 598.62, "end": 604.4, "text": " We think of learning as this straight line where you just acquire more and more knowledge until you finally become an expert.", "tokens": [51072, 492, 519, 295, 2539, 382, 341, 2997, 1622, 689, 291, 445, 20001, 544, 293, 544, 3601, 1826, 291, 2721, 1813, 364, 5844, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07760547482690146, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.2744138426848406e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 60440, "start": 604.4, "end": 612.26, "text": " The traditional view treats the expert's brain like a massive, perfectly organized library of accessible facts. You just put more books on the shelf.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5164, 1910, 19566, 264, 5844, 311, 3567, 411, 257, 5994, 11, 6239, 9983, 6405, 295, 9515, 9130, 13, 509, 445, 829, 544, 3642, 322, 264, 15222, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115054276254442, "compression_ratio": 1.4976525821596245, "no_speech_prob": 2.133676048343691e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 60440, "start": 612.38, "end": 612.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50764, 1779, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115054276254442, "compression_ratio": 1.4976525821596245, "no_speech_prob": 2.133676048343691e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 60440, "start": 612.8, "end": 621.98, "text": " But friction's formula is entirely different. It is. Raw history is accumulated, then compression happens, and that yields the skill.", "tokens": [50785, 583, 17710, 311, 8513, 307, 7696, 819, 13, 467, 307, 13, 23732, 2503, 307, 31346, 11, 550, 19355, 2314, 11, 293, 300, 32168, 264, 5389, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115054276254442, "compression_ratio": 1.4976525821596245, "no_speech_prob": 2.133676048343691e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 60440, "start": 622.12, "end": 623.64, "text": " History, compression, skill.", "tokens": [51251, 12486, 11, 19355, 11, 5389, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115054276254442, "compression_ratio": 1.4976525821596245, "no_speech_prob": 2.133676048343691e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 62364, "start": 623.64, "end": 638.3, "text": " Yes. An expert isn't someone who has memorized a mountain of facts. An expert is someone who has accumulated a massive history of failures, corrections, and environmental feedback, and then their brain ran a compression algorithm on all that messy data.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 1107, 5844, 1943, 380, 1580, 567, 575, 46677, 257, 6937, 295, 9130, 13, 1107, 5844, 307, 1580, 567, 575, 31346, 257, 5994, 2503, 295, 20774, 11, 36406, 11, 293, 8303, 5824, 11, 293, 550, 641, 3567, 5872, 257, 19355, 9284, 322, 439, 300, 16191, 1412, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03781620291776435, "compression_ratio": 1.6653225806451613, "no_speech_prob": 1.817938811640718e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 62364, "start": 638.54, "end": 646.72, "text": " Which completely upends how we think about the concept of practice. Like, we have all heard that you need to do deliberate practice to get better at something.", "tokens": [51110, 3013, 2584, 493, 2581, 577, 321, 519, 466, 264, 3410, 295, 3124, 13, 1743, 11, 321, 362, 439, 2198, 300, 291, 643, 281, 360, 30515, 3124, 281, 483, 1101, 412, 746, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03781620291776435, "compression_ratio": 1.6653225806451613, "no_speech_prob": 1.817938811640718e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 64672, "start": 646.72, "end": 648.4, "text": " Right. The 10,000 hours rule.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 1266, 11, 1360, 2496, 4978, 13, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 64672, "start": 648.5, "end": 655.48, "text": " Yeah. You focus on your weak spots, you get coaching, you adjust. But this suggests that practice doesn't actually increase your ability directly.", "tokens": [50454, 865, 13, 509, 1879, 322, 428, 5336, 10681, 11, 291, 483, 15818, 11, 291, 4369, 13, 583, 341, 13409, 300, 3124, 1177, 380, 767, 3488, 428, 3485, 3838, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 64672, "start": 655.7, "end": 656.9200000000001, "text": " Practice does not make you better.", "tokens": [50814, 27904, 775, 406, 652, 291, 1101, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 64672, "start": 657.0600000000001, "end": 657.38, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50882, 3153, 13, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 64672, "start": 657.72, "end": 671.44, "text": " Practice is simply the manufacturing phase. When you sit at a piano and attempt a complex chord, and you fail, and then you adjust your wrist angle and try again, you are manufacturing a repair episode. You're generating raw historical trace.", "tokens": [50915, 27904, 307, 2935, 264, 11096, 5574, 13, 1133, 291, 1394, 412, 257, 9211, 293, 5217, 257, 3997, 14137, 11, 293, 291, 3061, 11, 293, 550, 291, 4369, 428, 15043, 5802, 293, 853, 797, 11, 291, 366, 11096, 257, 10535, 3500, 13, 509, 434, 17746, 8936, 8584, 13508, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 64672, "start": 671.76, "end": 675.5400000000001, "text": " So mindless repetition just builds a flat, useless record.", "tokens": [51617, 407, 1575, 1832, 30432, 445, 15182, 257, 4962, 11, 14115, 2136, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1032907391382643, "compression_ratio": 1.698360655737705, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234905130321775e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 67554, "start": 675.54, "end": 681.14, "text": " Exactly. But deliberate practice builds a deeply textured history of failure and recovery.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 583, 30515, 3124, 15182, 257, 8760, 48656, 2503, 295, 7763, 293, 8597, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0969677201236587, "compression_ratio": 1.6964980544747081, "no_speech_prob": 1.598315338587064e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 67554, "start": 681.6999999999999, "end": 684.98, "text": " But the actual skill doesn't emerge during the practice itself.", "tokens": [50673, 583, 264, 3539, 5389, 1177, 380, 21511, 1830, 264, 3124, 2564, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0969677201236587, "compression_ratio": 1.6964980544747081, "no_speech_prob": 1.598315338587064e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 67554, "start": 685.16, "end": 701.74, "text": " No. The skill emerges later when the brain performs the compression operation on that accumulated history. It folds all those microscopic adjustments into a single fluid motion. But without the rich history of failing, the compression algorithm has absolutely nothing to work with.", "tokens": [50846, 883, 13, 440, 5389, 38965, 1780, 562, 264, 3567, 26213, 264, 19355, 6916, 322, 300, 31346, 2503, 13, 467, 31341, 439, 729, 47897, 18624, 666, 257, 2167, 9113, 5394, 13, 583, 1553, 264, 4593, 2503, 295, 18223, 11, 264, 19355, 9284, 575, 3122, 1825, 281, 589, 365, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0969677201236587, "compression_ratio": 1.6964980544747081, "no_speech_prob": 1.598315338587064e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 70174, "start": 701.74, "end": 716.46, "text": " This makes so much sense of the classic cognitive psychology studies on chess masters. Because we have this cultural image of a chess grandmaster as a, you know, human WUBER computer who can calculate 20 moves ahead, while a novice can only calculate two moves ahead.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 295, 264, 7230, 15605, 15105, 5313, 322, 24122, 19294, 13, 1436, 321, 362, 341, 6988, 3256, 295, 257, 24122, 2697, 21640, 382, 257, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1952, 343, 52, 11074, 3820, 567, 393, 8873, 945, 6067, 2286, 11, 1339, 257, 23883, 573, 393, 787, 8873, 732, 6067, 2286, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0989619917788748, "compression_ratio": 1.4751381215469612, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552036655014367e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 71646, "start": 716.46, "end": 725.9000000000001, "text": " Yet when researchers actually measure this under time pressure, masters and novices search a surprisingly similar number of moves ahead. The master isn't out calculating the novice in real time.", "tokens": [50365, 10890, 562, 10309, 767, 3481, 341, 833, 565, 3321, 11, 19294, 293, 23883, 1473, 3164, 257, 17600, 2531, 1230, 295, 6067, 2286, 13, 440, 4505, 1943, 380, 484, 28258, 264, 23883, 573, 294, 957, 565, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14114454984664918, "compression_ratio": 1.4264705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.393873623294073e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 72590, "start": 725.9, "end": 730.06, "text": " So how are they destroying the novice on the board if they aren't calculating further?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 577, 366, 436, 19926, 264, 23883, 573, 322, 264, 3150, 498, 436, 3212, 380, 28258, 3052, 30, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18117733461311064, "compression_ratio": 1.724890829694323, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722214333046102e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 72590, "start": 730.06, "end": 747.34, "text": " They are pattern matching against a heavily compressed history. When a master looks at a complex board state, they aren't calculating every piece from scratch. They are matching the geometry of the current game against an immense, folded up history of thousands of prior games, blunders, and brilliant traps.", "tokens": [50573, 814, 366, 5102, 14324, 1970, 257, 10950, 30353, 2503, 13, 1133, 257, 4505, 1542, 412, 257, 3997, 3150, 1785, 11, 436, 3212, 380, 28258, 633, 2522, 490, 8459, 13, 814, 366, 14324, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 2190, 1216, 1970, 364, 22920, 11, 23940, 493, 2503, 295, 5383, 295, 4059, 2813, 11, 888, 997, 433, 11, 293, 10248, 24173, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18117733461311064, "compression_ratio": 1.724890829694323, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722214333046102e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 74734, "start": 747.34, "end": 756.62, "text": " They're enacting a compressed operator. Precisely. And the definitive proof of this, which the text highlights, is the famous random board experiment.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 434, 25909, 278, 257, 30353, 12973, 13, 48746, 736, 13, 400, 264, 28152, 8177, 295, 341, 11, 597, 264, 2487, 14254, 11, 307, 264, 4618, 4974, 3150, 5120, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1461498767514772, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762999388719173e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 74734, "start": 756.62, "end": 767.5, "text": " Oh, I love this example. So if you take all the chess pieces and place them on the board completely at random in configurations that violate the rules of the game and would never naturally occur in a real match.", "tokens": [50829, 876, 11, 286, 959, 341, 1365, 13, 407, 498, 291, 747, 439, 264, 24122, 3755, 293, 1081, 552, 322, 264, 3150, 2584, 412, 4974, 294, 31493, 300, 37478, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 1216, 293, 576, 1128, 8195, 5160, 294, 257, 957, 2995, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1461498767514772, "compression_ratio": 1.5404255319148936, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762999388719173e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 76750, "start": 767.5, "end": 775.98, "text": " The master's advantage vanishes completely. Their memory and their ability to calculate the next best move drop almost to the level of an absolute beginner.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4505, 311, 5002, 3161, 16423, 2584, 13, 6710, 4675, 293, 641, 3485, 281, 8873, 264, 958, 1151, 1286, 3270, 1920, 281, 264, 1496, 295, 364, 8236, 22080, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11026790995656709, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015930765112985e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 76750, "start": 775.98, "end": 784.06, "text": " Because their compressed history is suddenly useless, the environment shifted, the patterns they compress no longer apply to this random static.", "tokens": [50789, 1436, 641, 30353, 2503, 307, 5800, 14115, 11, 264, 2823, 18892, 11, 264, 8294, 436, 14778, 572, 2854, 3079, 281, 341, 4974, 13437, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11026790995656709, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015930765112985e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 76750, "start": 784.06, "end": 790.06, "text": " They don't have superior raw processing power. They just have a superior compressed history of actual chess.", "tokens": [51193, 814, 500, 380, 362, 13028, 8936, 9007, 1347, 13, 814, 445, 362, 257, 13028, 30353, 2503, 295, 3539, 24122, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11026790995656709, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015930765112985e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 79006, "start": 790.06, "end": 799.42, "text": " Man, that maps so cleanly onto a spectrum of skill that we all experience moving from the novice to the expert and finally to something much more dangerous.", "tokens": [50365, 2458, 11, 300, 11317, 370, 2541, 356, 3911, 257, 11143, 295, 5389, 300, 321, 439, 1752, 2684, 490, 264, 23883, 573, 281, 264, 5844, 293, 2721, 281, 746, 709, 544, 5795, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10184538618047187, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.64924497669805e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 79006, "start": 799.8199999999999, "end": 802.54, "text": " Let's walk through that progression on the retention lattice.", "tokens": [50853, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 300, 18733, 322, 264, 22871, 34011, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10184538618047187, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.64924497669805e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 79006, "start": 802.54, "end": 815.2199999999999, "text": " Okay, so let's start with the novice. The novice is operating with a very high retained trace. They are very close to the raw history. Think of someone learning to drive a manual transmission car.", "tokens": [50989, 1033, 11, 370, 718, 311, 722, 365, 264, 23883, 573, 13, 440, 23883, 573, 307, 7447, 365, 257, 588, 1090, 33438, 13508, 13, 814, 366, 588, 1998, 281, 264, 8936, 2503, 13, 6557, 295, 1580, 2539, 281, 3332, 257, 9688, 11574, 1032, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10184538618047187, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.64924497669805e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 81522, "start": 815.22, "end": 825.38, "text": " Oh, agonizing. Right. They are incredibly slow to act because they are actively thinking through every intermediate step. They are narrating their own actions out loud.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 623, 266, 3319, 13, 1779, 13, 814, 366, 6252, 2964, 281, 605, 570, 436, 366, 13022, 1953, 807, 633, 19376, 1823, 13, 814, 366, 6397, 990, 641, 1065, 5909, 484, 6588, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 81522, "start": 825.38, "end": 830.98, "text": " Okay, press the clutch, move the stick to second gear, slowly ease off the clutch while pressing the gas.", "tokens": [50873, 1033, 11, 1886, 264, 20597, 11, 1286, 264, 2897, 281, 1150, 7394, 11, 5692, 12708, 766, 264, 20597, 1339, 12417, 264, 4211, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 81522, "start": 830.98, "end": 832.74, "text": " It's so painful to watch. Yeah.", "tokens": [51153, 467, 311, 370, 11697, 281, 1159, 13, 865, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 81522, "start": 832.74, "end": 835.5400000000001, "text": " But there is a hidden superpower in that clunkiness. Okay.", "tokens": [51241, 583, 456, 307, 257, 7633, 45765, 294, 300, 596, 3197, 1324, 13, 1033, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 81522, "start": 835.5400000000001, "end": 840.26, "text": " Because if the car stalls out, the novice's diagnostic uncertainty is very low.", "tokens": [51381, 1436, 498, 264, 1032, 50248, 484, 11, 264, 23883, 573, 311, 27897, 15697, 307, 588, 2295, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 81522, "start": 840.26, "end": 841.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51617, 7587, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11663051200124015, "compression_ratio": 1.6214285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.3669100573654447e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 84114, "start": 841.14, "end": 848.18, "text": " They know exactly which step they messed up because all the steps are fully visible to them. They can say, ah, I let the clutch out too fast. They can fix it.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 458, 2293, 597, 1823, 436, 16507, 493, 570, 439, 264, 4439, 366, 4498, 8974, 281, 552, 13, 814, 393, 584, 11, 3716, 11, 286, 718, 264, 20597, 484, 886, 2370, 13, 814, 393, 3191, 309, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08069599448860466, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.477978004739422e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 84114, "start": 848.18, "end": 857.46, "text": " But as they progress to an expert, they compress that trace. They act quickly. They shift gears instinctively while having a conversation and drinking coffee.", "tokens": [50717, 583, 382, 436, 4205, 281, 364, 5844, 11, 436, 14778, 300, 13508, 13, 814, 605, 2661, 13, 814, 5513, 20915, 16556, 3413, 1339, 1419, 257, 3761, 293, 7583, 4982, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08069599448860466, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.477978004739422e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 84114, "start": 857.46, "end": 857.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51181, 1779, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08069599448860466, "compression_ratio": 1.565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.477978004739422e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 85778, "start": 857.78, "end": 863.14, "text": " But if something feels slightly off in the transmission, they might just feel an intuitive hesitation.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 746, 3417, 4748, 766, 294, 264, 11574, 11, 436, 1062, 445, 841, 364, 21769, 36125, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10926991190229143, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947494839783528e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 85778, "start": 863.86, "end": 873.54, "text": " They might struggle to immediately articulate the exact mechanical failure without stopping, focusing, and mentally digging back into their earlier learning stages.", "tokens": [50669, 814, 1062, 7799, 281, 4258, 30305, 264, 1900, 12070, 7763, 1553, 12767, 11, 8416, 11, 293, 17072, 17343, 646, 666, 641, 3071, 2539, 10232, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10926991190229143, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947494839783528e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 85778, "start": 873.54, "end": 878.8199999999999, "text": " And then we reach the extreme end of the optimization curve, what fiction calls the brittle expert.", "tokens": [51153, 400, 550, 321, 2524, 264, 8084, 917, 295, 264, 19618, 7605, 11, 437, 13266, 5498, 264, 49325, 5844, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10926991190229143, "compression_ratio": 1.581896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947494839783528e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 87882, "start": 878.82, "end": 888.5, "text": " The brittle expert has compressed their history perfectly. They have discarded absolutely all surplus diagnostic data to achieve maximum speed.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 49325, 5844, 575, 30353, 641, 2503, 6239, 13, 814, 362, 45469, 3122, 439, 31019, 27897, 1412, 281, 4584, 6674, 3073, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10006670408611056, "compression_ratio": 1.5967078189300412, "no_speech_prob": 2.493914363216332e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 87882, "start": 888.5, "end": 890.74, "text": " So under normal conditions, they look like a god.", "tokens": [50849, 407, 833, 2710, 4487, 11, 436, 574, 411, 257, 3044, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10006670408611056, "compression_ratio": 1.5967078189300412, "no_speech_prob": 2.493914363216332e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 87882, "start": 890.74, "end": 901.38, "text": " They are the most efficient operators in the room. But the moment there is a distribution shift, the moment the environment changes in a way they haven't seen before, they fail catastrophically.", "tokens": [50961, 814, 366, 264, 881, 7148, 19077, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 583, 264, 1623, 456, 307, 257, 7316, 5513, 11, 264, 1623, 264, 2823, 2962, 294, 257, 636, 436, 2378, 380, 1612, 949, 11, 436, 3061, 28363, 984, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10006670408611056, "compression_ratio": 1.5967078189300412, "no_speech_prob": 2.493914363216332e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 90138, "start": 901.38, "end": 909.62, "text": " This immediately made me think of how we navigate our cities now. Think about the novice driver navigating a new city using a physical paper map.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 4258, 1027, 385, 519, 295, 577, 321, 12350, 527, 6486, 586, 13, 6557, 466, 264, 23883, 573, 6787, 32054, 257, 777, 2307, 1228, 257, 4001, 3035, 4471, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07082126217503701, "compression_ratio": 1.7095709570957096, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040457365822715e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 90138, "start": 909.62, "end": 911.3, "text": " Oh, wow. Yeah. A physical map.", "tokens": [50777, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 865, 13, 316, 4001, 4471, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07082126217503701, "compression_ratio": 1.7095709570957096, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040457365822715e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 90138, "start": 911.3, "end": 919.3, "text": " Right. They are slow. They have to pull over, trace their finger along the grid, look at the topography, and identify landmarks.", "tokens": [50861, 1779, 13, 814, 366, 2964, 13, 814, 362, 281, 2235, 670, 11, 13508, 641, 5984, 2051, 264, 10748, 11, 574, 412, 264, 1192, 5820, 11, 293, 5876, 26962, 82, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07082126217503701, "compression_ratio": 1.7095709570957096, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040457365822715e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 90138, "start": 919.3, "end": 929.78, "text": " But because they are doing that, they know the why of the route. If they hit a massive road closure, they can look at the map and find a detour because they understand the spatial relationships of the whole area.", "tokens": [51261, 583, 570, 436, 366, 884, 300, 11, 436, 458, 264, 983, 295, 264, 7955, 13, 759, 436, 2045, 257, 5994, 3060, 24653, 11, 436, 393, 574, 412, 264, 4471, 293, 915, 257, 1141, 396, 570, 436, 1223, 264, 23598, 6159, 295, 264, 1379, 1859, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07082126217503701, "compression_ratio": 1.7095709570957096, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040457365822715e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 92978, "start": 929.78, "end": 933.62, "text": " They possess a high retained trace of the environment itself.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 17490, 257, 1090, 33438, 13508, 295, 264, 2823, 2564, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11696777824594193, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.50148144785478e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 92978, "start": 933.62, "end": 940.5, "text": " But the brittle expert is the person who just types the address into their phone and blindly follows the blue dot.", "tokens": [50557, 583, 264, 49325, 5844, 307, 264, 954, 567, 445, 3467, 264, 2985, 666, 641, 2593, 293, 47744, 10002, 264, 3344, 5893, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11696777824594193, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.50148144785478e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 92978, "start": 940.5, "end": 941.22, "text": " Guilty.", "tokens": [50901, 2694, 11544, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11696777824594193, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.50148144785478e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 92978, "start": 941.22, "end": 953.38, "text": " Right. We all do it. It is unquestionably the most efficient way to travel. You don't have to think. You just compress the entire complex geography of a city into a single audio command. Turn left in 500 feet.", "tokens": [50937, 1779, 13, 492, 439, 360, 309, 13, 467, 307, 517, 20343, 313, 1188, 264, 881, 7148, 636, 281, 3147, 13, 509, 500, 380, 362, 281, 519, 13, 509, 445, 14778, 264, 2302, 3997, 26695, 295, 257, 2307, 666, 257, 2167, 6278, 5622, 13, 7956, 1411, 294, 5923, 3521, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11696777824594193, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.50148144785478e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 92978, "start": 953.38, "end": 959.3, "text": " But what happens when the GPS glitches or the bridge is out, but the map hasn't updated yet?", "tokens": [51545, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 19462, 23552, 279, 420, 264, 7283, 307, 484, 11, 457, 264, 4471, 6132, 380, 10588, 1939, 30, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11696777824594193, "compression_ratio": 1.591503267973856, "no_speech_prob": 1.50148144785478e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 95930, "start": 959.3, "end": 961.8599999999999, "text": " The brittle expert drives their car straight into a lake.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 49325, 5844, 11754, 641, 1032, 2997, 666, 257, 11001, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394518526588998, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693173315347366e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 95930, "start": 961.8599999999999, "end": 970.9799999999999, "text": " Exactly. They have zero environmental awareness to fall back on. They fail catastrophically because they optimized to weigh their ability to repair their own route.", "tokens": [50493, 7587, 13, 814, 362, 4018, 8303, 8888, 281, 2100, 646, 322, 13, 814, 3061, 28363, 984, 570, 436, 26941, 281, 13843, 641, 3485, 281, 10535, 641, 1065, 7955, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394518526588998, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693173315347366e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 95930, "start": 970.9799999999999, "end": 979.62, "text": " The real warning here is that our modern corporate and cultural definitions of excellence almost always conflate the healthy expert with the brittle expert.", "tokens": [50949, 440, 957, 9164, 510, 307, 300, 527, 4363, 10896, 293, 6988, 21988, 295, 21268, 1920, 1009, 1497, 17593, 264, 4627, 5844, 365, 264, 49325, 5844, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394518526588998, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693173315347366e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 95930, "start": 979.62, "end": 980.9799999999999, "text": " Because they look the same.", "tokens": [51381, 1436, 436, 574, 264, 912, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1394518526588998, "compression_ratio": 1.628, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693173315347366e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 98098, "start": 980.98, "end": 995.94, "text": " Because in routine, stable conditions, they look identical. They are both incredibly fast and productive. You only discover you have hired a brittle expert or that you have become one yourself when the environment shifts and you find yourself sinking in the lake.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 294, 9927, 11, 8351, 4487, 11, 436, 574, 14800, 13, 814, 366, 1293, 6252, 2370, 293, 13304, 13, 509, 787, 4411, 291, 362, 13144, 257, 49325, 5844, 420, 300, 291, 362, 1813, 472, 1803, 562, 264, 2823, 19201, 293, 291, 915, 1803, 28148, 294, 264, 11001, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0608209096468412, "compression_ratio": 1.4692737430167597, "no_speech_prob": 1.783049402570569e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 99594, "start": 995.94, "end": 1010.2800000000001, "text": " Okay. So, human minds are relentlessly good at compressing history into these automatic skills. We are essentially compression engines constantly trying to optimize away the friction of our lives.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 11, 1952, 9634, 366, 34045, 12048, 665, 412, 14778, 278, 2503, 666, 613, 12509, 3942, 13, 492, 366, 4476, 19355, 12982, 6460, 1382, 281, 19719, 1314, 264, 17710, 295, 527, 2909, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12831501338792883, "compression_ratio": 1.724, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042148721211793e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 99594, "start": 1010.5, "end": 1014.3800000000001, "text": " What happens to us psychologically when that compression finishes?", "tokens": [51093, 708, 2314, 281, 505, 41387, 562, 300, 19355, 23615, 30, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12831501338792883, "compression_ratio": 1.724, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042148721211793e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 99594, "start": 1014.62, "end": 1016.12, "text": " When there's nothing left to fold away.", "tokens": [51299, 1133, 456, 311, 1825, 1411, 281, 4860, 1314, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12831501338792883, "compression_ratio": 1.724, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042148721211793e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 99594, "start": 1016.2800000000001, "end": 1023.94, "text": " Yeah. What happens when you get so good at your job or your hobby that there's nothing left to compress? We experience boredom.", "tokens": [51382, 865, 13, 708, 2314, 562, 291, 483, 370, 665, 412, 428, 1691, 420, 428, 18240, 300, 456, 311, 1825, 1411, 281, 14778, 30, 492, 1752, 13521, 298, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12831501338792883, "compression_ratio": 1.724, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042148721211793e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 102394, "start": 1023.94, "end": 1031.46, "text": " We do. But affliction suggests that our everyday folk understanding of what boredom actually is completely misses the mechanism.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 360, 13, 583, 2096, 75, 4105, 13409, 300, 527, 7429, 15748, 3701, 295, 437, 13521, 298, 767, 307, 2584, 29394, 264, 7513, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09715060591697693, "compression_ratio": 1.523404255319149, "no_speech_prob": 1.616894335434993e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 102394, "start": 1031.46, "end": 1042.5, "text": " Because we tend to think boredom is just a lack of stimulation, right? Like a dull room with nothing shiny to look at. Or we think it's too much predictability knowing exactly what your partner is going to say before they say it.", "tokens": [50741, 1436, 321, 3928, 281, 519, 13521, 298, 307, 445, 257, 5011, 295, 37405, 11, 558, 30, 1743, 257, 23471, 1808, 365, 1825, 16997, 281, 574, 412, 13, 1610, 321, 519, 309, 311, 886, 709, 6069, 2310, 5276, 2293, 437, 428, 4975, 307, 516, 281, 584, 949, 436, 584, 309, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09715060591697693, "compression_ratio": 1.523404255319149, "no_speech_prob": 1.616894335434993e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 104250, "start": 1042.5, "end": 1047.14, "text": " Neither of those is the actual variable driving the psychological state of boredom.", "tokens": [50365, 23956, 295, 729, 307, 264, 3539, 7006, 4840, 264, 14346, 1785, 295, 13521, 298, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25055619290000514, "compression_ratio": 1.064102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037884554067407e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 104714, "start": 1047.14, "end": 1056.5600000000002, "text": " The theory here actually draws on concepts from artificial intelligence, specifically the work of J\u00fcrgen Schmid Hooper, who developed formal models of curiosity.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5261, 510, 767, 20045, 322, 10392, 490, 11677, 7599, 11, 4682, 264, 589, 295, 508, 1655, 1766, 2065, 25394, 3631, 7192, 11, 567, 4743, 9860, 5245, 295, 18769, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15748816567498283, "compression_ratio": 1.5176991150442478, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108492136348353e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 104714, "start": 1057.5600000000002, "end": 1068.16, "text": " The core metric is expected marginal compression gain, or EMCG. It is basically the rate at which your internal predictive model of the world is improving.", "tokens": [50886, 440, 4965, 20678, 307, 5176, 16885, 19355, 6052, 11, 420, 16237, 34, 38, 13, 467, 307, 1936, 264, 3314, 412, 597, 428, 6920, 35521, 2316, 295, 264, 1002, 307, 11470, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15748816567498283, "compression_ratio": 1.5176991150442478, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108492136348353e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 104714, "start": 1068.3600000000001, "end": 1069.1200000000001, "text": " The rate of compression.", "tokens": [51426, 440, 3314, 295, 19355, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15748816567498283, "compression_ratio": 1.5176991150442478, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108492136348353e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 106912, "start": 1069.12, "end": 1080.34, "text": " Precisely. It is a measurement that asks your brain, if I interact with this environment, will it help me compress my history any further? Will I learn something that simplifies my understanding?", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 467, 307, 257, 13160, 300, 8962, 428, 3567, 11, 498, 286, 4648, 365, 341, 2823, 11, 486, 309, 854, 385, 14778, 452, 2503, 604, 3052, 30, 3099, 286, 1466, 746, 300, 6883, 11221, 452, 3701, 30, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09947533940159997, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.416163518917768e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 106912, "start": 1080.6, "end": 1081.26, "text": " Okay, I follow.", "tokens": [50939, 1033, 11, 286, 1524, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09947533940159997, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.416163518917768e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 106912, "start": 1081.82, "end": 1092.3799999999999, "text": " Boredom is the psychological state where that rate of improvement hits absolute zero. Your brain realizes, I cannot squeeze any more efficiency or structural understanding out of this situation.", "tokens": [51000, 363, 2769, 298, 307, 264, 14346, 1785, 689, 300, 3314, 295, 10444, 8664, 8236, 4018, 13, 2260, 3567, 29316, 11, 286, 2644, 13578, 604, 544, 10493, 420, 15067, 3701, 484, 295, 341, 2590, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09947533940159997, "compression_ratio": 1.573643410852713, "no_speech_prob": 1.416163518917768e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 109238, "start": 1092.38, "end": 1102.5, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting. Because if boredom is just that rate hitting zero, it explains why we can feel profoundly bored in two entirely opposite situations.", "tokens": [50365, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 1436, 498, 13521, 298, 307, 445, 300, 3314, 8850, 4018, 11, 309, 13948, 983, 321, 393, 841, 39954, 13521, 294, 732, 7696, 6182, 6851, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08430339569269224, "compression_ratio": 1.5630252100840336, "no_speech_prob": 1.555336805528218e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 109238, "start": 1102.7, "end": 1110.42, "text": " Exactly. There are two types of saturation. The first is mastery saturation. This is when the puzzle is completely solved, you have fully compressed the domain.", "tokens": [50881, 7587, 13, 821, 366, 732, 3467, 295, 27090, 13, 440, 700, 307, 37951, 27090, 13, 639, 307, 562, 264, 12805, 307, 2584, 13041, 11, 291, 362, 4498, 30353, 264, 9274, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08430339569269224, "compression_ratio": 1.5630252100840336, "no_speech_prob": 1.555336805528218e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 109238, "start": 1110.64, "end": 1112.3000000000002, "text": " Like playing tic-tac-toe as an adult.", "tokens": [51278, 1743, 2433, 256, 299, 12, 83, 326, 12, 1353, 68, 382, 364, 5075, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08430339569269224, "compression_ratio": 1.5630252100840336, "no_speech_prob": 1.555336805528218e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 111230, "start": 1112.3, "end": 1125.62, "text": " Perfect example. You know every possible permutation. Playing another game yields absolutely no new insight. Your model is flawless, so your expected marginal compression game is zero. You are deeply bored.", "tokens": [50365, 10246, 1365, 13, 509, 458, 633, 1944, 4784, 11380, 13, 24801, 1071, 1216, 32168, 3122, 572, 777, 11269, 13, 2260, 2316, 307, 45693, 11, 370, 428, 5176, 16885, 19355, 1216, 307, 4018, 13, 509, 366, 8760, 13521, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09433994060609399, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 3.924687831668994e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 111230, "start": 1126.02, "end": 1129.3, "text": " But the second type of boredom looks completely different from the outside.", "tokens": [51051, 583, 264, 1150, 2010, 295, 13521, 298, 1542, 2584, 819, 490, 264, 2380, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09433994060609399, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 3.924687831668994e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 111230, "start": 1129.56, "end": 1137.6399999999999, "text": " Right. That is noise saturation. This occurs when the environment is pure randomness or just incredibly dense static.", "tokens": [51228, 1779, 13, 663, 307, 5658, 27090, 13, 639, 11843, 562, 264, 2823, 307, 6075, 4974, 1287, 420, 445, 6252, 18011, 13437, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09433994060609399, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 3.924687831668994e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 113764, "start": 1137.64, "end": 1144.14, "text": " Imagine trying to predict the outcome of a perfectly balanced roulette wheel by staring at it for 10 hours.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 1382, 281, 6069, 264, 9700, 295, 257, 6239, 13902, 18450, 36563, 5589, 538, 18043, 412, 309, 337, 1266, 2496, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07716949132024026, "compression_ratio": 1.5827338129496402, "no_speech_prob": 1.7081994456089045e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 113764, "start": 1144.5600000000002, "end": 1146.6000000000001, "text": " Or watching a television tuned to dead air.", "tokens": [50711, 1610, 1976, 257, 8815, 10870, 281, 3116, 1988, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07716949132024026, "compression_ratio": 1.5827338129496402, "no_speech_prob": 1.7081994456089045e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 113764, "start": 1146.74, "end": 1154.1000000000001, "text": " Yes. No matter how much data you consume, your brain cannot compress it into a predictive model because there is no underlying structure to learn.", "tokens": [50820, 1079, 13, 883, 1871, 577, 709, 1412, 291, 14732, 11, 428, 3567, 2644, 14778, 309, 666, 257, 35521, 2316, 570, 456, 307, 572, 14217, 3877, 281, 1466, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07716949132024026, "compression_ratio": 1.5827338129496402, "no_speech_prob": 1.7081994456089045e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 113764, "start": 1154.46, "end": 1161.92, "text": " The material is fundamentally uncompressible. So your brain realizes it can't make any progress, the rate hits zero, and again you are bored.", "tokens": [51206, 440, 2527, 307, 17879, 8585, 11637, 964, 13, 407, 428, 3567, 29316, 309, 393, 380, 652, 604, 4205, 11, 264, 3314, 8664, 4018, 11, 293, 797, 291, 366, 13521, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07716949132024026, "compression_ratio": 1.5827338129496402, "no_speech_prob": 1.7081994456089045e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 116192, "start": 1161.92, "end": 1172.6200000000001, "text": " The boredom of the completely solved puzzle and the boredom of pure static. They feel subjectively identical to us, a kind of restless disengagement, but they require completely different solutions.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 13521, 298, 295, 264, 2584, 13041, 12805, 293, 264, 13521, 298, 295, 6075, 13437, 13, 814, 841, 3983, 3413, 14800, 281, 505, 11, 257, 733, 295, 45451, 717, 1501, 11129, 11, 457, 436, 3651, 2584, 819, 6547, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10773214667734474, "compression_ratio": 1.6404494382022472, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687653421251005e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 116192, "start": 1172.8000000000002, "end": 1176.78, "text": " And this framework also pinpoints exactly where the opposite of boredom lives.", "tokens": [50909, 400, 341, 8388, 611, 5447, 20552, 2293, 689, 264, 6182, 295, 13521, 298, 2909, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10773214667734474, "compression_ratio": 1.6404494382022472, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687653421251005e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 116192, "start": 1177.02, "end": 1177.72, "text": " The flow state.", "tokens": [51120, 440, 3095, 1785, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10773214667734474, "compression_ratio": 1.6404494382022472, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687653421251005e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 116192, "start": 1177.9, "end": 1185.26, "text": " Right. Mihaly sticks at Mihaly's concept of flow, that intoxicating feeling of being completely immersed in a task where you lose track of time.", "tokens": [51164, 1779, 13, 48168, 5222, 12518, 412, 48168, 5222, 311, 3410, 295, 3095, 11, 300, 40809, 30541, 2633, 295, 885, 2584, 35416, 294, 257, 5633, 689, 291, 3624, 2837, 295, 565, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10773214667734474, "compression_ratio": 1.6404494382022472, "no_speech_prob": 1.8687653421251005e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 118526, "start": 1185.26, "end": 1191.34, "text": " Mathematically, flow is located in the positive interior between mastery and noise.", "tokens": [50365, 15776, 40197, 11, 3095, 307, 6870, 294, 264, 3353, 10636, 1296, 37951, 293, 5658, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297393692864312, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.681313833816478e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 118526, "start": 1191.62, "end": 1193.18, "text": " Where active compression is happening.", "tokens": [50683, 2305, 4967, 19355, 307, 2737, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297393692864312, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.681313833816478e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 118526, "start": 1193.26, "end": 1197.76, "text": " Exactly. Flow is the state where compression progress is happening at an optimal rate.", "tokens": [50765, 7587, 13, 32792, 307, 264, 1785, 689, 19355, 4205, 307, 2737, 412, 364, 16252, 3314, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297393692864312, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.681313833816478e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 118526, "start": 1198.0, "end": 1201.42, "text": " You haven't mastered the domain yet, but it's not random noise either.", "tokens": [51002, 509, 2378, 380, 38686, 264, 9274, 1939, 11, 457, 309, 311, 406, 4974, 5658, 2139, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297393692864312, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.681313833816478e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 118526, "start": 1201.78, "end": 1210.14, "text": " You are actively folding new challenging history into a better model, and our brains reward that process with a feeling of deep engagement.", "tokens": [51191, 509, 366, 13022, 25335, 777, 7595, 2503, 666, 257, 1101, 2316, 11, 293, 527, 15442, 7782, 300, 1399, 365, 257, 2633, 295, 2452, 8742, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297393692864312, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.681313833816478e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 121014, "start": 1210.14, "end": 1221.16, "text": " Okay, so wait. If I'm stuck in mastery saturation, let's say I am 10 years into my career, I could do my job with my eyes closed, and I am completely mind-numbingly bored at my desk.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 1699, 13, 759, 286, 478, 5541, 294, 37951, 27090, 11, 718, 311, 584, 286, 669, 1266, 924, 666, 452, 3988, 11, 286, 727, 360, 452, 1691, 365, 452, 2575, 5395, 11, 293, 286, 669, 2584, 1575, 12, 77, 2860, 12163, 13521, 412, 452, 10026, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 121014, "start": 1221.5600000000002, "end": 1225.5200000000002, "text": " Do I just need to quit? How do I get EMCG back without upending my life?", "tokens": [50936, 1144, 286, 445, 643, 281, 10366, 30, 1012, 360, 286, 483, 16237, 34, 38, 646, 1553, 493, 2029, 452, 993, 30, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 121014, "start": 1225.96, "end": 1231.18, "text": " Fletian outlines three very specific mechanisms to cure mastery saturation without abandoning the environment.", "tokens": [51156, 479, 2631, 952, 40125, 1045, 588, 2685, 15902, 281, 13698, 37951, 27090, 1553, 9072, 278, 264, 2823, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 121014, "start": 1231.3200000000002, "end": 1231.5600000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51424, 1033, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 121014, "start": 1231.74, "end": 1235.2800000000002, "text": " The first one sounds completely counterproductive. Voluntary handicapping.", "tokens": [51445, 440, 700, 472, 3263, 2584, 5682, 14314, 20221, 13, 8911, 2760, 822, 31369, 10534, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 121014, "start": 1235.3600000000001, "end": 1236.14, "text": " Yeah, it sounds like self-sabotage.", "tokens": [51626, 865, 11, 309, 3263, 411, 2698, 12, 82, 455, 310, 609, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0838254635150616, "compression_ratio": 1.5382165605095541, "no_speech_prob": 2.150740523176875e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 123614, "start": 1236.14, "end": 1242.0400000000002, "text": " It is intentional restriction. You force yourself to use a strictly weaker set of tools.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 21935, 29529, 13, 509, 3464, 1803, 281, 764, 257, 20792, 24286, 992, 295, 3873, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390542180914628, "compression_ratio": 1.7641921397379912, "no_speech_prob": 1.868301520435711e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 123614, "start": 1242.38, "end": 1246.6000000000001, "text": " You force yourself to do the complex math by hand instead of using the software.", "tokens": [50677, 509, 3464, 1803, 281, 360, 264, 3997, 5221, 538, 1011, 2602, 295, 1228, 264, 4722, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390542180914628, "compression_ratio": 1.7641921397379912, "no_speech_prob": 1.868301520435711e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 123614, "start": 1247.1200000000001, "end": 1251.5600000000002, "text": " You force yourself to write the code without relying on the high-level autocomplete libraries.", "tokens": [50914, 509, 3464, 1803, 281, 2464, 264, 3089, 1553, 24140, 322, 264, 1090, 12, 12418, 45833, 298, 17220, 15148, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390542180914628, "compression_ratio": 1.7641921397379912, "no_speech_prob": 1.868301520435711e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 123614, "start": 1251.94, "end": 1254.5600000000002, "text": " You try to paint the portrait using only three colors.", "tokens": [51155, 509, 853, 281, 4225, 264, 17126, 1228, 787, 1045, 4577, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390542180914628, "compression_ratio": 1.7641921397379912, "no_speech_prob": 1.868301520435711e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 123614, "start": 1255.3200000000002, "end": 1259.8200000000002, "text": " So if breaking my own tools is one way to cure boredom, why does that actually work?", "tokens": [51324, 407, 498, 7697, 452, 1065, 3873, 307, 472, 636, 281, 13698, 13521, 298, 11, 983, 775, 300, 767, 589, 30, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390542180914628, "compression_ratio": 1.7641921397379912, "no_speech_prob": 1.868301520435711e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 125982, "start": 1259.82, "end": 1267.32, "text": " Because if I'm bored at work, making my job artificially harder seems like it would just make me angry, not engaged.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 286, 478, 13521, 412, 589, 11, 1455, 452, 1691, 39905, 2270, 6081, 2544, 411, 309, 576, 445, 652, 385, 6884, 11, 406, 8237, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14081481834510703, "compression_ratio": 1.5734597156398105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2155005734565405e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 125982, "start": 1267.7, "end": 1273.1799999999998, "text": " It works because you haven't changed the environment, but you have artificially destroyed your perfect compression.", "tokens": [50759, 467, 1985, 570, 291, 2378, 380, 3105, 264, 2823, 11, 457, 291, 362, 39905, 2270, 8937, 428, 2176, 19355, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14081481834510703, "compression_ratio": 1.5734597156398105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2155005734565405e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 125982, "start": 1273.84, "end": 1277.8, "text": " By restricting your tools, the domain becomes difficult again.", "tokens": [51066, 3146, 1472, 37714, 428, 3873, 11, 264, 9274, 3643, 2252, 797, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14081481834510703, "compression_ratio": 1.5734597156398105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2155005734565405e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 125982, "start": 1278.1599999999999, "end": 1279.96, "text": " It regains its uncompressed texture.", "tokens": [51282, 467, 1121, 2315, 1080, 8585, 79, 3805, 8091, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14081481834510703, "compression_ratio": 1.5734597156398105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2155005734565405e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 127996, "start": 1279.96, "end": 1288.04, "text": " You have essentially demoted yourself from a brittle expert back to an earlier stage where you have to build new history and find new workarounds.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 4476, 1371, 23325, 1803, 490, 257, 49325, 5844, 646, 281, 364, 3071, 3233, 689, 291, 362, 281, 1322, 777, 2503, 293, 915, 777, 589, 289, 4432, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 127996, "start": 1288.3400000000001, "end": 1290.56, "text": " Your rate of learning becomes positive again.", "tokens": [50784, 2260, 3314, 295, 2539, 3643, 3353, 797, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 127996, "start": 1290.92, "end": 1293.14, "text": " This is exactly what speedrunners in video games do.", "tokens": [50913, 639, 307, 2293, 437, 3073, 12997, 2999, 294, 960, 2813, 360, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 127996, "start": 1293.24, "end": 1294.6200000000001, "text": " Oh, yeah. That's a great comparison.", "tokens": [51029, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 663, 311, 257, 869, 9660, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 127996, "start": 1294.8600000000001, "end": 1295.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51110, 1779, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 127996, "start": 1295.6200000000001, "end": 1301.64, "text": " Someone masters Super Mario, plays it thousands of times, and hits mastery saturation.", "tokens": [51148, 8734, 19294, 4548, 9343, 11, 5749, 309, 5383, 295, 1413, 11, 293, 8664, 37951, 27090, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14988043020059774, "compression_ratio": 1.5284552845528456, "no_speech_prob": 1.635620892198597e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 130164, "start": 1301.64, "end": 1306.38, "text": " So, to cure their boredom, they invent an insane handicap.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 281, 13698, 641, 13521, 298, 11, 436, 7962, 364, 10838, 45975, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 130164, "start": 1307.2800000000002, "end": 1312.88, "text": " They try to beat the game blindfolded, or using a steering wheel controller instead of a gamepad.", "tokens": [50647, 814, 853, 281, 4224, 264, 1216, 44846, 292, 11, 420, 1228, 257, 14823, 5589, 10561, 2602, 295, 257, 1216, 13647, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 130164, "start": 1313.2800000000002, "end": 1318.22, "text": " The game itself is mastered, so they handicap the interface to make the compression process active again.", "tokens": [50947, 440, 1216, 2564, 307, 38686, 11, 370, 436, 45975, 264, 9226, 281, 652, 264, 19355, 1399, 4967, 797, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 130164, "start": 1318.38, "end": 1321.0600000000002, "text": " Exactly. They are generating new compression gain.", "tokens": [51202, 7587, 13, 814, 366, 17746, 777, 19355, 6052, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 130164, "start": 1321.26, "end": 1323.68, "text": " Okay, what if I can't do that?", "tokens": [51346, 1033, 11, 437, 498, 286, 393, 380, 360, 300, 30, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 130164, "start": 1324.14, "end": 1328.8000000000002, "text": " What if my boss won't let me uninstall my software to make my job artificially harder?", "tokens": [51490, 708, 498, 452, 5741, 1582, 380, 718, 385, 517, 40166, 452, 4722, 281, 652, 452, 1691, 39905, 2270, 6081, 30, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13897336977664557, "compression_ratio": 1.6576923076923078, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667000253210105e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 132880, "start": 1328.8, "end": 1331.94, "text": " Then you move to the second mechanism, didactic reframing.", "tokens": [50365, 1396, 291, 1286, 281, 264, 1150, 7513, 11, 630, 19892, 1895, 2356, 278, 13, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 132880, "start": 1332.34, "end": 1337.48, "text": " This involves asking a completely different structural question of the exact same historical data.", "tokens": [50542, 639, 11626, 3365, 257, 2584, 819, 15067, 1168, 295, 264, 1900, 912, 8584, 1412, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 132880, "start": 1337.6, "end": 1338.0, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [50805, 1743, 437, 30, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 132880, "start": 1338.1399999999999, "end": 1343.58, "text": " If you execute the same mundane procedure every day at work, instead of just trying to get it done, you change the lens.", "tokens": [50832, 759, 291, 14483, 264, 912, 43497, 10747, 633, 786, 412, 589, 11, 2602, 295, 445, 1382, 281, 483, 309, 1096, 11, 291, 1319, 264, 6765, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 132880, "start": 1344.04, "end": 1347.98, "text": " You start asking, why did this specific corporate procedure evolve this way?", "tokens": [51127, 509, 722, 3365, 11, 983, 630, 341, 2685, 10896, 10747, 16693, 341, 636, 30, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 132880, "start": 1348.1, "end": 1352.8999999999999, "text": " Or, what would happen to the whole supply chain if I altered this one input variable by 5%?", "tokens": [51330, 1610, 11, 437, 576, 1051, 281, 264, 1379, 5847, 5021, 498, 286, 28783, 341, 472, 4846, 7006, 538, 1025, 4, 30, 51570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 132880, "start": 1353.18, "end": 1355.8, "text": " You multiply the number of things you were trying to solve for.", "tokens": [51584, 509, 12972, 264, 1230, 295, 721, 291, 645, 1382, 281, 5039, 337, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11484973938738713, "compression_ratio": 1.6415094339622642, "no_speech_prob": 1.405017053222879e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 135580, "start": 1355.8, "end": 1362.22, "text": " You stop trying to compress the task just for speed, and you start trying to compress it for resilience or historical understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1590, 1382, 281, 14778, 264, 5633, 445, 337, 3073, 11, 293, 291, 722, 1382, 281, 14778, 309, 337, 19980, 420, 8584, 3701, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 135580, "start": 1362.68, "end": 1367.52, "text": " You are mining the exact same rock, but you are extracting a completely different mineral.", "tokens": [50709, 509, 366, 15512, 264, 1900, 912, 3727, 11, 457, 291, 366, 49844, 257, 2584, 819, 21630, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 135580, "start": 1367.7, "end": 1368.22, "text": " I like that.", "tokens": [50960, 286, 411, 300, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 135580, "start": 1368.34, "end": 1372.36, "text": " And if that still doesn't work, there's a third mechanism, metacompression.", "tokens": [50992, 400, 498, 300, 920, 1177, 380, 589, 11, 456, 311, 257, 2636, 7513, 11, 1131, 326, 8586, 2775, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 135580, "start": 1372.6399999999999, "end": 1373.94, "text": " Finding the common denominator.", "tokens": [51207, 31947, 264, 2689, 20687, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 135580, "start": 1374.08, "end": 1374.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51279, 1079, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 135580, "start": 1374.74, "end": 1381.26, "text": " This is when you take multiple separate skills that have all independently reached mastery saturation, and you try to compress them together.", "tokens": [51312, 639, 307, 562, 291, 747, 3866, 4994, 3942, 300, 362, 439, 21761, 6488, 37951, 27090, 11, 293, 291, 853, 281, 14778, 552, 1214, 13, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13417226774198515, "compression_ratio": 1.693103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.2994348435810266e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 138126, "start": 1381.26, "end": 1389.42, "text": " You ask, what does my deep expertise in playing the piano have in common with my expertise in managing a team of software engineers?", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1029, 11, 437, 775, 452, 2452, 11769, 294, 2433, 264, 9211, 362, 294, 2689, 365, 452, 11769, 294, 11642, 257, 1469, 295, 4722, 11955, 30, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10683225656484628, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127036992815257e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 138126, "start": 1389.72, "end": 1392.34, "text": " You look for the shared structural constraints one level up.", "tokens": [50788, 509, 574, 337, 264, 5507, 15067, 18491, 472, 1496, 493, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10683225656484628, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127036992815257e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 138126, "start": 1392.46, "end": 1392.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50925, 7587, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10683225656484628, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127036992815257e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 138126, "start": 1393.36, "end": 1402.48, "text": " The individual skills are boring to execute, but finding the hidden meta-level translation between them is a wide-open frontier for new learning.", "tokens": [50970, 440, 2609, 3942, 366, 9989, 281, 14483, 11, 457, 5006, 264, 7633, 19616, 12, 12418, 12853, 1296, 552, 307, 257, 4874, 12, 15752, 35853, 337, 777, 2539, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10683225656484628, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127036992815257e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 140248, "start": 1402.48, "end": 1408.32, "text": " But there is a massive, flashing warning light attached to all three of these cures.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 456, 307, 257, 5994, 11, 31049, 9164, 1442, 8570, 281, 439, 1045, 295, 613, 269, 1303, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10106673039181131, "compression_ratio": 1.532967032967033, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 140248, "start": 1408.88, "end": 1416.56, "text": " None of this, not handicapping, not reframing, not metacompression, none of it is possible if you do not have unstructured time.", "tokens": [50685, 14492, 295, 341, 11, 406, 31369, 10534, 11, 406, 1895, 2356, 278, 11, 406, 1131, 326, 8586, 2775, 11, 6022, 295, 309, 307, 1944, 498, 291, 360, 406, 362, 18799, 46847, 565, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10106673039181131, "compression_ratio": 1.532967032967033, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 140248, "start": 1416.72, "end": 1419.46, "text": " This might be the most vital psychological insight in the essays.", "tokens": [51077, 639, 1062, 312, 264, 881, 11707, 14346, 11269, 294, 264, 35123, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10106673039181131, "compression_ratio": 1.532967032967033, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191784462353919e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 141946, "start": 1419.46, "end": 1435.42, "text": " If you are constantly fed prepackaged novelties, if you spend every spare minute in line at the grocery store scrolling a social media feed, or if every hour of your weekend is ruthlessly scheduled with structured entertainment, you are never building raw history.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 366, 6460, 4636, 2666, 501, 2980, 7613, 6097, 11, 498, 291, 3496, 633, 13798, 3456, 294, 1622, 412, 264, 14410, 3531, 29053, 257, 2093, 3021, 3154, 11, 420, 498, 633, 1773, 295, 428, 6711, 307, 38225, 12048, 15678, 365, 18519, 12393, 11, 291, 366, 1128, 2390, 8936, 2503, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04789563092318448, "compression_ratio": 1.5085714285714287, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040499649707442e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 143542, "start": 1435.42, "end": 1442.0600000000002, "text": " An algorithmically driven feed provides a relentless stream of new states, new shiny objects.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 9284, 984, 9555, 3154, 6417, 257, 46136, 4309, 295, 777, 4368, 11, 777, 16997, 6565, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 143542, "start": 1442.6200000000001, "end": 1451.48, "text": " But because the context switches so rapidly and requires absolutely zero active engagement from you, none of it is retained long enough to be folded into a stable model.", "tokens": [50725, 583, 570, 264, 4319, 19458, 370, 12910, 293, 7029, 3122, 4018, 4967, 8742, 490, 291, 11, 6022, 295, 309, 307, 33438, 938, 1547, 281, 312, 23940, 666, 257, 8351, 2316, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 143542, "start": 1451.68, "end": 1452.3000000000002, "text": " It's just noise.", "tokens": [51178, 467, 311, 445, 5658, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 143542, "start": 1452.5600000000002, "end": 1457.1200000000001, "text": " It is. You consume the novelty, you discard it instantly, and you demand the next one.", "tokens": [51222, 467, 307, 13, 509, 14732, 264, 44805, 11, 291, 31597, 309, 13518, 11, 293, 291, 4733, 264, 958, 472, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 143542, "start": 1457.52, "end": 1460.94, "text": " Your brain is never allowed to perform the compression operation itself.", "tokens": [51470, 2260, 3567, 307, 1128, 4350, 281, 2042, 264, 19355, 6916, 2564, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 143542, "start": 1461.1200000000001, "end": 1464.3000000000002, "text": " You outsource the cure for your boredom to an external machine.", "tokens": [51650, 509, 14758, 2948, 264, 13698, 337, 428, 13521, 298, 281, 364, 8320, 3479, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10323659508629182, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756309439621477e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 146430, "start": 1464.3, "end": 1472.48, "text": " And a mind that has never been forced to sit with an unstructured, boring interval is a mind that has never had to construct its own compression from scratch.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 257, 1575, 300, 575, 1128, 668, 7579, 281, 1394, 365, 364, 18799, 46847, 11, 9989, 15035, 307, 257, 1575, 300, 575, 1128, 632, 281, 7690, 1080, 1065, 19355, 490, 8459, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 146430, "start": 1472.94, "end": 1475.24, "text": " They have no practice generating their own engagement.", "tokens": [50797, 814, 362, 572, 3124, 17746, 641, 1065, 8742, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 146430, "start": 1476.0, "end": 1480.1599999999999, "text": " Fliction argues that unstructured time is not the absence of a solution to boredom.", "tokens": [50950, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 18799, 46847, 565, 307, 406, 264, 17145, 295, 257, 3827, 281, 13521, 298, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 146430, "start": 1480.3999999999999, "end": 1484.74, "text": " It is the fundamental raw material that any lasting solution must be built from.", "tokens": [51170, 467, 307, 264, 8088, 8936, 2527, 300, 604, 20714, 3827, 1633, 312, 3094, 490, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 146430, "start": 1484.98, "end": 1490.98, "text": " If you never let yourself be bored, you completely lose the internal capacity to cure your own boredom.", "tokens": [51399, 759, 291, 1128, 718, 1803, 312, 13521, 11, 291, 2584, 3624, 264, 6920, 6042, 281, 13698, 428, 1065, 13521, 298, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 146430, "start": 1491.7, "end": 1492.52, "text": " You become dependent.", "tokens": [51735, 509, 1813, 12334, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13560235183850855, "compression_ratio": 1.7746478873239437, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258550475522497e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 149252, "start": 1492.52, "end": 1495.78, "text": " That is a heavy structural necessity to sit with.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 4676, 15067, 24217, 281, 1394, 365, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14370012283325195, "compression_ratio": 1.4593301435406698, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760981487618954e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 149252, "start": 1495.98, "end": 1499.86, "text": " You cannot build a complex skill without the raw, uncompressed history.", "tokens": [50538, 509, 2644, 1322, 257, 3997, 5389, 1553, 264, 8936, 11, 8585, 79, 3805, 2503, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14370012283325195, "compression_ratio": 1.4593301435406698, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760981487618954e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 149252, "start": 1500.1, "end": 1500.9, "text": " All right, let's zoom out.", "tokens": [50744, 1057, 558, 11, 718, 311, 8863, 484, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14370012283325195, "compression_ratio": 1.4593301435406698, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760981487618954e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 149252, "start": 1501.44, "end": 1504.74, "text": " So far, we've been intensely focused on a single agent, right?", "tokens": [50811, 407, 1400, 11, 321, 600, 668, 43235, 5178, 322, 257, 2167, 9461, 11, 558, 30, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14370012283325195, "compression_ratio": 1.4593301435406698, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760981487618954e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 149252, "start": 1505.12, "end": 1510.96, "text": " One person learning a skill, one programmer writing a macro, one mind trying not to be bored.", "tokens": [50995, 1485, 954, 2539, 257, 5389, 11, 472, 32116, 3579, 257, 18887, 11, 472, 1575, 1382, 406, 281, 312, 13521, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14370012283325195, "compression_ratio": 1.4593301435406698, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760981487618954e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 151096, "start": 1510.96, "end": 1513.56, "text": " But none of us exist in a vacuum.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 6022, 295, 505, 2514, 294, 257, 14224, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14645902500596159, "compression_ratio": 1.5518672199170125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104562987675266e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 151096, "start": 1514.3400000000001, "end": 1524.1200000000001, "text": " What happens when millions of individual compressed histories, our habits, our corporate policies, our building codes, our legal systems, are forced to share the exact same space and interact?", "tokens": [50534, 708, 2314, 562, 6803, 295, 2609, 30353, 30631, 11, 527, 14100, 11, 527, 10896, 7657, 11, 527, 2390, 14211, 11, 527, 5089, 3652, 11, 366, 7579, 281, 2073, 264, 1900, 912, 1901, 293, 4648, 30, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14645902500596159, "compression_ratio": 1.5518672199170125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104562987675266e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 151096, "start": 1524.26, "end": 1526.1000000000001, "text": " This moves us into the dynamics of ecology.", "tokens": [51030, 639, 6067, 505, 666, 264, 15679, 295, 39683, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14645902500596159, "compression_ratio": 1.5518672199170125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104562987675266e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 151096, "start": 1526.64, "end": 1530.6000000000001, "text": " When rules and constraints collide, they don't just stack neatly like bricks.", "tokens": [51149, 1133, 4474, 293, 18491, 49093, 11, 436, 500, 380, 445, 8630, 36634, 411, 25497, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14645902500596159, "compression_ratio": 1.5518672199170125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104562987675266e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 151096, "start": 1530.76, "end": 1531.88, "text": " They react to each other.", "tokens": [51355, 814, 4515, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14645902500596159, "compression_ratio": 1.5518672199170125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104562987675266e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 153188, "start": 1531.88, "end": 1538.38, "text": " Before we dive into the math of this, I want to be super clear with you about the examples we're going to use here.", "tokens": [50365, 4546, 321, 9192, 666, 264, 5221, 295, 341, 11, 286, 528, 281, 312, 1687, 1850, 365, 291, 466, 264, 5110, 321, 434, 516, 281, 764, 510, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1273263881081029, "compression_ratio": 1.5874439461883407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897464109697947e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 153188, "start": 1539.18, "end": 1546.3200000000002, "text": " The source material uses constitutional law, statutory law, and physical policies to illustrate how large systems of rules behave.", "tokens": [50730, 440, 4009, 2527, 4960, 20176, 2101, 11, 42037, 2101, 11, 293, 4001, 7657, 281, 23221, 577, 2416, 3652, 295, 4474, 15158, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1273263881081029, "compression_ratio": 1.5874439461883407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897464109697947e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 153188, "start": 1546.48, "end": 1552.3600000000001, "text": " And we're looking at these purely as structural examples of interacting systems exactly as the author does.", "tokens": [51095, 400, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 613, 17491, 382, 15067, 5110, 295, 18017, 3652, 2293, 382, 264, 3793, 775, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1273263881081029, "compression_ratio": 1.5874439461883407, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897464109697947e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 155236, "start": 1552.36, "end": 1553.1, "text": " Yes, absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 3122, 13, 50402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 155236, "start": 1553.4599999999998, "end": 1557.6399999999999, "text": " We are not taking a stance on real-world governance or economic theory.", "tokens": [50420, 492, 366, 406, 1940, 257, 21033, 322, 957, 12, 13217, 17449, 420, 4836, 5261, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 155236, "start": 1558.1799999999998, "end": 1560.4799999999998, "text": " We aren't taking political sides, left, right, whatever.", "tokens": [50656, 492, 3212, 380, 1940, 3905, 4881, 11, 1411, 11, 558, 11, 2035, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 155236, "start": 1560.86, "end": 1567.9399999999998, "text": " We are simply examining the geometry of how rules behave when you lock them in a room together, reporting impartially on the text.", "tokens": [50790, 492, 366, 2935, 34662, 264, 18426, 295, 577, 4474, 15158, 562, 291, 4017, 552, 294, 257, 1808, 1214, 11, 10031, 32177, 2270, 322, 264, 2487, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 155236, "start": 1568.06, "end": 1568.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51150, 1779, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 155236, "start": 1568.54, "end": 1574.6399999999999, "text": " The shift here is moving from looking at a single rule to looking at an entire ecosystem of rules.", "tokens": [51174, 440, 5513, 510, 307, 2684, 490, 1237, 412, 257, 2167, 4978, 281, 1237, 412, 364, 2302, 11311, 295, 4474, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17300995360029506, "compression_ratio": 1.625531914893617, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783905436660527e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 157464, "start": 1574.64, "end": 1585.22, "text": " Fliction argues that constraints, whether it's a local zoning law, a corporate HR policy, or a safety protocol on an oil rig, they are not static walls.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 18491, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 257, 2654, 37184, 2101, 11, 257, 10896, 19460, 3897, 11, 420, 257, 4514, 10336, 322, 364, 3184, 8329, 11, 436, 366, 406, 13437, 7920, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 157464, "start": 1585.4, "end": 1586.14, "text": " They are living agents.", "tokens": [50903, 814, 366, 2647, 12554, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 157464, "start": 1586.2800000000002, "end": 1586.6000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50947, 7587, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 157464, "start": 1586.74, "end": 1588.3200000000002, "text": " They co-create each other over time.", "tokens": [50970, 814, 598, 12, 14066, 473, 1184, 661, 670, 565, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 157464, "start": 1588.64, "end": 1595.5600000000002, "text": " When a judge makes a highly specific ruling on a vague statute, they are performing a tiny, localized update to that rule.", "tokens": [51065, 1133, 257, 6995, 1669, 257, 5405, 2685, 21437, 322, 257, 24247, 24774, 11, 436, 366, 10205, 257, 5870, 11, 44574, 5623, 281, 300, 4978, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 157464, "start": 1595.7800000000002, "end": 1600.0800000000002, "text": " And over decades, all those tiny updates push against the other rules around them.", "tokens": [51422, 400, 670, 7878, 11, 439, 729, 5870, 9205, 2944, 1970, 264, 661, 4474, 926, 552, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 157464, "start": 1600.3600000000001, "end": 1601.64, "text": " The rules adapt to the pressure.", "tokens": [51651, 440, 4474, 6231, 281, 264, 3321, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13398875360903534, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.586023738557596e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 160164, "start": 1601.64, "end": 1608.5400000000002, "text": " So if we have an ecology of rules that are constantly shifting, it raises a very practical question for anyone trying to build a safe system.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 321, 362, 364, 39683, 295, 4474, 300, 366, 6460, 17573, 11, 309, 19658, 257, 588, 8496, 1168, 337, 2878, 1382, 281, 1322, 257, 3273, 1185, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13392852455057125, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675461146127945e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 160164, "start": 1608.8400000000001, "end": 1610.7, "text": " Does having more rules make us safer?", "tokens": [50725, 4402, 1419, 544, 4474, 652, 505, 15856, 30, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13392852455057125, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675461146127945e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 160164, "start": 1610.9, "end": 1612.64, "text": " This raises an important question, yes.", "tokens": [50828, 639, 19658, 364, 1021, 1168, 11, 2086, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13392852455057125, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675461146127945e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 160164, "start": 1612.9, "end": 1613.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50928, 1779, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13392852455057125, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675461146127945e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 160164, "start": 1613.46, "end": 1625.46, "text": " If an airplane has five overlapping safety systems, or a hospital requires nurses to fill out 10 different compliance checklists before administering medication, are we fundamentally more protected against failure?", "tokens": [50956, 759, 364, 17130, 575, 1732, 33535, 4514, 3652, 11, 420, 257, 4530, 7029, 17446, 281, 2836, 484, 1266, 819, 15882, 1520, 36693, 949, 22096, 278, 13851, 11, 366, 321, 17879, 544, 10594, 1970, 7763, 30, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13392852455057125, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675461146127945e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 162546, "start": 1625.46, "end": 1634.26, "text": " We intuitively assume that if rules are cooperating, if they are all pulling in the exact same direction and enforcing the same standard, that the system is robust.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 46506, 6552, 300, 498, 4474, 366, 13414, 990, 11, 498, 436, 366, 439, 8407, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 3513, 293, 25495, 2175, 264, 912, 3832, 11, 300, 264, 1185, 307, 13956, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09814000810895647, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503409304233443e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 162546, "start": 1634.72, "end": 1643.1200000000001, "text": " But the mathematical modeling of constraint diversity shows that constraints that always move together are actually a dangerous pathology.", "tokens": [50828, 583, 264, 18894, 15983, 295, 25534, 8811, 3110, 300, 18491, 300, 1009, 1286, 1214, 366, 767, 257, 5795, 3100, 1793, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09814000810895647, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503409304233443e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 162546, "start": 1643.3600000000001, "end": 1644.66, "text": " This is the paradox of redundancy.", "tokens": [51260, 639, 307, 264, 26221, 295, 27830, 6717, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09814000810895647, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503409304233443e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 164466, "start": 1644.66, "end": 1656.0600000000002, "text": " If you mandate 10 safety checklists, but they all check for the exact same failure mode using the exact same underlying assumptions, they function mathematically as a single point of failure.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 23885, 1266, 4514, 1520, 36693, 11, 457, 436, 439, 1520, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 7763, 4391, 1228, 264, 1900, 912, 14217, 17695, 11, 436, 2445, 44003, 382, 257, 2167, 935, 295, 7763, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009168474861745, "compression_ratio": 1.6349206349206349, "no_speech_prob": 2.5837264185785136e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 164466, "start": 1656.26, "end": 1656.6000000000001, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50945, 3153, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009168474861745, "compression_ratio": 1.6349206349206349, "no_speech_prob": 2.5837264185785136e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 164466, "start": 1656.8000000000002, "end": 1662.9, "text": " If a novel threat, something you didn't anticipate, bypasses the logic of the first checklist, it will seamlessly bypass the other nine.", "tokens": [50972, 759, 257, 7613, 4734, 11, 746, 291, 994, 380, 21685, 11, 24996, 279, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 700, 30357, 11, 309, 486, 38083, 24996, 264, 661, 4949, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009168474861745, "compression_ratio": 1.6349206349206349, "no_speech_prob": 2.5837264185785136e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 164466, "start": 1663.3000000000002, "end": 1667.26, "text": " Redundancy dressed up as multiplicity provides absolutely no extra protection.", "tokens": [51297, 4477, 997, 6717, 12386, 493, 382, 17596, 507, 6417, 3122, 572, 2857, 6334, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009168474861745, "compression_ratio": 1.6349206349206349, "no_speech_prob": 2.5837264185785136e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 166726, "start": 1667.26, "end": 1669.54, "text": " It just adds administrative drag.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 445, 10860, 17900, 5286, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 166726, "start": 1669.76, "end": 1670.32, "text": " Okay, but wait.", "tokens": [50490, 1033, 11, 457, 1699, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 166726, "start": 1670.58, "end": 1684.44, "text": " If I know redundancies is bad, and I want true diversity, surely if I have rules that look for completely different things, and maybe even conflict with each other slightly, that raises the diversity of my system and makes it more robust, right?", "tokens": [50531, 759, 286, 458, 27830, 32286, 307, 1578, 11, 293, 286, 528, 2074, 8811, 11, 11468, 498, 286, 362, 4474, 300, 574, 337, 2584, 819, 721, 11, 293, 1310, 754, 6596, 365, 1184, 661, 4748, 11, 300, 19658, 264, 8811, 295, 452, 1185, 293, 1669, 309, 544, 13956, 11, 558, 30, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 166726, "start": 1684.72, "end": 1685.62, "text": " You would hope so.", "tokens": [51238, 509, 576, 1454, 370, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 166726, "start": 1685.76, "end": 1694.44, "text": " But there is a specific, devious mathematical proof in the text involving a hypothetical system of four constraints that shatters this assumption.", "tokens": [51290, 583, 456, 307, 257, 2685, 11, 368, 1502, 18894, 8177, 294, 264, 2487, 17030, 257, 33053, 1185, 295, 1451, 18491, 300, 402, 37690, 341, 15302, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 166726, "start": 1694.58, "end": 1695.2, "text": " It's wild.", "tokens": [51731, 467, 311, 4868, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10344276428222657, "compression_ratio": 1.5945945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.561432406982366e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 169520, "start": 1695.2, "end": 1700.72, "text": " It proves that a system can look mathematically perfectly diverse while actually being completely paralyzed.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 300, 257, 1185, 393, 574, 44003, 6239, 9521, 1339, 767, 885, 2584, 41919, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 169520, "start": 1701.02, "end": 1703.66, "text": " Walk us through how four rules can trick the math.", "tokens": [50656, 10818, 505, 807, 577, 1451, 4474, 393, 4282, 264, 5221, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 169520, "start": 1703.96, "end": 1706.24, "text": " Imagine a system governed by four rules.", "tokens": [50803, 11739, 257, 1185, 35529, 538, 1451, 4474, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 169520, "start": 1706.52, "end": 1708.6000000000001, "text": " The first three rules are perfectly redundant.", "tokens": [50931, 440, 700, 1045, 4474, 366, 6239, 40997, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 169520, "start": 1709.02, "end": 1714.18, "text": " They are clones of each other, checking for the exact same thing, failing on the exact same edge cases.", "tokens": [51056, 814, 366, 43803, 295, 1184, 661, 11, 8568, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 11, 18223, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 4691, 3331, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 169520, "start": 1714.7, "end": 1717.14, "text": " By themselves, their diversity is zero.", "tokens": [51340, 3146, 2969, 11, 641, 8811, 307, 4018, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 169520, "start": 1717.38, "end": 1718.54, "text": " They are a monoculture.", "tokens": [51474, 814, 366, 257, 1108, 905, 8389, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 169520, "start": 1718.74, "end": 1722.28, "text": " Okay, so we have a weak, fragile monoculture of three clones.", "tokens": [51542, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 362, 257, 5336, 11, 23847, 1108, 905, 8389, 295, 1045, 43803, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211616783811335, "compression_ratio": 1.7345454545454546, "no_speech_prob": 2.0919544308634075e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 172228, "start": 1722.28, "end": 1728.34, "text": " Now, you introduced a fourth rule, but this fourth rule is an active, diametric conflict with the first three.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 291, 7268, 257, 6409, 4978, 11, 457, 341, 6409, 4978, 307, 364, 4967, 11, 7484, 17475, 6596, 365, 264, 700, 1045, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419268974891076, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068083499686358e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 172228, "start": 1728.6399999999999, "end": 1733.5, "text": " It rules out completely different states, to the point where the entire system is actually infeasible.", "tokens": [50683, 467, 4474, 484, 2584, 819, 4368, 11, 281, 264, 935, 689, 264, 2302, 1185, 307, 767, 1536, 68, 296, 964, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419268974891076, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068083499686358e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 172228, "start": 1733.78, "end": 1737.7, "text": " There is no physical way to satisfy all four rules simultaneously.", "tokens": [50940, 821, 307, 572, 4001, 636, 281, 19319, 439, 1451, 4474, 16561, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15419268974891076, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068083499686358e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 173770, "start": 1737.7, "end": 1744.06, "text": " You have three rules shouting, always do X, and one rule shouting, never do X under any circumstances.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 1045, 4474, 20382, 11, 1009, 360, 1783, 11, 293, 472, 4978, 20382, 11, 1128, 360, 1783, 833, 604, 9121, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1125219699948333, "compression_ratio": 1.6816326530612244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039870169917703e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 173770, "start": 1744.22, "end": 1744.6200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50691, 7587, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1125219699948333, "compression_ratio": 1.6816326530612244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039870169917703e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 173770, "start": 1744.96, "end": 1752.76, "text": " Now, when you run a standard statistical analysis on this population to measure its overall diversity, the algorithm looks at the correlations.", "tokens": [50728, 823, 11, 562, 291, 1190, 257, 3832, 22820, 5215, 322, 341, 4415, 281, 3481, 1080, 4787, 8811, 11, 264, 9284, 1542, 412, 264, 13983, 763, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1125219699948333, "compression_ratio": 1.6816326530612244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039870169917703e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 173770, "start": 1753.46, "end": 1760.54, "text": " It averages the strong positive correlation of the three clones against the extreme negative correlation of the conflicting fourth rule.", "tokens": [51153, 467, 42257, 264, 2068, 3353, 20009, 295, 264, 1045, 43803, 1970, 264, 8084, 3671, 20009, 295, 264, 43784, 6409, 4978, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1125219699948333, "compression_ratio": 1.6816326530612244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039870169917703e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 173770, "start": 1760.78, "end": 1761.48, "text": " And mathematically.", "tokens": [51519, 400, 44003, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1125219699948333, "compression_ratio": 1.6816326530612244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039870169917703e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 176148, "start": 1761.48, "end": 1764.1, "text": " Mathematically, they cancel each other out perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 15776, 40197, 11, 436, 10373, 1184, 661, 484, 6239, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827409386634827, "compression_ratio": 1.5577889447236182, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674034336068954e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 176148, "start": 1764.42, "end": 1769.8600000000001, "text": " The resulting diversity score reports that this population is operating at maximum theoretical diversity.", "tokens": [50512, 440, 16505, 8811, 6175, 7122, 300, 341, 4415, 307, 7447, 412, 6674, 20864, 8811, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827409386634827, "compression_ratio": 1.5577889447236182, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674034336068954e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 176148, "start": 1770.06, "end": 1776.64, "text": " It looks like a flawlessly balanced, highly diverse ecosystem of rules on the spreadsheet.", "tokens": [50794, 467, 1542, 411, 257, 13717, 12048, 13902, 11, 5405, 9521, 11311, 295, 4474, 322, 264, 27733, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827409386634827, "compression_ratio": 1.5577889447236182, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674034336068954e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 176148, "start": 1776.88, "end": 1780.48, "text": " The metric tells the auditor that this is a robust ecology.", "tokens": [51135, 440, 20678, 5112, 264, 33970, 300, 341, 307, 257, 13956, 39683, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827409386634827, "compression_ratio": 1.5577889447236182, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674034336068954e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 178048, "start": 1780.48, "end": 1791.88, "text": " But the on-the-ground reality is that 75% of the system is a fragile monoculture, and the entire structure is paralyzed by a built-in conflict that makes it unworkable.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 322, 12, 3322, 12, 2921, 4103, 307, 300, 9562, 4, 295, 264, 1185, 307, 257, 23847, 1108, 905, 8389, 11, 293, 264, 2302, 3877, 307, 41919, 538, 257, 3094, 12, 259, 6596, 300, 1669, 309, 517, 1902, 712, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0834360122680664, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106034691695803e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 178048, "start": 1791.98, "end": 1796.04, "text": " I picture this like hiring four security guards to protect a sensitive building.", "tokens": [50940, 286, 3036, 341, 411, 15335, 1451, 3825, 17652, 281, 2371, 257, 9477, 2390, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0834360122680664, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106034691695803e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 178048, "start": 1796.5, "end": 1803.74, "text": " Three of those guards went to the exact same training academy, they were the exact same outdated manual, and they share the exact same blind spots.", "tokens": [51166, 6244, 295, 729, 17652, 1437, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 3097, 25525, 11, 436, 645, 264, 1900, 912, 36313, 9688, 11, 293, 436, 2073, 264, 1900, 912, 6865, 10681, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0834360122680664, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106034691695803e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 180374, "start": 1803.74, "end": 1813.04, "text": " If a clever thief knows how to socially engineer guard number one, they can breeze right past guards two and three without changing their tactic at all.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 13494, 23176, 3255, 577, 281, 21397, 11403, 6290, 1230, 472, 11, 436, 393, 24532, 558, 1791, 17652, 732, 293, 1045, 1553, 4473, 641, 31012, 412, 439, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10875201581129387, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 180374, "start": 1813.32, "end": 1815.14, "text": " A completely redundant defense.", "tokens": [50844, 316, 2584, 40997, 7654, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10875201581129387, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 180374, "start": 1815.36, "end": 1815.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50946, 1779, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10875201581129387, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 180374, "start": 1815.82, "end": 1821.38, "text": " And then management realizes they need diversity, so they hire a fourth guard from a totally different tactical background.", "tokens": [50969, 400, 550, 4592, 29316, 436, 643, 8811, 11, 370, 436, 11158, 257, 6409, 6290, 490, 257, 3879, 819, 26323, 3678, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10875201581129387, "compression_ratio": 1.529126213592233, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 182138, "start": 1821.38, "end": 1834.18, "text": " But instead of watching the loading dock, the fourth guard spends his entire 12-hour shift actively fighting with the first three guards because their protocols are fundamentally incompatible.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 2602, 295, 1976, 264, 15114, 20929, 11, 264, 6409, 6290, 25620, 702, 2302, 2272, 12, 18048, 5513, 13022, 5237, 365, 264, 700, 1045, 17652, 570, 641, 20618, 366, 17879, 40393, 267, 964, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 182138, "start": 1834.24, "end": 1835.8600000000001, "text": " They are just arguing the whole time.", "tokens": [51008, 814, 366, 445, 19697, 264, 1379, 565, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 182138, "start": 1835.92, "end": 1836.3400000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51092, 7587, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 182138, "start": 1836.5400000000002, "end": 1842.94, "text": " If an external auditor comes by and evaluates your security team based on statistical variance, the auditor might say,", "tokens": [51123, 759, 364, 8320, 33970, 1487, 538, 293, 6133, 1024, 428, 3825, 1469, 2361, 322, 22820, 21977, 11, 264, 33970, 1062, 584, 11, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 182138, "start": 1843.0800000000002, "end": 1846.3400000000001, "text": " Wow, the variance in your team's tactical behavior is incredibly high.", "tokens": [51450, 3153, 11, 264, 21977, 294, 428, 1469, 311, 26323, 5223, 307, 6252, 1090, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 182138, "start": 1846.5200000000002, "end": 1848.7600000000002, "text": " You have a perfectly diverse security ecosystem.", "tokens": [51622, 509, 362, 257, 6239, 9521, 3825, 11311, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12463662203620463, "compression_ratio": 1.604026845637584, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983128449220674e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 184876, "start": 1848.76, "end": 1853.02, "text": " But in reality, you just have a volatile, paralyzed monoculture.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 4103, 11, 291, 445, 362, 257, 34377, 11, 41919, 1108, 905, 8389, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837749647057574, "compression_ratio": 1.5519713261648747, "no_speech_prob": 1.366910599466531e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 184876, "start": 1853.22, "end": 1860.98, "text": " It perfectly illustrates how a high diversity score cannot be trusted at face value if it is simply masking a tug-of-war between clones and contradictions.", "tokens": [50588, 467, 6239, 41718, 577, 257, 1090, 8811, 6175, 2644, 312, 16034, 412, 1851, 2158, 498, 309, 307, 2935, 31226, 257, 33543, 12, 2670, 12, 6925, 1296, 43803, 293, 15858, 15607, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837749647057574, "compression_ratio": 1.5519713261648747, "no_speech_prob": 1.366910599466531e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 184876, "start": 1861.72, "end": 1868.16, "text": " True robustness requires rules that cover genuinely different failure modes without locking the system into paralysis.", "tokens": [51013, 13587, 13956, 1287, 7029, 4474, 300, 2060, 17839, 819, 7763, 14068, 1553, 23954, 264, 1185, 666, 49507, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837749647057574, "compression_ratio": 1.5519713261648747, "no_speech_prob": 1.366910599466531e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 184876, "start": 1868.74, "end": 1874.56, "text": " Okay, so if these massive interacting ecologies of rules inevitably begin to drift over time,", "tokens": [51364, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 613, 5994, 18017, 11437, 6204, 295, 4474, 28171, 1841, 281, 19699, 670, 565, 11, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08837749647057574, "compression_ratio": 1.5519713261648747, "no_speech_prob": 1.366910599466531e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 187456, "start": 1874.56, "end": 1880.96, "text": " or if they start conflicting like our paralyzed security guards, we eventually face a stark choice.", "tokens": [50365, 420, 498, 436, 722, 43784, 411, 527, 41919, 3825, 17652, 11, 321, 4728, 1851, 257, 17417, 3922, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14720569439788364, "compression_ratio": 1.471794871794872, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354661102977122e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 187456, "start": 1881.26, "end": 1884.1599999999999, "text": " Do we fix the problem now, or do we put it off?", "tokens": [50700, 1144, 321, 3191, 264, 1154, 586, 11, 420, 360, 321, 829, 309, 766, 30, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14720569439788364, "compression_ratio": 1.471794871794872, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354661102977122e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 187456, "start": 1884.34, "end": 1888.76, "text": " And this brings us to the final and perhaps most universally relatable concept in this deep dive.", "tokens": [50854, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 293, 4317, 881, 43995, 42355, 3410, 294, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14720569439788364, "compression_ratio": 1.471794871794872, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354661102977122e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 187456, "start": 1889.36, "end": 1891.6, "text": " The mathematics of deferring maintenance.", "tokens": [51105, 440, 18666, 295, 25704, 2937, 11258, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14720569439788364, "compression_ratio": 1.471794871794872, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354661102977122e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 189160, "start": 1891.6, "end": 1899.1, "text": " Every single person listening to this has looked at a messy garage, a buggy line of code, a creaky organizational process,", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 2167, 954, 4764, 281, 341, 575, 2956, 412, 257, 16191, 14400, 11, 257, 7426, 1480, 1622, 295, 3089, 11, 257, 1197, 15681, 24730, 1399, 11, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 189160, "start": 1899.1, "end": 1903.1, "text": " or even a lingering pain in their knee and thought, I know it's broken, but I'll fix it later.", "tokens": [50740, 420, 754, 257, 49542, 1822, 294, 641, 9434, 293, 1194, 11, 286, 458, 309, 311, 5463, 11, 457, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 189160, "start": 1903.26, "end": 1904.12, "text": " We all do it.", "tokens": [50948, 492, 439, 360, 309, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 189160, "start": 1904.1799999999998, "end": 1909.02, "text": " And the central question Affliction poses is, when is deferred correction mathematically rational?", "tokens": [50994, 400, 264, 5777, 1168, 12840, 75, 4105, 26059, 307, 11, 562, 307, 25704, 986, 19984, 44003, 15090, 30, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 189160, "start": 1909.28, "end": 1911.9199999999998, "text": " When is, I'll fix it later, actually the smartest thing you can do?", "tokens": [51249, 1133, 307, 11, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 11, 767, 264, 41491, 551, 291, 393, 360, 30, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 189160, "start": 1912.02, "end": 1914.82, "text": " And when is it a recipe for catastrophic collapse?", "tokens": [51386, 400, 562, 307, 309, 257, 6782, 337, 34915, 15584, 30, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.115143616994222, "compression_ratio": 1.6035714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750210159871548e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 191482, "start": 1914.82, "end": 1920.6799999999998, "text": " To untangle this, we have to recognize that there are two completely different financial and energetic realities at play here.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 1701, 7846, 341, 11, 321, 362, 281, 5521, 300, 456, 366, 732, 2584, 819, 4669, 293, 24935, 27785, 412, 862, 510, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1133425095502068, "compression_ratio": 1.6550522648083623, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918409168938497e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 191482, "start": 1921.3799999999999, "end": 1922.58, "text": " Maintenance versus repair.", "tokens": [50693, 30437, 719, 5717, 10535, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1133425095502068, "compression_ratio": 1.6550522648083623, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918409168938497e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 191482, "start": 1922.96, "end": 1925.32, "text": " Maintenance is continuous and unconditional.", "tokens": [50772, 30437, 719, 307, 10957, 293, 47916, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1133425095502068, "compression_ratio": 1.6550522648083623, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918409168938497e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 191482, "start": 1926.36, "end": 1933.78, "text": " It is the steady tax you pay every single day, regardless of whether the system is currently broken or not, just to keep things aligned.", "tokens": [50942, 467, 307, 264, 13211, 3366, 291, 1689, 633, 2167, 786, 11, 10060, 295, 1968, 264, 1185, 307, 4362, 5463, 420, 406, 11, 445, 281, 1066, 721, 17962, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1133425095502068, "compression_ratio": 1.6550522648083623, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918409168938497e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 191482, "start": 1934.32, "end": 1943.5, "text": " It's brushing your teeth twice a day, running daily automated security scans on your servers, or paying the salary of a compliance officer.", "tokens": [51340, 467, 311, 33130, 428, 7798, 6091, 257, 786, 11, 2614, 5212, 18473, 3825, 35116, 322, 428, 15909, 11, 420, 6229, 264, 15360, 295, 257, 15882, 8456, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1133425095502068, "compression_ratio": 1.6550522648083623, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918409168938497e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 194350, "start": 1943.5, "end": 1945.58, "text": " You pay it no matter what the weather is doing.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1689, 309, 572, 1871, 437, 264, 5503, 307, 884, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 194350, "start": 1946.02, "end": 1948.82, "text": " Repair, on the other hand, is discontinuous and conditional.", "tokens": [50491, 3696, 1246, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 307, 31420, 12549, 293, 27708, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 194350, "start": 1949.48, "end": 1953.9, "text": " You only trigger a repair when the system has actively failed or left its viable state.", "tokens": [50664, 509, 787, 7875, 257, 10535, 562, 264, 1185, 575, 13022, 7612, 420, 1411, 1080, 22024, 1785, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 194350, "start": 1954.02, "end": 1954.8, "text": " Right, like an emergency.", "tokens": [50891, 1779, 11, 411, 364, 7473, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 194350, "start": 1955.3, "end": 1963.0, "text": " It's getting an emergency root canal, pulling the servers offline to patch a critical vulnerability, or injecting capital into a failing bank.", "tokens": [50955, 467, 311, 1242, 364, 7473, 5593, 9911, 11, 8407, 264, 15909, 21857, 281, 9972, 257, 4924, 24210, 11, 420, 10711, 278, 4238, 666, 257, 18223, 3765, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 194350, "start": 1963.4, "end": 1968.48, "text": " You only pay for it when things go wrong, but when you do pay for it, the cost is violently convex,", "tokens": [51360, 509, 787, 1689, 337, 309, 562, 721, 352, 2085, 11, 457, 562, 291, 360, 1689, 337, 309, 11, 264, 2063, 307, 46728, 42432, 11, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 194350, "start": 1968.62, "end": 1973.14, "text": " meaning it gets disproportionately more expensive the longer you let the problem compound.", "tokens": [51621, 3620, 309, 2170, 43397, 544, 5124, 264, 2854, 291, 718, 264, 1154, 14154, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11051459645116052, "compression_ratio": 1.721362229102167, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899338273560714e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 197314, "start": 1973.14, "end": 1974.98, "text": " And the problem always compounds, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 1154, 1009, 21810, 11, 558, 30, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 197314, "start": 1975.2800000000002, "end": 1977.48, "text": " Uncorrected errors don't just sit still.", "tokens": [50472, 1156, 19558, 2554, 292, 13603, 500, 380, 445, 1394, 920, 13, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 197314, "start": 1977.5600000000002, "end": 1978.0400000000002, "text": " They drift.", "tokens": [50586, 814, 19699, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 197314, "start": 1978.7800000000002, "end": 1981.2, "text": " Fliction focuses heavily on the compounding rate.", "tokens": [50647, 3235, 4105, 16109, 10950, 322, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 197314, "start": 1981.72, "end": 1985.26, "text": " This is the speed at which an ignored error amplifies itself over time.", "tokens": [50794, 639, 307, 264, 3073, 412, 597, 364, 19735, 6713, 9731, 11221, 2564, 670, 565, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 197314, "start": 1985.5400000000002, "end": 1995.42, "text": " So we are weighing the continuous, annoying cost of daily maintenance against the compounding, terrifying cost of a deferred crisis repair.", "tokens": [50985, 407, 321, 366, 31986, 264, 10957, 11, 11304, 2063, 295, 5212, 11258, 1970, 264, 14154, 278, 11, 18106, 2063, 295, 257, 25704, 986, 5869, 10535, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 197314, "start": 1995.6200000000001, "end": 1995.7800000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51489, 865, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 197314, "start": 1995.9, "end": 1997.4, "text": " How do we actually make the choice?", "tokens": [51503, 1012, 360, 321, 767, 652, 264, 3922, 30, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16565033940985652, "compression_ratio": 1.6008064516129032, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308662540750029e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 199740, "start": 1997.4, "end": 2007.3600000000001, "text": " The text maps out two distinct scenarios where choosing to defer, choosing to say I'll fix it later, can actually open up as a rational window.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 11317, 484, 732, 10644, 15077, 689, 10875, 281, 25704, 11, 10875, 281, 584, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 11, 393, 767, 1269, 493, 382, 257, 15090, 4910, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11626192501613072, "compression_ratio": 1.6512605042016806, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 199740, "start": 2007.6200000000001, "end": 2011.38, "text": " The first scenario is driven entirely by fixed administrative overheads.", "tokens": [50876, 440, 700, 9005, 307, 9555, 7696, 538, 6806, 17900, 19922, 82, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11626192501613072, "compression_ratio": 1.6512605042016806, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 199740, "start": 2011.96, "end": 2015.72, "text": " Imagine the flat cost of simply monitoring a system every day.", "tokens": [51093, 11739, 264, 4962, 2063, 295, 2935, 11028, 257, 1185, 633, 786, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11626192501613072, "compression_ratio": 1.6512605042016806, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 199740, "start": 2016.3200000000002, "end": 2021.3200000000002, "text": " Now compare that to the flat administrative cost of just initiating a repair ticket when something finally snaps.", "tokens": [51311, 823, 6794, 300, 281, 264, 4962, 17900, 2063, 295, 445, 6265, 990, 257, 10535, 10550, 562, 746, 2721, 19206, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11626192501613072, "compression_ratio": 1.6512605042016806, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 202132, "start": 2021.32, "end": 2028.6599999999999, "text": " If the daily monitoring overhead is substantially higher than the flat cost of initiating a fix, a deferral window opens immediately.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 5212, 11028, 19922, 307, 30797, 2946, 813, 264, 4962, 2063, 295, 6265, 990, 257, 3191, 11, 257, 25704, 2155, 4910, 9870, 4258, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 202132, "start": 2029.1599999999999, "end": 2033.6399999999999, "text": " It is mathematically rational from day one to say, I'm not going to watch this, I'll just wait until it breaks.", "tokens": [50757, 467, 307, 44003, 15090, 490, 786, 472, 281, 584, 11, 286, 478, 406, 516, 281, 1159, 341, 11, 286, 603, 445, 1699, 1826, 309, 9857, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 202132, "start": 2033.78, "end": 2039.1599999999999, "text": " Because it literally costs more money and time to stare at it than it does to just submit the work order when it finally snaps.", "tokens": [50988, 1436, 309, 3736, 5497, 544, 1460, 293, 565, 281, 22432, 412, 309, 813, 309, 775, 281, 445, 10315, 264, 589, 1668, 562, 309, 2721, 19206, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 202132, "start": 2039.3, "end": 2039.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51264, 7587, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 202132, "start": 2040.0, "end": 2041.6, "text": " But what if the overheads are reversed?", "tokens": [51299, 583, 437, 498, 264, 19922, 82, 366, 30563, 30, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 202132, "start": 2042.22, "end": 2048.2999999999997, "text": " What if continuous monitoring is incredibly cheap, but triggering a crisis repair is astronomically expensive?", "tokens": [51410, 708, 498, 10957, 11028, 307, 6252, 7084, 11, 457, 40406, 257, 5869, 10535, 307, 26302, 984, 5124, 30, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07958882649739583, "compression_ratio": 1.665625, "no_speech_prob": 1.680964503876503e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 204830, "start": 2048.3, "end": 2054.1600000000003, "text": " This introduces the second scenario, which is driven entirely by the geometry of the compounding curve.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 31472, 264, 1150, 9005, 11, 597, 307, 9555, 7696, 538, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 14154, 278, 7605, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 204830, "start": 2054.54, "end": 2065.2200000000003, "text": " Even if the emergency repair is expensive, if the problem compounds very, very slowly, I might still have a window where ignoring it is momentarily cheaper than paying the daily maintenance tax.", "tokens": [50677, 2754, 498, 264, 7473, 10535, 307, 5124, 11, 498, 264, 1154, 21810, 588, 11, 588, 5692, 11, 286, 1062, 920, 362, 257, 4910, 689, 26258, 309, 307, 1623, 3289, 12284, 813, 6229, 264, 5212, 11258, 3366, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 204830, "start": 2065.4, "end": 2065.7400000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51220, 1079, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 204830, "start": 2066.2200000000003, "end": 2067.04, "text": " I'll fix it later.", "tokens": [51261, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 204830, "start": 2067.34, "end": 2069.3, "text": " Isn't just a symptom of human procrastination.", "tokens": [51317, 6998, 380, 445, 257, 29370, 295, 1952, 39306, 2486, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 204830, "start": 2070.28, "end": 2073.98, "text": " Under the right geometric conditions, it can be the mathematically optimal choice.", "tokens": [51464, 6974, 264, 558, 33246, 4487, 11, 309, 393, 312, 264, 44003, 16252, 3922, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330864756715064, "compression_ratio": 1.6142857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778458625782197e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 207398, "start": 2073.98, "end": 2081.4, "text": " But the crucial, unforgiving caveat in Fliction's math is that this deferral window is always finite.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 11462, 11, 31411, 15441, 43012, 294, 3235, 4105, 311, 5221, 307, 300, 341, 25704, 2155, 4910, 307, 1009, 19362, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 207398, "start": 2081.6, "end": 2082.7, "text": " It doesn't last forever.", "tokens": [50746, 467, 1177, 380, 1036, 5680, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 207398, "start": 2082.88, "end": 2084.44, "text": " It is not a permanent state.", "tokens": [50810, 467, 307, 406, 257, 10996, 1785, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 207398, "start": 2084.92, "end": 2091.76, "text": " If you wait too long, the convex cost of the crisis repair will inevitably explode past whatever you saved on maintenance.", "tokens": [50912, 759, 291, 1699, 886, 938, 11, 264, 42432, 2063, 295, 264, 5869, 10535, 486, 28171, 21411, 1791, 2035, 291, 6624, 322, 11258, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 207398, "start": 2092.42, "end": 2097.54, "text": " To make this tangible, let's look at how this plays out across four very different real-world domains.", "tokens": [51287, 1407, 652, 341, 27094, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 577, 341, 5749, 484, 2108, 1451, 588, 819, 957, 12, 13217, 25514, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 207398, "start": 2097.78, "end": 2098.72, "text": " Let's start with biology.", "tokens": [51555, 961, 311, 722, 365, 14956, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 207398, "start": 2099.42, "end": 2103.62, "text": " A biological system like an untreated infection or an escalating vascular condition.", "tokens": [51637, 316, 13910, 1185, 411, 364, 1701, 26559, 11764, 420, 364, 17871, 990, 371, 22084, 4188, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13899125891216732, "compression_ratio": 1.5974025974025974, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724445621117077e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 210362, "start": 2103.62, "end": 2106.42, "text": " In biology, the compounding rate is extremely high.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 14956, 11, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 307, 4664, 1090, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 210362, "start": 2106.96, "end": 2111.68, "text": " An infection doesn't just sit dormant in your arm, it actively replicates and amplifies itself.", "tokens": [50532, 1107, 11764, 1177, 380, 445, 1394, 12521, 394, 294, 428, 3726, 11, 309, 13022, 3248, 299, 1024, 293, 9731, 11221, 2564, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 210362, "start": 2112.18, "end": 2117.7799999999997, "text": " Because the problem accelerates so aggressively, the deferral window collapses almost instantly.", "tokens": [50793, 1436, 264, 1154, 10172, 1024, 370, 32024, 11, 264, 25704, 2155, 4910, 48765, 1920, 13518, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 210362, "start": 2118.66, "end": 2124.5, "text": " If you have a severe infection, telling yourself, I'll fix it later, becomes catastrophic within days.", "tokens": [51117, 759, 291, 362, 257, 8922, 11764, 11, 3585, 1803, 11, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 11, 3643, 34915, 1951, 1708, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 210362, "start": 2124.88, "end": 2126.88, "text": " The compounding curve is just too steep.", "tokens": [51428, 440, 14154, 278, 7605, 307, 445, 886, 16841, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 210362, "start": 2127.2, "end": 2129.08, "text": " Now contrast that with software maintenance.", "tokens": [51544, 823, 8712, 300, 365, 4722, 11258, 13, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14420963287353517, "compression_ratio": 1.5919117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552501556910126e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 212908, "start": 2129.08, "end": 2135.64, "text": " Let's say you have a dormant, non-propagating bug in an obscure part of your code base.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 257, 12521, 394, 11, 2107, 12, 79, 1513, 559, 990, 7426, 294, 364, 34443, 644, 295, 428, 3089, 3096, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 212908, "start": 2135.86, "end": 2137.7599999999998, "text": " This is the exact opposite geometry.", "tokens": [50704, 639, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 18426, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 212908, "start": 2138.2599999999998, "end": 2140.14, "text": " The compounding rate is near zero.", "tokens": [50824, 440, 14154, 278, 3314, 307, 2651, 4018, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 212908, "start": 2140.42, "end": 2141.52, "text": " The bug just sits there.", "tokens": [50932, 440, 7426, 445, 12696, 456, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 212908, "start": 2141.64, "end": 2144.46, "text": " It doesn't actively infect the rest of the code or replicate itself.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 1177, 380, 13022, 5888, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 3089, 420, 25356, 2564, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 212908, "start": 2145.22, "end": 2153.88, "text": " Meanwhile, the overhead of maintaining constant vigilance running continuous integration servers, halting development to fix every minor typo is very high.", "tokens": [51172, 13879, 11, 264, 19922, 295, 14916, 5754, 39093, 719, 2614, 10957, 10980, 15909, 11, 7523, 783, 3250, 281, 3191, 633, 6696, 2125, 78, 307, 588, 1090, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 212908, "start": 2153.96, "end": 2154.72, "text": " Right, it's exhausting.", "tokens": [51609, 1779, 11, 309, 311, 34076, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1368711191579836, "compression_ratio": 1.5745454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 2.261931744337864e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 215472, "start": 2154.72, "end": 2160.18, "text": " Therefore, deferring the fix is highly rational. You batch the minor bugs and fix them all at once later.", "tokens": [50365, 7504, 11, 25704, 2937, 264, 3191, 307, 5405, 15090, 13, 509, 15245, 264, 6696, 15120, 293, 3191, 552, 439, 412, 1564, 1780, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10361790376551011, "compression_ratio": 1.6383928571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015458052965782e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 215472, "start": 2160.4399999999996, "end": 2162.62, "text": " But the danger is miscategorizing the bug.", "tokens": [50651, 583, 264, 4330, 307, 3346, 66, 2968, 284, 3319, 264, 7426, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10361790376551011, "compression_ratio": 1.6383928571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015458052965782e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 215472, "start": 2163.3799999999997, "end": 2174.3999999999996, "text": " If you assume the compounding rate is zero, but it's actually a security vulnerability that hackers are actively exploiting to access more systems, the compounding rate is massive and deferring it destroys the company.", "tokens": [50798, 759, 291, 6552, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 307, 4018, 11, 457, 309, 311, 767, 257, 3825, 24210, 300, 39766, 366, 13022, 12382, 1748, 281, 2105, 544, 3652, 11, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 307, 5994, 293, 25704, 2937, 309, 36714, 264, 2237, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10361790376551011, "compression_ratio": 1.6383928571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015458052965782e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 217440, "start": 2174.4, "end": 2179.54, "text": " Precisely. You have to understand the true compounding rate of the system you are managing.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 509, 362, 281, 1223, 264, 2074, 14154, 278, 3314, 295, 264, 1185, 291, 366, 11642, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.167003713003019, "compression_ratio": 1.623931623931624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080497172888842e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 217440, "start": 2180.52, "end": 2182.46, "text": " The third domain is physical infrastructure.", "tokens": [50671, 440, 2636, 9274, 307, 4001, 6896, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.167003713003019, "compression_ratio": 1.623931623931624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080497172888842e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 217440, "start": 2183.42, "end": 2187.54, "text": " Think of bridges, municipal water systems, or the electrical grid.", "tokens": [50816, 6557, 295, 21114, 11, 27177, 1281, 3652, 11, 420, 264, 12147, 10748, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.167003713003019, "compression_ratio": 1.623931623931624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080497172888842e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 217440, "start": 2187.86, "end": 2198.1, "text": " A rusted beam on a bridge doesn't necessarily replicate like a biological infection, but infrastructure has a different structural tear, the sheer convexity of the crisis cost.", "tokens": [51038, 316, 367, 6589, 14269, 322, 257, 7283, 1177, 380, 4725, 25356, 411, 257, 13910, 11764, 11, 457, 6896, 575, 257, 819, 15067, 12556, 11, 264, 23061, 42432, 507, 295, 264, 5869, 2063, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.167003713003019, "compression_ratio": 1.623931623931624, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080497172888842e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 219810, "start": 2198.1, "end": 2203.38, "text": " Replacing a single rusted beam during routine maintenance is relatively cheap.", "tokens": [50365, 47762, 5615, 257, 2167, 367, 6589, 14269, 1830, 9927, 11258, 307, 7226, 7084, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13126603092055722, "compression_ratio": 1.6126126126126126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614394542964871e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 219810, "start": 2204.02, "end": 2210.36, "text": " But if you defer that maintenance until the beam snaps and the bridge collapses, the cost isn't just replacing the bridge.", "tokens": [50661, 583, 498, 291, 25704, 300, 11258, 1826, 264, 14269, 19206, 293, 264, 7283, 48765, 11, 264, 2063, 1943, 380, 445, 19139, 264, 7283, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13126603092055722, "compression_ratio": 1.6126126126126126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614394542964871e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 219810, "start": 2210.44, "end": 2211.22, "text": " No, it's catastrophic.", "tokens": [50982, 883, 11, 309, 311, 34915, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13126603092055722, "compression_ratio": 1.6126126126126126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614394542964871e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 219810, "start": 2211.7, "end": 2219.2599999999998, "text": " It's the economic devastation of rerouted traffic, the years of environmental reviews, the emergency redesigns, and the loss of life.", "tokens": [51045, 467, 311, 264, 4836, 13959, 399, 295, 43819, 346, 292, 6419, 11, 264, 924, 295, 8303, 10229, 11, 264, 7473, 39853, 82, 11, 293, 264, 4470, 295, 993, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13126603092055722, "compression_ratio": 1.6126126126126126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614394542964871e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 221926, "start": 2219.26, "end": 2226.6800000000003, "text": " The cost curve is so wildly convex that it demands continuous maintenance, even if the compounding rate is slow.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2063, 7605, 307, 370, 34731, 42432, 300, 309, 15107, 10957, 11258, 11, 754, 498, 264, 14154, 278, 3314, 307, 2964, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 221926, "start": 2227.2400000000002, "end": 2230.82, "text": " And the fourth domain is the one that brings all these dangerous variables together at once.", "tokens": [50764, 400, 264, 6409, 9274, 307, 264, 472, 300, 5607, 439, 613, 5795, 9102, 1214, 412, 1564, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 221926, "start": 2231.48, "end": 2232.6000000000004, "text": " Massive fiscal systems.", "tokens": [50976, 10482, 488, 15897, 3652, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 221926, "start": 2232.9, "end": 2237.26, "text": " Think of a sovereign debt crisis or a massive corporate restructuring that keeps getting kicked down the road.", "tokens": [51047, 6557, 295, 257, 28756, 7831, 5869, 420, 257, 5994, 10896, 1472, 1757, 1345, 300, 5965, 1242, 14609, 760, 264, 3060, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 221926, "start": 2237.6600000000003, "end": 2242.1400000000003, "text": " A heavily indebted fiscal structure exhibits the worst of all parameters simultaneously.", "tokens": [51285, 316, 10950, 24162, 4517, 292, 15897, 3877, 39205, 264, 5855, 295, 439, 9834, 16561, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 221926, "start": 2242.7200000000003, "end": 2246.44, "text": " You have massive fixed overheads just to audit and comply with the system.", "tokens": [51538, 509, 362, 5994, 6806, 19922, 82, 445, 281, 17748, 293, 27956, 365, 264, 1185, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10737980833841027, "compression_ratio": 1.6688741721854305, "no_speech_prob": 2.150976445569608e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 224644, "start": 2246.44, "end": 2250.46, "text": " You have incredibly high initiation costs for a crisis bailout.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 6252, 1090, 43569, 5497, 337, 257, 5869, 19313, 346, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 224644, "start": 2251.08, "end": 2258.7400000000002, "text": " The structural imbalance compounds actively every day due to compounding interest and the gradual loss of institutional trust.", "tokens": [50597, 440, 15067, 43007, 21810, 13022, 633, 786, 3462, 281, 14154, 278, 1179, 293, 264, 32890, 4470, 295, 18391, 3361, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 224644, "start": 2258.88, "end": 2259.68, "text": " It's just a nightmare.", "tokens": [50987, 467, 311, 445, 257, 18724, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 224644, "start": 2260.0, "end": 2265.7000000000003, "text": " And the ultimate cost of a systemic crash is deeply convex, impacting the entire surrounding ecology.", "tokens": [51043, 400, 264, 9705, 2063, 295, 257, 23789, 8252, 307, 8760, 42432, 11, 29963, 264, 2302, 11498, 39683, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 224644, "start": 2265.86, "end": 2268.6, "text": " It is the absolute perfect storm of bad math.", "tokens": [51336, 467, 307, 264, 8236, 2176, 7679, 295, 1578, 5221, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 224644, "start": 2268.82, "end": 2273.02, "text": " And this leads to an asymptotic estimate in the paper that is truly chilling.", "tokens": [51484, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 364, 35114, 9411, 12539, 294, 264, 3035, 300, 307, 4908, 31047, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.135244091351827, "compression_ratio": 1.625925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.52513060774212e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 227302, "start": 2273.02, "end": 2280.4, "text": " When you model all these variables interacting over time, the systems that appear to have the highest tolerance for deferring maintenance,", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 2316, 439, 613, 9102, 18017, 670, 565, 11, 264, 3652, 300, 4204, 281, 362, 264, 6343, 23368, 337, 25704, 2937, 11258, 11, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08992210030555725, "compression_ratio": 1.7054545454545456, "no_speech_prob": 1.846837353186581e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 227302, "start": 2281.0, "end": 2288.3, "text": " the massive wealthy systems where the daily monitoring costs seem like a drop in the bucket compared to their vast resources,", "tokens": [50764, 264, 5994, 17707, 3652, 689, 264, 5212, 11028, 5497, 1643, 411, 257, 3270, 294, 264, 13058, 5347, 281, 641, 8369, 3593, 11, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08992210030555725, "compression_ratio": 1.7054545454545456, "no_speech_prob": 1.846837353186581e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 227302, "start": 2288.56, "end": 2294.9, "text": " are actually the ones whose thresholds erode the absolute fastest the moment the problem begins to actively compound.", "tokens": [51142, 366, 767, 264, 2306, 6104, 14678, 82, 1189, 1429, 264, 8236, 14573, 264, 1623, 264, 1154, 7338, 281, 13022, 14154, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08992210030555725, "compression_ratio": 1.7054545454545456, "no_speech_prob": 1.846837353186581e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 227302, "start": 2295.08, "end": 2299.22, "text": " Wait, if a system looks rich and stable, it actually crashes faster once it tips over?", "tokens": [51468, 3802, 11, 498, 257, 1185, 1542, 4593, 293, 8351, 11, 309, 767, 28642, 4663, 1564, 309, 6082, 670, 30, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08992210030555725, "compression_ratio": 1.7054545454545456, "no_speech_prob": 1.846837353186581e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 229922, "start": 2299.22, "end": 2307.54, "text": " Yes. A system that believes it has a massive, luxurious runway for deferring a problem will lose that runway disproportionately fast.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 316, 1185, 300, 12307, 309, 575, 257, 5994, 11, 30840, 26642, 337, 25704, 2937, 257, 1154, 486, 3624, 300, 26642, 43397, 2370, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07454431851704915, "compression_ratio": 1.541899441340782, "no_speech_prob": 1.604574871409692e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 229922, "start": 2307.98, "end": 2316.2599999999998, "text": " Deferral tolerance is eroded fastest in precisely the systems that most appear on a static reading to be able to afford the luxury of waiting.", "tokens": [50803, 1346, 612, 2155, 23368, 307, 1189, 12340, 14573, 294, 13402, 264, 3652, 300, 881, 4204, 322, 257, 13437, 3760, 281, 312, 1075, 281, 6157, 264, 15558, 295, 3806, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07454431851704915, "compression_ratio": 1.541899441340782, "no_speech_prob": 1.604574871409692e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 231626, "start": 2316.26, "end": 2322.2400000000002, "text": " So what does this all mean for us, for you and me, managing our own lives or our own organizations?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 505, 11, 337, 291, 293, 385, 11, 11642, 527, 1065, 2909, 420, 527, 1065, 6150, 30, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08955708146095276, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 2.028339085233255e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 231626, "start": 2322.46, "end": 2328.5400000000004, "text": " It means that mistaking a high compounding problem like an eroding company culture, a growing biological illness,", "tokens": [50675, 467, 1355, 300, 3544, 2456, 257, 1090, 14154, 278, 1154, 411, 364, 1189, 8616, 2237, 3713, 11, 257, 4194, 13910, 10152, 11, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08955708146095276, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 2.028339085233255e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 231626, "start": 2328.5400000000004, "end": 2336.36, "text": " or a creeping debt for a low compounding problem like a harmless software bug is the exact mechanism of catastrophic failure.", "tokens": [50979, 420, 257, 47753, 7831, 337, 257, 2295, 14154, 278, 1154, 411, 257, 40160, 4722, 7426, 307, 264, 1900, 7513, 295, 34915, 7763, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08955708146095276, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 2.028339085233255e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 231626, "start": 2336.5400000000004, "end": 2336.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51379, 1079, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08955708146095276, "compression_ratio": 1.6150234741784038, "no_speech_prob": 2.028339085233255e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 233688, "start": 2336.88, "end": 2344.6800000000003, "text": " We tell ourselves, I'll fix it later, because we intuitively apply the safe logic of a dormant bug to the aggressive reality of a compounding infection.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 980, 4175, 11, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 11, 570, 321, 46506, 3079, 264, 3273, 9952, 295, 257, 12521, 394, 7426, 281, 264, 10762, 4103, 295, 257, 14154, 278, 11764, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11167123967950994, "compression_ratio": 1.6028368794326242, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 233688, "start": 2345.38, "end": 2348.62, "text": " And by the time we realize our error, the math has already doomed us.", "tokens": [50790, 400, 538, 264, 565, 321, 4325, 527, 6713, 11, 264, 5221, 575, 1217, 33847, 505, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11167123967950994, "compression_ratio": 1.6028368794326242, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 233688, "start": 2349.08, "end": 2353.48, "text": " The window has slammed shut, and the convex cost of repair is entirely unsurvivable.", "tokens": [50975, 440, 4910, 575, 50196, 5309, 11, 293, 264, 42432, 2063, 295, 10535, 307, 7696, 2693, 374, 27810, 712, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11167123967950994, "compression_ratio": 1.6028368794326242, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 233688, "start": 2353.56, "end": 2355.6800000000003, "text": " It is a fundamental failure of categorization.", "tokens": [51199, 467, 307, 257, 8088, 7763, 295, 19250, 2144, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11167123967950994, "compression_ratio": 1.6028368794326242, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 233688, "start": 2356.1800000000003, "end": 2360.7200000000003, "text": " We misjudge the geometry of the problem we are deferring, and the math shows absolutely no mercy.", "tokens": [51330, 492, 3346, 9218, 432, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 1154, 321, 366, 25704, 2937, 11, 293, 264, 5221, 3110, 3122, 572, 13174, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11167123967950994, "compression_ratio": 1.6028368794326242, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556655135432918e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 236072, "start": 2360.72, "end": 2364.8399999999997, "text": " Wow. Okay, let's pull all of this immense ground we've covered together.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 2235, 439, 295, 341, 22920, 2727, 321, 600, 5343, 1214, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096103833271907, "compression_ratio": 1.6360424028268552, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214475287949393e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 236072, "start": 2365.5, "end": 2375.22, "text": " We started by dismantling the illusion of the present state, realizing that our automatic skills, our computer macros, and our legal rules are actually compressed scars.", "tokens": [50604, 492, 1409, 538, 30506, 1688, 264, 18854, 295, 264, 1974, 1785, 11, 16734, 300, 527, 12509, 3942, 11, 527, 3820, 7912, 2635, 11, 293, 527, 5089, 4474, 366, 767, 30353, 31353, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096103833271907, "compression_ratio": 1.6360424028268552, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214475287949393e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 236072, "start": 2375.8199999999997, "end": 2380.8999999999996, "text": " They are long, messy histories of trial and error folded up for the sake of efficiency.", "tokens": [51120, 814, 366, 938, 11, 16191, 30631, 295, 7308, 293, 6713, 23940, 493, 337, 264, 9717, 295, 10493, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096103833271907, "compression_ratio": 1.6360424028268552, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214475287949393e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 236072, "start": 2381.4599999999996, "end": 2388.3799999999997, "text": " We explored the anti-alignment theorem, proving that the closer we get to perfect efficiency, the further we get from repairability.", "tokens": [51402, 492, 24016, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 11, 27221, 300, 264, 4966, 321, 483, 281, 2176, 10493, 11, 264, 3052, 321, 483, 490, 10535, 2310, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096103833271907, "compression_ratio": 1.6360424028268552, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214475287949393e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 238838, "start": 2388.38, "end": 2397.44, "text": " We risk becoming brittle experts, blindingly fast in normal conditions, but entirely doomed when the environment shifts because we discarded our diagnostic history.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 3148, 5617, 49325, 8572, 11, 6865, 12163, 2370, 294, 2710, 4487, 11, 457, 7696, 33847, 562, 264, 2823, 19201, 570, 321, 45469, 527, 27897, 2503, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07317932261977085, "compression_ratio": 1.6412213740458015, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339850459628495e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 238838, "start": 2397.7400000000002, "end": 2404.04, "text": " We completely redefine boredom, not as lack of shiny objects, but as the cessation of learning and compression.", "tokens": [50833, 492, 2584, 38818, 533, 13521, 298, 11, 406, 382, 5011, 295, 16997, 6565, 11, 457, 382, 264, 47052, 399, 295, 2539, 293, 19355, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07317932261977085, "compression_ratio": 1.6412213740458015, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339850459628495e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 238838, "start": 2404.46, "end": 2412.0, "text": " And we realize that curing it requires the uncomfortable discipline of voluntary handicapping and, most importantly, the protection of unstructured time.", "tokens": [51169, 400, 321, 4325, 300, 1262, 278, 309, 7029, 264, 10532, 13635, 295, 28563, 31369, 10534, 293, 11, 881, 8906, 11, 264, 6334, 295, 18799, 46847, 565, 13, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07317932261977085, "compression_ratio": 1.6412213740458015, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339850459628495e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 241200, "start": 2412.0, "end": 2420.52, "text": " We navigated the ecology of constraints, discovering how redundant rules can masquerade as healthy diversity while actually paralyzing a system from the inside out.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 7407, 770, 264, 39683, 295, 18491, 11, 24773, 577, 40997, 4474, 393, 2300, 8035, 762, 382, 4627, 8811, 1339, 767, 32645, 8781, 257, 1185, 490, 264, 1854, 484, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06724825927189418, "compression_ratio": 1.544, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451541493995197e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 241200, "start": 2421.0, "end": 2425.8, "text": " And finally, we mapped out the finite, unforgiving window of, I'll fix it later.", "tokens": [50815, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 33318, 484, 264, 19362, 11, 31411, 15441, 4910, 295, 11, 286, 603, 3191, 309, 1780, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06724825927189418, "compression_ratio": 1.544, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451541493995197e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 241200, "start": 2426.4, "end": 2434.14, "text": " Realizing that our intuition about when to defer maintenance is dangerously flawed, especially in massive systems that look too big to fail.", "tokens": [51085, 8467, 3319, 300, 527, 24002, 466, 562, 281, 25704, 11258, 307, 4330, 5098, 38823, 11, 2318, 294, 5994, 3652, 300, 574, 886, 955, 281, 3061, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06724825927189418, "compression_ratio": 1.544, "no_speech_prob": 2.2451541493995197e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 243414, "start": 2434.14, "end": 2438.98, "text": " It is a profound reframing of how we interact with complexity at every single level.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 1895, 2356, 278, 295, 577, 321, 4648, 365, 14024, 412, 633, 2167, 1496, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903601426344651, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 2.020637346680787e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 243414, "start": 2439.7, "end": 2448.2599999999998, "text": " But as we wrap up, if we connect this to the bigger picture, there is one final implication that emerges when you lay all five of these essays on top of each other.", "tokens": [50643, 583, 382, 321, 7019, 493, 11, 498, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 11, 456, 307, 472, 2572, 37814, 300, 38965, 562, 291, 2360, 439, 1732, 295, 613, 35123, 322, 1192, 295, 1184, 661, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903601426344651, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 2.020637346680787e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 243414, "start": 2448.72, "end": 2454.24, "text": " An implication Fliction's math points directly toward, but that we haven't explicitly named yet.", "tokens": [51094, 1107, 37814, 3235, 4105, 311, 5221, 2793, 3838, 7361, 11, 457, 300, 321, 2378, 380, 20803, 4926, 1939, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903601426344651, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 2.020637346680787e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 243414, "start": 2454.46, "end": 2455.8799999999997, "text": " What happens when we scale this up?", "tokens": [51381, 708, 2314, 562, 321, 4373, 341, 493, 30, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903601426344651, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 2.020637346680787e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 245588, "start": 2455.88, "end": 2459.4, "text": " Consider the current trajectory of our global technological infrastructure.", "tokens": [50365, 17416, 264, 2190, 21512, 295, 527, 4338, 18439, 6896, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16624743439430414, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 3.129168582235997e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 245588, "start": 2460.1800000000003, "end": 2463.6, "text": " Look at the rise of massive, opaque artificial intelligence models.", "tokens": [50580, 2053, 412, 264, 6272, 295, 5994, 11, 42687, 11677, 7599, 5245, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16624743439430414, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 3.129168582235997e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 245588, "start": 2464.12, "end": 2467.56, "text": " Look at the hyper-optimization of just-in-time global supply chains.", "tokens": [50777, 2053, 412, 264, 9848, 12, 5747, 332, 2144, 295, 445, 12, 259, 12, 3766, 4338, 5847, 12626, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16624743439430414, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 3.129168582235997e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 245588, "start": 2468.1400000000003, "end": 2474.1800000000003, "text": " If this entire corpus of work is correct, our whole civilization is currently relentlessly optimizing for inactability.", "tokens": [50978, 759, 341, 2302, 1181, 31624, 295, 589, 307, 3006, 11, 527, 1379, 18036, 307, 4362, 34045, 12048, 40425, 337, 294, 578, 2310, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16624743439430414, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 3.129168582235997e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 245588, "start": 2474.56, "end": 2476.88, "text": " We are becoming a planetary-scale, brittle expert.", "tokens": [51299, 492, 366, 5617, 257, 35788, 12, 20033, 11, 49325, 5844, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16624743439430414, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 3.129168582235997e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 247688, "start": 2476.88, "end": 2485.6, "text": " We are compressing all historical knowledge, all intermediate human reasoning, and all local buffers into highly efficient black box systems.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 14778, 278, 439, 8584, 3601, 11, 439, 19376, 1952, 21577, 11, 293, 439, 2654, 9204, 433, 666, 5405, 7148, 2211, 2424, 3652, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12642613086071644, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111051937677591e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 247688, "start": 2485.98, "end": 2491.54, "text": " We are discarding the raw, unstructured history to maximize execution speed and minimize overhead.", "tokens": [50820, 492, 366, 31597, 278, 264, 8936, 11, 18799, 46847, 2503, 281, 19874, 15058, 3073, 293, 17522, 19922, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12642613086071644, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111051937677591e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 247688, "start": 2491.96, "end": 2495.82, "text": " We are driving towards the absolute minimal trace on a global scale.", "tokens": [51119, 492, 366, 4840, 3030, 264, 8236, 13206, 13508, 322, 257, 4338, 4373, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12642613086071644, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111051937677591e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 247688, "start": 2496.08, "end": 2498.38, "text": " And if the anti-alignment theorem holds true?", "tokens": [51325, 400, 498, 264, 6061, 12, 304, 41134, 20904, 9190, 2074, 30, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12642613086071644, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111051937677591e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 247688, "start": 2498.84, "end": 2502.42, "text": " It means we are systematically maximizing our global repair blindness.", "tokens": [51463, 467, 1355, 321, 366, 39531, 5138, 3319, 527, 4338, 10535, 46101, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12642613086071644, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111051937677591e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 250242, "start": 2502.42, "end": 2511.44, "text": " If we hit a massive distribution shift, a novel climate event, a cascading digital failure across networks, a geopolitical fracturing,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 2045, 257, 5994, 7316, 5513, 11, 257, 7613, 5659, 2280, 11, 257, 3058, 66, 8166, 4562, 7763, 2108, 9590, 11, 257, 46615, 804, 17948, 1345, 11, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09385396185375396, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582733871981173e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 250242, "start": 2511.76, "end": 2518.14, "text": " we might find that because we prioritize perfect efficiency, we have retained absolutely no trace of how to fix the modern world.", "tokens": [50832, 321, 1062, 915, 300, 570, 321, 25164, 2176, 10493, 11, 321, 362, 33438, 3122, 572, 13508, 295, 577, 281, 3191, 264, 4363, 1002, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09385396185375396, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582733871981173e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 250242, "start": 2518.48, "end": 2525.7200000000003, "text": " We will possess the automated skill to enact civilization, but we will have entirely lost the structural representation required to repair it.", "tokens": [51168, 492, 486, 17490, 264, 18473, 5389, 281, 25909, 18036, 11, 457, 321, 486, 362, 7696, 2731, 264, 15067, 10290, 4739, 281, 10535, 309, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09385396185375396, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582733871981173e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 252572, "start": 2525.72, "end": 2532.16, "text": " We are building the ultimate automated macro for society, but we are throwing away the instructions on how it was originally coded.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 2390, 264, 9705, 18473, 18887, 337, 4086, 11, 457, 321, 366, 10238, 1314, 264, 9415, 322, 577, 309, 390, 7993, 34874, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 252572, "start": 2532.7599999999998, "end": 2533.6, "text": " That is haunting.", "tokens": [50717, 663, 307, 44512, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 252572, "start": 2534.0, "end": 2537.24, "text": " And it is exactly the kind of perspective-shifting insight we look for.", "tokens": [50779, 400, 309, 307, 2293, 264, 733, 295, 4585, 12, 2716, 10106, 11269, 321, 574, 337, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 252572, "start": 2537.64, "end": 2540.8799999999997, "text": " Thank you for joining us today for being the crucial third voice as we unpacked all this.", "tokens": [50961, 1044, 291, 337, 5549, 505, 965, 337, 885, 264, 11462, 2636, 3177, 382, 321, 26699, 292, 439, 341, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 252572, "start": 2541.06, "end": 2542.2, "text": " Do yourself a favor today.", "tokens": [51132, 1144, 1803, 257, 2294, 965, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 252572, "start": 2542.3599999999997, "end": 2544.8399999999997, "text": " Find a moment of completely unstructured time.", "tokens": [51197, 11809, 257, 1623, 295, 2584, 18799, 46847, 565, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 252572, "start": 2545.2599999999998, "end": 2545.72, "text": " Sit with it.", "tokens": [51342, 14523, 365, 309, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 252572, "start": 2546.02, "end": 2546.98, "text": " Build some raw history.", "tokens": [51380, 11875, 512, 8936, 2503, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 252572, "start": 2547.4199999999996, "end": 2550.12, "text": " Don't let an algorithm compress your experience for you.", "tokens": [51450, 1468, 380, 718, 364, 9284, 14778, 428, 1752, 337, 291, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 252572, "start": 2550.2999999999997, "end": 2551.4199999999996, "text": " Just let it be messy.", "tokens": [51594, 1449, 718, 309, 312, 16191, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 252572, "start": 2551.68, "end": 2553.62, "text": " We will see you on the next Deep Dive.", "tokens": [51663, 492, 486, 536, 291, 322, 264, 958, 14895, 413, 488, 13, 51760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11969591044693542, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.973619618428346e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 255362, "start": 2553.62, "end": 2583.6, "text": " We will see you on the next Deep Dive.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 486, 536, 291, 322, 264, 958, 14895, 413, 488, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.6320054871695382, "compression_ratio": 0.8260869565217391, "no_speech_prob": 1.3002971963049781e-11}], "language": "en"}
